{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals","id":1346010,"title":"5 YEARS with no Abyssals, Liminals or Sidereals.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-04T19:47:29-08:00","id":1346010,"title":"5 YEARS with no Abyssals, Liminals or Sidereals.","content":"Half a decade has passed since 3E became a thing and we've just got Dragon-Bloods, with Lunars crawling in development. <br /> I cannot imagine running a game long-term as Storyteller and not having need of an Abyssal and Sidereal books. <br /> <br /> What are Abyssal Mains doing in the meantime? Staying in 2.5? Switching to Solar/DB in the meantime? Giving up and moving on to other games?<br /> <br /> I've sort of switched to DB, but lost my group so I guess I'm mostly in the &quot;giving up and moving on to other games&quot; category.<br /> What about you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:03:20-08:00","id":1346017,"title":"","content":"The people I know with a favourite non-released splat have been pretty well enjoying the ones that we have. Solars and DBs are fresh and different enough from how they were in 2e that they feel cool, I haven't seen any Lunars yet but I'm sure I will. We've moved onto 5e DnD for the past long while, but it has nothing to do with Sidereals not being out and everything to do with DnD just being rock solid. We'll be going back to exalted kinda soon I hope, with some lessons learned.<br /> <br /> I've been spending the last few months compiling ideas and plot notes for my Dynastic game. I'm hoping to introduce my players to a lot of the concepts like how the different ministries and military branches work so that they've got all the tools they need in the second half to start manipulating things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:03:26-08:00","id":1346018,"title":"","content":"I converted Alchemicals. I can die happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:11:09-08:00","id":1346021,"title":"","content":"On a mercantile level, I understand that fresh content is needed to keep an audience, and an audience kept for a profitable game line. I wish the development team haste and a lack of obstacles producing more of the Exalted we all love.<br /> <br /> But on a more personal level, one gets out what one puts in. First and second edition are a font of ideas that can be translated into 3e. And many forumites have posted their homebrew here on the site! For the Abyssal impatient to bring darkness or light to Creation, or the Alchemical Champion to cross the seal of eight divinities, a little google-fu will get a charmset to your monitor. <br /> <br /> I've homebrewed up a Sidereal Charmset / Resplendent Destiny mechanics / Sutra / etc. for my table (probably completely unbalanced!) so that my players can enjoy a Vizier in the group. Same for Alchemicals. And though they are not professionally done, and I will buy and be delighted by the (vastly more) thought put into their official release, the splats are accessible if you reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:16:14-08:00","id":1346022,"title":"","content":"Abyssals at least can be built as Solars with too much eyeshadow and sorta-kinda work. I've been chronically unable to use a Sid in my game despite there being a few situations where it would be perfect to include one. <br /> <br /> EX3 is in a really terrible place where there's basically zero GMing advice, a very limited set of premade foes, and zero advice on custom creation of new content. Anyone who wants to GM an Exalted game is plunging blindly forward while making mountains of homebrew and praying that it works well enough to entertain their players. <br /> Charm(set) creation guidelines shouldn't have been in Exigents. They needed to be in core. Storyteller advice shouldn't have been a not-even-yet-on-the-horizon book. It needed to be in core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T20:20:48-08:00","id":1346024,"title":"","content":"Are there any fanmade Storyteller guides out there? If not maybe somebody should start one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T21:00:55-08:00","id":1346033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346022#post1346022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... a very limited set of premade foes...</div> </div> </div> </div>For premade foes, perhaps check out adversaries of the righteous.<br /> <br /> Regarding adding things to Core, spare the poor book's binding! Especially the print on demand version!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:22:17-08:00","id":1346059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals#post1346010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot imagine running a game long-term as Storyteller and not having need of an Abyssal and Sidereal books.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Is it just me or has every Sidereal we've run into completely only ever used Martial Arts? Like yeah they're good at it, but it's a bit odd that none of them use ANY of their Native Charms.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:32:42-08:00","id":1346062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346059#post1346059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Is it just me or has every Sidereal we've run into completely only ever used Martial Arts? Like yeah they're good at it, but it's a bit odd that none of them use ANY of their Native Charms.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I've just been using 1e Sidereals as inspiration. It's worked fairly well so far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:01:20-08:00","id":1346070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346024#post1346024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any fanmade Storyteller guides out there? If not maybe somebody should start one.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an entire fan made series on youtube by one of our forum goers. Also a book to go with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4390,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","user":"Deamonlight","date":".  added qoute. 11-05-2019, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:07:07-08:00","id":1346072,"title":"","content":"So speaking from experience, Exalted 1e didn't have any Charm creation advice, the storytelling chapter was like a dozen pages (incluidng advancement rules that are actually in the core), and about half as many to a quarter the sample enemies per type. Yet, it was still WW's most successful RPG since Vampire at the time, and had a pretty healthy and lively homebrew community before Dragon-Blooded came out.<br /> <br /> I guess to me, Exalted 3e isn't as intimidating, but I think Exalted 2e got folks in a veiw that 1) Everything would be statted and provided for them and 2) That there'd be advice (that no one raed, as the joke about Chapter 7 went) and 3) The pace was pretty breakneck, so you would get everything soon.<br /> <br /> A big thing to note is 2e had very little actually new content also. It mostly was just taking 1e and retaking it in the 2e system a lot of the time, or expanding what was already stated, so there was a bit more &quot;backporting&quot; you could do. 3e has a lot cleaner &quot;This is a reboot&quot; going on, which I think make sit harder to just loot previous editions. WHich mind, I'm fine with. We already have those.<br /> <br /> But for most groups and my group at least, we just play with what we got. Though I also admit I don't find folks &quot;main&quot; an Exalted type much, so might be my own annecdotal experience being different in these things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:20:32-08:00","id":1346077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346062#post1346062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh, I've just been using 1e Sidereals as inspiration. It's worked fairly well so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that's just you filling in the blanks with homebrew and essentially saying &quot;<a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2016/5/5/11592622/this-is-fine-meme-comic\" target=\"_blank\">This Is Fine</a>&quot;. <br /> It's not a real solution, it's a temporary bandaid - worse, it's the kind of bandaid that works in one group but fails another and changes from Storyteller to Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:36:50-08:00","id":1346079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346077#post1346077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's just you filling in the blanks with homebrew and essentially saying &quot;This Is Fine&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I rent an apartment, there will be things I <i>want</i> to have, that will not be there. I don't rent an apartment expecting there to be a couch and bed ready for me; <i>I bring my mattresses when I move in</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:42:04-08:00","id":1346080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346072#post1346072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess to me, Exalted 3e isn't as intimidating, but I think Exalted 2e got folks in a veiw that 1) Everything would be statted and provided for them and 2) That there'd be advice (that no one raed, as the joke about Chapter 7 went) and 3) The pace was pretty breakneck, so you would get everything soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) But there are certain stats and rules that <b><i>you need</i></b> in order to run the game. Character Creation rules, for instance. Charm trees, for instance. Base mechanics like how things like Sidereal Astrology and Resonance would work in 3E, if they'd still be things, for instance. <br /> This is one of the things I don't get about this argument, which I've heard before - &quot;people are spoiled brats because they expect the developers to supply them with RULES! Pfeh! Back in my day we made our own rules!&quot;. <br /> <br /> So why do I need Exalted, then?<br /> I can just make my own game - system and all - and make up all the things I'm lacking here. <br /> <br /> 2) I read it. It does sadden me that not many do, but I did read it. And I bet newbie Storytellers would have loved to have some tips. The Storyteller chapter isn't a thing that's crucial to me, personally, though and it's not my main concern here.<br /> <br /> 3) The breakneck pace you mention was roughly 2 years. Within 2 years we've had various splat books for 1E and 2E. Second edition Infernals and Alchemicals came in at about 3 years (so 1 year after the others) if I recall correctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346072#post1346072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big thing to note is 2e had very little actually new content also. It mostly was just taking 1e and retaking it in the 2e system a lot of the time, or expanding what was already stated, so there was a bit more &quot;backporting&quot; you could do. 3e has a lot cleaner &quot;This is a reboot&quot; going on, which I think make sit harder to just loot previous editions. WHich mind, I'm fine with. We already have those.<br /> <br /> But for most groups and my group at least, we just play with what we got. Though I also admit I don't find folks &quot;main&quot; an Exalted type much, so might be my own annecdotal experience being different in these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can criticise the copypasta and rushed nature of the books and you're not wrong to do so, but at the same time those editions had every splat available within 3 years tops. Our current edition took <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>4 years</b></span> to give us Dragon-Bloods. <br /> <br /> We are now at <b>5 years</b> since core book release and we have two base splats and just one more on the way. <br /> <br /> It has now been <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">5 years</span> </b></span>and we are lacking some essential stuff. <br /> <br /> <b>F<span style=\"font-size:24px\">IV</span>E YE<span style=\"font-size:24px\">E</span><span style=\"font-size:28px\">EAA<span style=\"font-size:36px\">AR</span>RRS</span><span style=\"font-size:24px\">S</span>S ! ! !</b><br /> <br /> ...At what point do I stop being thought of as being overly needy unimaginative/uncreative brat versus someone with a legitimate complaint? At what point do the defensive arguments of &quot;quality takes time!&quot; and &quot;tHiS iS fInE&quot; stop working? By what year can we expect people to figure out that &quot;Star Citizen&quot; is a lie? <br /> <br /> ............That last question may not be related to the rest of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346079#post1346079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I rent an apartment, there will be things I <i>want</i> to have, that will not be there. I don't rent an apartment expecting there to be a couch and bed ready for me; <i>I bring my mattresses when I move in</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you didn't rent an apartment, you bought a game where Abyssals and Sidereals are essential cast members for long-term Series and you have not been supplied with any way to run long-term Abyssal and Sidereal cast members for... Let me check here... Oh yes...<br /> <br /> <b>F<span style=\"font-size:24px\">IV</span>E YE<span style=\"font-size:24px\">E</span><span style=\"font-size:28px\">EAA<span style=\"font-size:36px\">AR</span>RRS</span><span style=\"font-size:24px\">S</span>S ! ! !</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:48:22-08:00","id":1346084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346080#post1346080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you didn't rent an apartment, you bought a game...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, this is called an &quot;analogy.&quot; I'm describing one thing to explain my thought process about a different thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd in this case, Abyssals and Sidereals are akin to a bed and mattress, in that they're obviously something you're going to <i>want</i> in your apartment, but are not included by default.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Except, in this case, we got samples of both in the Antagonists chapter, so it's like your landlord saw you <i>not</i> bringing a mattress on move-in day, and, out of the goodness of his heart, provided you with a cheap one, because it's better than nothing.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:56:27-08:00","id":1346085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346084#post1346084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd in this case, Abyssals and Sidereals are akin to a bed and mattress, in that they're obviously something you're going to <i>want</i> in your apartment, but are not included by default.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Except, in this case, we got samples of both in the Antagonists chapter, so it's like your landlord saw you <i>not</i> bringing a mattress on move-in day, and, out of the goodness of his heart, provided you with a cheap one, because it's better than nothing.)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2016/5/5/11592622/this-is-fine-meme-comic\" target=\"_blank\">This Is Fine.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:03:55-08:00","id":1346088,"title":"","content":"The main thing here is that I vastly prefer the quality of the books we have gotten to the rush &quot;we have to print X words per month&quot; of Second Edition.<br /> And don't get me wrong, I can't <i>wait</i> for Sidereals, not to mention the Infernals that you haven't even mentioned and that might still take 5+ years to get to.<br /> But I honestly think that the Second Edition &quot;2.5&quot; errata tells me all I need to know about what happens if you try to rush these products out. <br /> We've just gotten the best Lunars in 3 Editions. I'm willing to wait a little longer if that means Sidereals get a similar treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:25:27-08:00","id":1346091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346085#post1346085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Is Fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The house is not on fire, though. You just didn't bring the bed from your old place, and are upset that the landlord didn't give you a king-size mattress.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:42:19-08:00","id":1346092,"title":"","content":"Alucard, are you kidding me? <br /> <br /> Look at what happens to a would-be first time GM. <br /> <br /> If they want to do anything but mortals and Solars, they've got half a dozen premades before they enter the dark marshes of homebrew. They know damn near nothing about any of these other exalts unless they pay for a book that has zero relevant mechanics. Even if they shell out that money, getting useful Charms requires they fully understand the difference between 2e and 3e design. Any GM not willing to <i>extensively</i> homebrew is going to have problems. (DBs finally coming out made this a <i>lot</i> better though)<br /> They have no guidelines or advice on how to make spirits, fae, animals, or even interesting and competitive statblocks. Nada. Zip. Zilch. And, I might add, there's nothing in the core book that can handle a half-decent Dawn let alone an optimized one. The GM who wants to hand his combat-focused player something fun to fight has to make it himself. Any GM who doesn't have a deep understanding of the mechanics and balance is going to have problems. And maybe quit, or just have a game where the Dawn never feels threatened. <br /> They have a party of three to five golden supermen who, thanks to Supernal, are going to be absurdly effective at their chosen specialties. Solars start at levels of power that would be game-breaking in other games. And the poor GM has no advice whatsoever on how to make things work. Not a goddamn word. So unless this new guy has a good grasp of Exalted's radically different play model, the game is going to fall apart. <br /> It's even worse if there's a crafter in the party, since then the GM has to be ready to make artifacts and their charms and attunement bonuses from scratch. Or a summoner dissatisfied with their handful of E1 options. Or an anyone who wants a Retainer or Ally that's neither mortal nor Solar. <br /> <br /> Right now, damn near any GM stepping in blind is going to be crushed. I held it together until friends moving and players being unable to remember even the names of their charms killed my game. I'm sure somebody who started with EX1 or EX2 could have done better. But I can say <b>for absolute fact</b> that nobody else I know would even consider running a system with this lack of GM support. <br /> <br /> A third of the book is Charms. You're telling me there's no room to cut 10% of that to include two dozen pages of advice? Even 5% of that for a dozen pages of advice? Just a single charm from each Ability to free up half a dozen pages of help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T01:05:38-08:00","id":1346097,"title":"","content":"More seriously if we hadn't had to deal with the glacial pace of Holden and Morke in the early years of the Edition we may have actually had Sidereals in progress already. It's undeniable that once Minton and Vance took the reins we've gotten actual progress. Pissing and moaning like a petulant little baby about 'FIIIIVVVVVEEEEE YEEEEEEEAAAAAARRRRRRS' solves precisely nothing and makes you look like a brat.<br /> <br /> Now, there were definitely some poor choices in the corebook. One, it had too many goddamn Charms. Fucking hell, there are too many Charms. I heard someone once say if you took a Craft-Supernal Twilight and made them buy nothing but Craft Charms with their XP, they would hit E5 and still not have bought all the Craft Charms and <i>I believe them</i>. There are too many Charms, too many of them are underwhelming, and a lot of them are unclear and imprecise.<br /> <br /> And support for homebrew is pathetic. It gives you a bunch of sample characters, but when it comes to building NEW ones it goes &quot;I'unno, figure it out&quot;. This is also pretty poor for Evocation write-ups.<br /> <br /> Scion 2e actually does far better than this, as its books give you archetypes for base stats, and a bunch of various Qualities and Powers you can weld onto them to customize what kind of nasty critter you want your PCs to encounter. It gives you a <i>toolbox</i>, in addition to a medley of pre-made antagonists.<br /> <br /> Now, in spite of all this, I'm not gonna start pissing and moaning for all the content to come out NOOOOOOOW because I was in Exalted for the 2e days and I remember when they were spitting out splatbooks super fast. Problem was there was no quality oversight. And I'd rather have a book that had <i>quality</i> writing in it, rather than a shit book sooner.<br /> <br /> (Though Holden and Morke still aren't off the hook for how abysmal their pace was for getting products out after the Kickstarter. Fucking hell, YEARS to get us the Backer Charms and didn't even get us Arms of the Chosen before they got the boot?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T01:11:57-08:00","id":1346099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346088#post1346088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main thing here is that I vastly prefer the quality of the books we have gotten to the rush &quot;we have to print X words per month&quot; of Second Edition.<br /> And don't get me wrong, I can't <i>wait</i> for Sidereals, not to mention the Infernals that you haven't even mentioned and that might still take 5+ years to get to.<br /> But I honestly think that the Second Edition &quot;2.5&quot; errata tells me all I need to know about what happens if you try to rush these products out.<br /> We've just gotten the best Lunars in 3 Editions. I'm willing to wait a little longer if that means Sidereals get a similar treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;let's not rush perfection&quot; argument doesn't work after it took 5 years just to get Dragon-Bloods and maybe Lunars (the latter of which aren't out yet as of the time of this post). <br /> <br /> Infernals can be said to be &quot;non-essential&quot;. Obviously, we want 3E Infernals, but the Core splats are Solars, DB, Abyssal and Sidereal, with Lunars possibly essential as well. Those are the ones that absolutely must be developed and released within a reasonable span of time. <br /> <br /> You cannot have an edition of Exalted go past half a decade without those splats being available. <br /> <br /> Sidereals aren't even on the horizon. We have no time table for Sidereals. We have no time table for Abyssals. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346091#post1346091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The house is not on fire, though. You just didn't bring the bed from your old place, and are upset that the landlord didn't give you a king-size mattress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homebrewing is not the solution.<br /> <br /> This isn't the same thing as writing up a locale for the group to visit - you're telling me I have to revise 600+ pages of content (Sidereals + Abyssals), including Charm Trees and additional mechanics (Resonance, Sidereal Astrology, Necrotech, Necromancy, Martial Arts, <i>Sidereal </i>Martial Arts, Resplendent Destinies, the Loom of Fate, etc), and that all this is on me?<br /> <br /> I'm not a game developer. It's not on me to write half the system. <br /> <br /> Especially not after <b>5 years</b>.<br /> <br /> I<i>t's on the devs</i>, Alucard. It's on <b>them</b> to do. <br /> I don't know how to do all that - why do you think I buy the books?<br /> <br /> But if this is the direction that we're going, then answer me this: ....Why do I need Onyx Path? <br /> If I can just homebrew this stuff, why don't I just write up an entire game system by myself? Why do I need Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T02:11:56-08:00","id":1346104,"title":"","content":"Is there a point to this thread or did you just want to come in and kvetch? Cause I'm not seeing a point to this, you don't accomplish anything you're not asking anyone to give you information because you think you're missing something, so why does this exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T02:45:12-08:00","id":1346108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346080#post1346080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>F<span style=\"font-size:24px\">IV</span>E YE<span style=\"font-size:24px\">E</span><span style=\"font-size:28px\">EAA<span style=\"font-size:36px\">AR</span>RRS</span><span style=\"font-size:24px\">S</span>S ! ! !</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T03:08:31-08:00","id":1346111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346077#post1346077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But that's just you filling in the blanks with homebrew and essentially saying &quot;<a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2016/5/5/11592622/this-is-fine-meme-comic\" target=\"_blank\">This Is Fine</a>&quot;.<br /> It's not a real solution, it's a temporary bandaid - worse, it's the kind of bandaid that works in one group but fails another and changes from Storyteller to Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally the only solution available.<br /> <br /> What other choice do you have that will actually produce results? Discovering the writers' address and whipping them ?<br /> <br /> I'd love to get them to work full time with a couple more staff, but I can't exactly afford it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T03:09:37-08:00","id":1346112,"title":"","content":"Holden and Hatewheel took ages and ages.<br /> So they were fired.<br /> In 2 years, the new Devs have produced 3 books, a whole bunch of short pdfs, and they've almost finished another book (the raw text is available). It's not amazing, and it's not terrible.<br /> <br /> Personally, I found running the game hard at the beginning but it's fine now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T03:44:18-08:00","id":1346115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346108#post1346108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4bcnO3VQ_fc</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ..............You win both the thread and my heart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346111#post1346111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's literally the only solution available.<br /> <br /> What other choice do you have that will actually produce results? Discovering the writers' address and whipping them ?<br /> <br /> I'd love to get them to work full time with a couple more staff, but I can't exactly afford it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoooooooooaaaa... I would have went with &quot;intense staring&quot; and &quot;intentful throat-clearing while emoting towards an older copy of <i>Exalted: Abyssals</i>, then tapping a watch with a finger repeatedly&quot;. Why did you go straight for the whip? <br /> <br /> But in any case, this is mostly venting because I don't have a solution. Just frustration. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346112#post1346112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holden and Hatewheel took ages and ages.<br /> So they were fired.<br /> In 2 years, the new Devs have produced 3 books, a whole bunch of short pdfs, and they've almost finished another book (the raw text is available). It's not amazing, and it's not terrible.<br /> <br /> Personally, I found running the game hard at the beginning but it's fine now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't actually know about the inner workings of the company and the dev change. Reading about it in this and a previous post, I'm certainly more hopeful now and this definitely lifts some of the frustration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T04:06:27-08:00","id":1346118,"title":"","content":"hahahahaha<br /> I understand your frustration, I sure would love to have all major splats on my hands already, but we make do with what we have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T04:31:38-08:00","id":1346124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346077#post1346077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a real solution, it's a temporary bandaid - worse, it's the kind of bandaid that works in one group but fails another and changes from Storyteller to Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Nobody is suggesting it is the only solution.<br /> <br /> It's certainly not an ideal solution.<br /> <br /> But it's an option that some people can partake of.<br /> <br /> Do you not think that Sidereals have lots of iconic powers that convert really easily? Is it very hard to bring over Neighborhood Relocation Scheme? Or even Dodge Fate?<br /> <br /> Astrology should be built differently, but is the familiar form completely untenable <i>for the moment </i>?<br /> <br /> I agree that it sucks that the progress of the game was delayed by two years, and that even picking up the pace is not the fastest (although with the comprehensive nature of the last couple of books featuring Exalted, a bit of time is probably necessary).<br /> <br /> But there are still options that can be employed temporarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:32:36-08:00","id":1346153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346084#post1346084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd in this case, Abyssals and Sidereals are akin to a bed and mattress, in that they're obviously something you're going to <i>want</i> in your apartment, but are not included by default.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Except, in this case, we got samples of both in the Antagonists chapter, so it's like your landlord saw you <i>not</i> bringing a mattress on move-in day, and, out of the goodness of his heart, provided you with a cheap one, because it's better than nothing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except beds and mattresses aren't things you expect to come with the apartment. It's more like renting an apartment, only to find the sink in the kitchen was never installed. Sure, you can live without the kitchen sink since you have everything but (pun intentional), but when you inquire about the eventual future installation of said kitchen sink, you're told waiting over five years isn't that bad. Also, there are people who already installed their own kitchen sinks, so maybe you should do that.<br /> <br /> And the landlord also has a chapter in your lease agreement that shows you examples of installed kitchen sinks, so maybe that's enough. It's better than nothing, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:37:13-08:00","id":1346154,"title":"","content":"No, as there are actually <i>laws </i>against apartments not having sinks. If your landlord leases you an apartment like that, you can take him to court over that shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:47:53-08:00","id":1346155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346115#post1346115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoooooooooaaaa... I would have went with &amp;quot;intense staring&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;intentful throat-clearing while emoting towards an older copy of <i>Exalted: Abyssals</i>, then tapping a watch with a finger repeatedly&amp;quot;. Why did you go straight for the whip?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that the developers are pretty eager to do more work, but it\u2019s hard. I\u2019m fairly certain current developers aren\u2019t full-time writers for Exalted, so they\u2019re not sitting down for 40-50 hours a week working solidly and just not producing for the game or anything. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also pretty impressed by the quality that they\u2019ve been putting out, and I think the time is worth it. We could have Abyssals by New Year if they just went through and took every Solar charm but changed the fluff text to something death-y, but that sucks. I\u2019d rather they took their time to give us something that makes the old Abyssals look dull and boring in comparison to their new awesomeness.<br /> <br /> And hey, it could be way worse. Imagine the poor people* who only plays Exalted for Alchemicals. There are at least Abyssals in the corebook and in the adversary manual, and the alchemicals are likely going to be the very last splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> *person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T07:57:50-08:00","id":1346160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346115#post1346115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't actually know about the inner workings of the company and the dev change. Reading about it in this and a previous post, I'm certainly more hopeful now and this definitely lifts some of the frustration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this makes a bit more sense. Holden and Morke, other than having some personal life events, held the line hostage and completely derailed Ex3's development pipeline with their shenanigans. If I didn't know that they putzed around for 3 of the &quot;5 years&quot;, and left nothing but the approved pitches for their successors to work from I would be a little disgruntled too.<br /> <br /> The work that Eric, Robert, and the writing teams they've assembled, have done in 2 years is amazing given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> edit for additional context to that last line: I'm not a rabid fanboy, but the books that they have put out- Arms of the Chosen, Dragon-Blooded:What Fire has Wrought, The Realm, and (soon to be) Lunars: Fangs At The Gate, are some of the best Exalted books in the history of the line, and I don't think that is a controversial opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":1542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","user":"MoroseMorgan","date":". 11-05-2019, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:17:47-08:00","id":1346164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346155#post1346155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling that the developers are pretty eager to do more work, but it\u2019s hard. I\u2019m fairly certain current developers aren\u2019t full-time writers for Exalted, so they\u2019re not sitting down for 40-50 hours a week working solidly and just not producing for the game or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":24}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:32:15-08:00","id":1346166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346099#post1346099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You cannot have an edition of Exalted go past half a decade without those splats being available.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why Not? Been doing just fine without them so far...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 11-05-2019, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:57:42-08:00","id":1346171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346164#post1346164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still find time to answer the endless fan questions in the Ask the Devs thread. Thanks again for still keeping that up, I\u2019d find it exhausting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:11:21-08:00","id":1346174,"title":"","content":"Lunars is coming up on a year. I'm slightly impatient for the book to be released, but that has a lot of past frustrations built into, so my impatience is probably slightly unreasonable. If I see another Exalted Splat go up on kickstarter in the next few months I say things are probably okay. Without a large team major spats coming out at a rate of about 1 per year is probably reasonable. We've gotten good content from the new dev team, so I'm inclined to let them work so long as content keeps coming. However, we are way behind on books, so I pretty much expect them to always be working on a splatbook until the major spats are all released, and probably keep us informed on the process, so that we know work is really getting done.<br /> <br /> For those that dont follow Exalted closely the pace of things is in fact totally unreasonable and it can be reasonably assumed by those people that Exalted is basically a failed game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:12:17-08:00","id":1346176,"title":"","content":"1) Not to toot my own horn, but this is one of the major reasons I play mortals. I don't need multiple books<br /> <br /> 2) Exalted has always been that weird combo of &quot;you <i>need</i> to homebrew some stuff&quot; and also &quot;and we aren't going to help you very much&quot;. There isn't much I can say about it without coming off as kinda-dismissive, so, uh &quot;get cracking&quot; I guess?<br /> <br /> 3) The development-timeline of 3E has been a clusterfuck rolled up in a shitshow. I suggest you look it up.<br /> <br /> 4) its not <i>impossible</i> to bring stuff over from 2E into 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:21:58-08:00","id":1346182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346085#post1346085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2016/5/5/11592622/this-is-fine-meme-comic\" target=\"_blank\">This Is Fine.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Careful with responses like this. It's not exactly respecting Alucard or the conversation.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:31:14-08:00","id":1346184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346164#post1346164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOW.<br /> <br /> All I can say is mad props.<br /> <br /> This certainly puts the ask a dev thread in a new light. Now I kinda feel like an ass for asking questions so often when you're already stretched thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:31:51-08:00","id":1346203,"title":"","content":"Kind of for context, Onyx Path in general isn't very fast. <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> for Mage: the Awakening 2e was written alongside the 2e corebook and didn't come out until 2019. Scion 2e and Trinity Continuum were announced alongside Exalted an originally slated to KS that year. We didn't get them until later. And while there were issues with the previous devs holding things up, the manuscript was in layout and art direction for about a year.<br /> <br /> A big thing to remember is that unless you're WotC, it's kind of hard to actually do RPGs at any decent scale or pace. Especially when most everything you od or work with is freelancers who have, as noted, more often than not other jobs. A lot of bottlenecks can happen and things can change as things go along.<br /> <br /> It looks like things are on pace. A big help is some of the things learned from previous Kickstarters, like not putting all the extra material in the book but having a companion, and also having a manuscript done before you go to KS, were amongst htem. But I think i'ts worth noting that the whole &quot;Half a decade withotu Abyssals&quot; is being said in a very different decade for RPGs than the early 00s, and different expectations of quality to get there.<br /> <br /> As noted, the devs have a lotta books they wanna do. It's just that two hardcovers and six supplements or more a year is something they can't do and promise the quality we've been getting. Until RPG freelancers are a job worth doing over other shit, it's what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:45:49-08:00","id":1346204,"title":"","content":"The QUALITY of product that Onyx Path puts out, however, is pretty exceptional, even if it takes a bit longer than some would like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:25:48-08:00","id":1346227,"title":"","content":"I think the pace is reasonable now but agree that the lack of ST advice is bad. It's not just what was/wasn't in the books but how the previous developers interacted with the community and how that engagement disappeared after the book came out.<br /> <br /> For a point of comparison Manual of Exalted Power: Infernals was a fucking trainwreck. Without a lot of context originally provided by Neph and Holden for what Green Sun Princes were supposed to be it couldn't have possibly been a successful product. However once that context was provided chapter 1 and 2 became heterodoxical to the point of gaslighting and Infernals became a darling of 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately by the time Ex3 came out Morke and Holden were 100% done with this shit, even if they didn't know it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-05-2019, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:43:26-08:00","id":1346232,"title":"","content":"Frankly to me, Holden and Hatewheel were so horrific and terrible in their dismissivness of the people who wanted to play the game, what other people might enjoy, and their frankly insane attempt to burn down the game (and the rest of Onyx Path) as soon as someone called them out for taking over 3 years to deliver a book and fired them that I'm amazed the line is continuing, much less that we've gotten developers who work full time, 40 hour weeks, constantly answer rules questions for a ruleset they didn't write but have had thrown into their lap full of corner cases and edges where you have to go 'how is this supposed to work' to them, and are still producing books as fast as they can.<br /> <br /> In the same time that it took Holden and Hatewheel to produce 1 Exalted book, they've produced 4, because they had to rewrite a lot of Arms too because Hatewheel and Holden refused to allow their material of it to be published. This isn't even counting the Hundred Devils Night Parade and the Adversaries of the Righteous, which contain both regular animals and massive amounts of demons, spirits, and Exalted, including, since you're repeatedly bringing up Abyssals, the most recent one, which included an Abyssal who is also a Necromancer, which includes a handful of Necromancy spells- including a new, better version of Summon Ghost that finally puts it on par with Demon Summoning- and a Necromantic Initiation.<br /> <br /> When you say 'it's been FIVE YEARS', to me, no, it hasn't. It's been 2 and a half-ish, since developers that weren't a par of infants with inflated egos and god-complexes were put in charge, and I see multiple brand new books presented all containing actual new, non-copy/pasted material.<br /> <br /> The fact from a previous post you had no idea Holden and Hatewheel had even been fired says a lot about how you probably weren't aware of the circumstances going on, and, just as a thought, maybe instead of an aggressive topic complaining about this stuff to demand information, you should have just posted 'hey, what's the status of Exalted right now'.<br /> <br /> It's not like we don't get those every month or two with vaguely snide implications that the gameline is dying from random people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:52:49-08:00","id":1346235,"title":"","content":"If they convince Neph to come back to exalted and we would see an uptick in content. That man could write once he got into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:53:33-08:00","id":1346236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=T8YCSJpF4g4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=T8YCSJpF4g4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=T8YCSJpF4g4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=T8YCSJpF4g4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But seriously:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://memecrunch.com/meme/7WF7O/10-years-later/image.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://memecrunch.com/meme/7WF7O/10-...ater/image.jpg</a><br /> <br /> But seriously:<br /> <br /> Eric and Vance are pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:11:49-08:00","id":1346238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346235#post1346235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they convince Neph to come back to exalted and we would see an uptick in content. That man could write once he got into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't he responsible for some of the worst parts of Infernals like &quot;Yozis are robots made out of Charms&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:27:50-08:00","id":1346240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346238#post1346238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't he responsible for some of the worst parts of Infernals like &amp;quot;Yozis are robots made out of Charms&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>His talent is for taking an idea and turning that idea into evocative game mechanics. Yes, he had the idea that Yozis are made of charms, but he did it with the blessing of though who originally wrote the Yozis. If it was good it not is entirely subjective, personally I love it, and a lot of very happy and excited fans loved it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:05:29-08:00","id":1346248,"title":"","content":"Eh, it was kind of an annoying meme at the time but Yozi being &quot;Charm robots&quot; wasn't text and more just something he kind of said that was probably hyperbolic and sounded cool in forum culture (&quot;as was the style at the time&quot;, #AbeSimpson), and probably didn't even stand as a popular meme even for a year or something.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger issue of any idea of Neph coming back to write Exalted, beyond &quot;too many cooks&quot;, is that he just doesn't seem from what I've seen*, on balance, that into a bunch of Exalted's main genres (contra at least John Morke, for whatever else, and the current writers who quite visibly were and are) and quite fairly enough his tastes often seem to run more to supers, sci-fi and horror (and he came into Exalted as a writer from other White Wolf horror themed properties as I recall). And he seems to have a busy enough life as is. So I'm not sure he would be up for a load of hard work that eats up his free time (as the labour of love for current devs as it seems) that could be spent on life stuff and passion projects and which isn't quite what he's most interested in.<br /> <br /> With Infernals for'ex it seems to me he probably wanted to write sort of Yozi inspired cosmic-horror superheroes with a metal aesthetic and become-as-the-Elder-Gods thing.... who in retrospect, quite as written, IMO probably didn't fit so well the power-scale and genre of where Exalted should be (which also caused various problems down the road with power-creep bleeding through to the Solars who had to &quot;balance&quot; Infernals). The problems were with the line developer oversight and vision of Ex2 (or lack thereof) that they kind of let him, more than it being his fault. As well as that Infernals may have just had a bad developer outline generally, judging from other chapters, as is discussed up-thread.<br /> <br /> *and I may well very easily be wrong on what he is interested in, of course! Er... this is pretty conjectural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:08:29-08:00","id":1346250,"title":"","content":"My main problem with the books were more the lack of storytellers guidelines, as was already said, than not having Abyssals or Sidereals as ennemies or whatever. I don't even see how they would help since I would never, and I cannot possibly understand anyone doing this, use PC rules (with Charmset and such) to handle NPCs because it's way too complicated to keep track of as a ST. So apart from a world building perspective (which is extremely useful, I love reading The Realm), the new splats wouldn't change much of my options. What I could really appreciate would be an easy-to-use manual to have good NPCs on the fly with little to no work, but guess what : I home-brewed it (like everyone else I guess)<br /> <br /> I totally relate that the game seems very noob-crushing from a game design perspective : I can't imagine discovering RPG with Exalted 3e and having enough experience and wisdom to use it well. Luckily for me I discovered it with few years of experience, and never in my life have I loved an RPG so much, so to anyone involved in this project : Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 11-05-2019, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:13:00-08:00","id":1346252,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's healthy forum environment to post personal attacks against the previous developers. It's okay for people to have opinions and be critical of things, but some of the posts I've seen in this thread look more like directed attacks. That's not necessary.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand, I was brought into the writing team summer last year and have contributed to four books since. I've had a great and friendly experience and it's a delight to work with Robert, Eric, the other developers, and the rest of the writing team. Another person who deserves a lot of credit is Dixie who was thrown headfirst into Exalted last year and have done a tremendous job since both getting familiar with the game and keeping the balls rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:46:08-08:00","id":1346267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346252#post1346252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's healthy forum environment to post personal attacks against the previous developers. It's okay for people to have opinions and be critical of things, but some of the posts I've seen in this thread look more like directed attacks. That's not necessary.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand, I was brought into the writing team summer last year and have contributed to four books since. I've had a great and friendly experience and it's a delight to work with Robert, Eric, the other developers, and the rest of the writing team. Another person who deserves a lot of credit is Dixie who was thrown headfirst into Exalted last year and have done a tremendous job since both getting familiar with the game and keeping the balls rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between a personal attack and a list of things they actually did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T13:54:39-08:00","id":1346271,"title":"","content":"I understand they actually did this but I overall agree with Ekorren : the last few posts did not promote what I'd feel is a &quot;healthy forum environment&quot;.<br /> <br /> But I think it's a complicated thing to promote because there are also some people who may have had a personal implication in what happened and they might need to express their frustration to get over it. But I don't think posting more on this specific matter should be the purpose of this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:08:37-08:00","id":1346278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346250#post1346250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I could really appreciate would be an easy-to-use manual to have good NPCs on the fly with little to no work, but guess what : I home-brewed it (like everyone else I guess)<br /> <br /> Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you have an NPC's on the Fly Homebrew? Where can I see such a project?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:49:09-08:00","id":1346290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346164#post1346164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time you post this, some idiot like me must make a post like this. But here goes anyway:<br /> <br /> What would it take to get you to write Exalted full time?<br /> <br /> Like, if you ran a Kickstarter for $40k, not to fund a deluxe book but so you could quit your day job and write full time for a year, would that cover it? Or could it be built into the stretch goals for a book?<br /> <br /> You and Vance are doing a good job, and the pace of release under your tenure is much improved. If we, the community, could do something supportive instead of make snippy posts about &quot;five years&quot; then I'm sure you'd find broad support.<br /> <br /> This isn't my industry, I don't know how this works. And considering the circumstances, you're doing a great job. But as much as I gripe, I own three copies of the Ex3 Corebook -- I'd totally pay a premium to get Extingents and Infernals faster, why won't you take my money?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346248#post1346248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Infernals for'ex it seems to me he probably wanted to write sort of Yozi inspired cosmic-horror superheroes with a metal aesthetic and become-as-the-Elder-Gods thing....</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I miss Neph!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-05-2019, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:51:04-08:00","id":1346292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346240#post1346240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His talent is for taking an idea and turning that idea into evocative game mechanics. Yes, he had the idea that Yozis are made of charms, but he did it with the blessing of though who originally wrote the Yozis. If it was good it not is entirely subjective, personally I love it, and a lot of very happy and excited fans loved it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Neph a lot and think he is pretty influential with 2e, but I think the design philosophy Exalted 3e started with and continues with is just not really in his framework. He likes a lot of particular kinds of world-building, detail-building, and application of mechanics to-setting that I think just dont' fit with Exalted 3e's goals of being open, leaving things to be decided, and introducing new things instead of trying to tie them all together to some unstated setting thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:55:49-08:00","id":1346294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346250#post1346250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I could really appreciate would be an easy-to-use manual to have good NPCs on the fly with little to no work, but guess what : I home-brewed it (like everyone else I guess)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait I want one.<br /> <br /> I'm about to start running my first Exalted campaign, and I'm honestly not that worried about lack of mechanics for Abyssal and Sidereal (and Dragonblooded and Lunars, since I don't have those books) NPCs. &quot;No concrete rules for how the villain is affecting the setting&quot; is the default for RPGs, so just having things like Sorcerous Workings to use as a guideline is more than I'm used to, and and I don't really want more than two or three Charms per foe. If I have to steal them from Solar charm trees or Evocations and tweak 'em a bit, I don't think anyone is going to notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T16:19:44-08:00","id":1346310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346024#post1346024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any fanmade Storyteller guides out there? If not maybe somebody should start one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made on nearly four years ago...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T16:48:12-08:00","id":1346317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346294#post1346294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait I want one.<br /> <br /> I'm about to start running my first Exalted campaign, and I'm honestly not that worried about lack of mechanics for Abyssal and Sidereal (and Dragonblooded and Lunars, since I don't have those books) NPCs. &quot;No concrete rules for how the villain is affecting the setting&quot; is the default for RPGs, so just having things like Sorcerous Workings to use as a guideline is more than I'm used to, and and I don't really want more than two or three Charms per foe. If I have to steal them from Solar charm trees or Evocations and tweak 'em a bit, I don't think anyone is going to notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll really like Crucible of Legends!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T18:55:28-08:00","id":1346329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346317#post1346317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll really like Crucible of Legends!</div> </div> </div> </div>-_-<br /> <br /> Well. I love your enthusiasm. Crucible is still... at best a year out.<br /> <br /> This thread has just reminded me that I need to get my shit in order and send in all of the applications. I'm currently in a position where I can actually consider going into freelance writing with almost dedicated 20 hours a week. I just hope that my skills are up to the task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T20:19:35-08:00","id":1346340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346164#post1346164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys already gave me the best version of Lunars in the entire history of the Exalted line, so my deepest gratitude for that.<br /> <br /> If you Devs want to Patreon or something to make more words flow, happy to make it happen.<br /> <br /> If the current pace of releases is what works best for you too, also 100% okay.<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve done more than enough for the Exalted line already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:01:31-08:00","id":1346350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346164#post1346164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're freelancers who already work 40+ hours a week at our day jobs; we develop Exalted in our rather limited spare time. I wish we could work faster and more efficiently on Exalted development, but circumstances simply don't allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I didn't know the backstory of the vicissitudes behind the development or your circumstances as a freelancer.<br /> I have a lot more faith now and things make a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> You developed and wrote for <b><i>Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought</i></b>, I know that much, so you wrote the best incarnation of Dragon-Bloods - both narratively and mechanically - of all editions. <br /> <br /> Is there anything that we, the community, can do to help <i>you</i> guys? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346252#post1346252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's healthy forum environment to post personal attacks against the previous developers. It's okay for people to have opinions and be critical of things, but some of the posts I've seen in this thread look more like directed attacks. That's not necessary.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand, I was brought into the writing team summer last year and have contributed to four books since. I've had a great and friendly experience and it's a delight to work with Robert, Eric, the other developers, and the rest of the writing team. Another person who deserves a lot of credit is Dixie who was thrown headfirst into Exalted last year and have done a tremendous job since both getting familiar with the game and keeping the balls rolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Had no idea of any of this.<br /> I know it's not much, but I gave your YT a sub.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:10:55-08:00","id":1346354,"title":"","content":"Jumping back to some points I read to while on the bus.<br /> <br /> All this detail about difficulties running a game? GM's having little idea what the hell to do?<br /> <br /> All of that is completely true. And dismissing it as &quot;Well I'VE never had that problem!&quot; does nothing to the fact that those people have difficulties running it... and the countless thanks I got from my own &quot;How to run Exalted&quot; guide when I barely advertised the damn thing is testament to that. The problem with Crucible of Legends is that it's quite the ways out. For all it's faults, 2e at least had an ST chapter and hell even an ST supplement so you could make other Exalt NPC's *as soon as you bought it* rather than being drip fed NPC's in books and needing to fill in the rest. I understand that there are many reasons for why this game to be and that OPP wants to move forward from correcting this, but at this point the damage has been done.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry to say it, but I will echo the exceeding long development times. Things have been better since we've had new oversight, but even with the hiring wave of people I seriously question what is going on. How long as Across the Eight Directions been in second drafts again? Like serious question. Steps have been taken to improve this it seems, but right now I feel as if those are insufficient. Maybe have some more people on the line? A cleaner reporting/submission structure? I don't know what the pain points are, that is where the main issues in the current process lie, and I also get that the main devs have full time jobs that eat up a lot of their time. But considering that multiple people have left due to the pace which the books come out (with myself being one several times), I'm going to echo that this is a real concern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the quality of the books is amazing! </div> </div> </div>To me the quality is insufficient for the time given. I'd rather sacrifice some quality to see faster releases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T00:20:11-08:00","id":1346392,"title":"","content":"I hesitated to post this as a) I'm mainly a lurker and b) this place should mostly be about sharing positive stories and ideas.<br /> <br /> I've been GMing exalted for about 10 years now, on and off. I've never been good at it but &quot;He who owns the books shall DM&quot; and what not. Since Ex3 I feel like GMing has gotten worse, harder to manage, more numbers to keep track of in my head. While I don't think Ex2 was better (no social system, perfect defenses, etc) it certainly had less to keep track of and less &quot;exceptions to the rule&quot; type charms. That's just my opinion however, I haven't crunched the numbers on charms.<br /> <br /> Nowadays there is just so much work to be done prepping for a session that I've stopped thinking of Exalted as a game to play and more of a job I do. I still try because like most people here I love the setting and the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> Recently my group has been moonlighting with another RPG called Lancer. I bring this up because, much to my great frustration, Lancer has an App called COMP/CON for character creation and GM management. It frustrates me because I can see how the same sort of tool could benefit exalted and take away most of the complexity that I struggle with. The App has only been in development for 8 Months and Lancer isn't even officially out yet but it's already come so far.<br /> <br /> I don't know the story behind the App, I think they were just lucky to have a fan who was a developer and had the free time. However it makes the game easy, let's us play around with our builds, let's us focus on role playing and jokes.<br /> <br /> I guess the reason I bring this up is that I'm afraid the complexity of this game is going to turn off new players or old players who have become time poor. Neither is a good thing for the game line.<br /> <br /> My one hope is that Onyx Path's growing connections with a full on video game studio might evolve into a focus on computer assisted gaming. Maybe that goes against the spirit of TTRPG's but personally I'm all for it if it means I can focus less on math and more on my friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6585-nightshrike","name":"nightshrike","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T05:51:08-08:00","id":1346439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nightshrike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346392#post1346392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the reason I bring this up is that I'm afraid the complexity of this game is going to turn off new players or old players who have become time poor. Neither is a good thing for the game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the Dragon-Blooded and Lunar KSes were both consistent in backers (there was a drop from the core, but there would've been one anyway regardless of what happened with it), and the bare minimum sales for a full Ex3 book on DriveThru is Gold (The Realm), with the rest even higher. So... there's a fair number of people out there continuing to back the KSes and buy the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:34:51-08:00","id":1346445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346439#post1346439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, the Dragon-Blooded and Lunar KSes were both consistent in backers (there was a drop from the core, but there would've been one anyway regardless of what happened with it), and the bare minimum sales for a full Ex3 book on DriveThru is Gold (The Realm), with the rest even higher. So... there's a fair number of people out there continuing to back the KSes and buy the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the argument is that Ex3 is dying. Rather it could definitely reach more people with an app or similar to make it more approachable.<br /> <br /> The complexity of combat and of managing dozens of Charms are hands down the biggest pain points in all the games I've played or ST'ed. Lot-Casting Atemi is a godsend, but something with official support could do even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T06:35:08-08:00","id":1346446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nightshrike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346392#post1346392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think Ex2 was better (no social system, perfect defenses, etc) it certainly had less to keep track of and less &quot;exceptions to the rule&quot; type charms. That's just my opinion however, I haven't crunched the numbers on charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e depends wildly on what your group considered essential or a part of the system.<br /> <br /> For example, it actually had a social system called Social Combat that was much more elabourate than Ex3's Social Influence system. It's just that only Lunars had charms that really interacted with concepts like rolling join debate and social units.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T08:49:20-08:00","id":1346465,"title":"","content":"A note about apps to reduce complexity (because I do agree that Exalted has a lot going on; when running combat I frequently make small mistakes because there's Initiative, Overwhelming penalties, motes going up and down, etc).<br /> <br /> There are a number of player-created macros I have copies of that I use to help, and I've found them very beneficial. I'd give credit to the creators... but I can't remember most of them. (Colin Fredericks?)<br /> <br /> This is a combat spreadsheet one of the forumites made that sorts players/NPCs by turn, keeps track of their overwhelming, etc. I've only used it once, but it worked really well.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SP9T31SAqo_vhTb4zsm6boRqZsnLJLn3H3wyHkGjtRk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SP9T31SAqo_vhTb4zsm6boRqZsnLJLn3H3wyHkGjtRk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SP9T31SAqo_vhTb4zsm6boRqZsnLJLn3H3wyHkGjtRk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SP9T31SAqo_vhTb4zsm6boRqZsnLJLn3H3wyHkGjtRk/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is a battle group generator where you choose the base unit (you can make your own or choose from a list), put in the drill/size/might, and it generates all the stats for you. One thing I find very useful is that when the size goes down, you can just move the size down and it reduces stats appropriately, so you don't have to work it out again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-battle-groups/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is a dice roller that lets you put in doubles, re-rolls, etc.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-dice-roller/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-dice-roller/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-dice-roller/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://colin-fredericks.github.io/ex3-dice-roller/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And last, here's a map that tells you travel times for spells, agatae, etc. It's not 100% perfect, but it's pretty good.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://howsfamily.net/Exalted/map/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-07-2019, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:57:42-08:00","id":1346629,"title":"","content":"I agree that Exalted could benefit from an app or cheat sheets. The fans are an amazing resource but the fact that the fans are really the driving force behind Exalted is kind of a problem. Personally, if I didn't have access to the myriad of resources produced by forum goers and discord users I wouldn't be able to run Exalted or introduce new players. The core book is thick and daunting to look at. A small packet of printouts is far simpler and less scary. I can convince people that Exalted is amazing but one look at the core book has most of them sudding having house fires to put out rather than time to play. An App might solve 99% of the issues. Hell, I'd rebuy the core book released as an app that lets click around and presents everything intuitively. At full price. I click on creation, and it tells me about the general area as written. Areas without detail just talk about the direction or general stuff. Add in a travel time tracker like the one above (Thanks Oz) and you have a tool for the game that interactive.<br /> <br /> Click to characters, and you can read abilities, you can make characters, you can read charms. I'll rebuy the dragon blooded book as an expansion and all the other books too. I don't care I already own them. Add in a dice roller for game play, one that interacts with all the dice tricks that exist. Add in other areas such as the underworld, the wyld, ect. Nothing new needs to be added, no new writing. Just compile what is out now and I'll rebuy it all. Then we can add in more as it is released. I'll probably end up with a book copy while waiting for the app to catch up and buy that twice too. My point is, money for Onyx path and they should either create one or partner up with someone. <br /> <br /> I personally don't need any kind of Storyteller guide as a long time ST of Exalted. I did enjoy reading and watching Sandact6's work. I'm only part way through the Youtube series but it is enjoyable and a good reminder of things. The written guide was great and I recommend reading. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sG52v0QCij7-vI0Y3Mb2s2gusu8dfkzdUOLkmMshw3Q/edit#heading=h.1qez97otd6bp\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.1qez97otd6bp</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T02:26:53-08:00","id":1346687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346278#post1346278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, you have an NPC's on the Fly Homebrew? Where can I see such a project?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just passing to say I didn't forget you. I'll post my home-brew tonight certainly. It's nothing exceptional though just an extended and more guided version of the QC advices given in the Core book, but if it can be of use to anybody I'll gladly share it.<br /> <br /> I'd also be surprised that no one else had shared something like this before so do not hesitate to check or ask other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 11-07-2019, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T03:31:16-08:00","id":1346690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346154#post1346154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, as there are actually <i>laws </i>against apartments not having sinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're going to use hyperbolic analogies, don't counter hyperbolic analogies by treating them as suddenly based on realistic circumstances. Else I'll point out if an apartment is listed as fully furnished and the lease states it is fully furnished, but for whatever reason there is no bed? Then you can also demand a bed be delivered in a timely fashion (which would be less than five years, for what its worth), or you can take the landlord to court. Even if a bed is implied, you stand a chance of winning the case, if your argument is strong and the judge is feeling kind.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> All that said, I get why we're five years in to Ex3 and only have two fatsplats out to date, with a third on the way. I understand the realities of it, and I appreciate that there's little that can reasonably be done to speed things along. No disrespect to the devs intended. Still, I get the frustrations of people waiting for official products to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:00:04-08:00","id":1346703,"title":"","content":"There's got to be a way to speed it up. Hire the Devs as at least part time employees (rather than freelancers), get a team 2 to work on alternating books?<br /> <br /> I remember that the Layout was a huge bottleneck with the original book. Maybe hire another person to do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:01:18-08:00","id":1346725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346703#post1346703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's got to be a way to speed it up. Hire the Devs as at least part time employees (rather than freelancers), get a team 2 to work on alternating books?<br /> <br /> I remember that the Layout was a huge bottleneck with the original book. Maybe hire another person to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt that all of those things would speed up production massively, but that none of those things are profitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T08:25:16-08:00","id":1346731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346725#post1346725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no doubt that all of those things would speed up production massively, but that none of those things are profitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also if they want to do it on their end themselves.<br /> <br /> Now I can't speak for them, but Vance really wants to break into the lawyer world. Which requires a lot of hours. If personally he wants to be a lawyer more than wanting to pursue his writing side gig, then you really can't fault him for that.<br /> <br /> I mean if I asked to do the same thing, to give up my own career with steady employment and excellent benefits for the shaky as hell payment schedules of freelancing work, I'd laugh and say no. I like the line, but there's no way in hell I'm killing my golden goose after I spent so long trying to get the damn thing.<br /> <br /> Also layout was a problem with the original book. No idea what the hell is causing it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T09:31:27-08:00","id":1346747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346703#post1346703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's got to be a way to speed it up. Hire the Devs as at least part time employees (rather than freelancers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that's going to increase the free time afforded by their full time jobs?<br /> <br /> People remember that Robert Vance is a lawyer, don't they?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">get a team 2 to work on alternating books?<br /> <br /> I remember that the Layout was a huge bottleneck with the original book. Maybe hire another person to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will these people also be paid enough to live on, or need additional jobs themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:18:50-08:00","id":1346787,"title":"","content":"So, hypothetically Onyx Path doubles the size of the Exalted team so that next year there's two kickstarters. It's not going to stop someone doing another thread like this when they're going <b>SIX YEARS! SIX YEARS! SIX YEARS! </b>about whichever's not been released yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:39:58-08:00","id":1346794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346747#post1346747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think that's going to increase the free time afforded by their full time jobs?<br /> <br /> People remember that Robert Vance is a lawyer, don't they?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Will these people also be paid enough to live on, or need additional jobs themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that they wouldn't have to work Full-time if they didn't want to. Or again, hire some people to work in parallel if that is not possible.<br /> <br /> White Wolf/OPP isn't an indie developer. Hiring additional people/increasing the budget would probably be a sound investment, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's unreasonable to complain about just how slowly the books are being put out, considering how integral they are to play. Things referenced/used in the Core rulebook, like Sidearals and Abyssals...<br /> <br /> My point is just that there are ways to speed this up (without sacrificing quality) and it's a fair enough criticism of OPP that they can change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:44:35-08:00","id":1346797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346794#post1346794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf/OPP isn't an indie developer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact of the matter is, in the RPG industry, if you're not named &quot;Wizards of the Coast&quot;, you <i>are</i> an indie developer. Or, at least, the gap between you and an indie dev is much smaller than that between you and an actual company. As far as I recall from various things they've said, Onyx Path has something like two or three actual full employees. <i>Everyone</i> else is a freelancer. And that's probably economically necessary - the margins on RPG books are basically razor-thin. No one stays in RPG publishing because of the huge profits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:48:47-08:00","id":1346799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346797#post1346797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the margins on RPG books are basically razor-thin. No one stays in RPG publishing because of the huge profits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they do because they like angry fans on forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though it's hard to imagine producers of books that had such a massive in influence (Vampire, WereWolf, Exalted) in RPG culture are having trouble establishing themselves as a stable company. I wish my favorite hobby was in a better shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:05:06-08:00","id":1346809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346794#post1346794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is just that there are ways to speed this up (without sacrificing quality) and it's a fair enough criticism of OPP that they can change.</div> </div> </div> </div>OPP have sped up the process, though, including having different developers work on different projects. As was announced on the blog months ago, Crucible of Legends is developed by Monica and Neall, Lauren is one of the developers for MFS, and Robert and Eric develop Exigents. So that's three books developed at the same time. It's just too early to see the results because it's a fairly new change, but I think there are good reasons to be hopeful for the pacing going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:01:02-08:00","id":1346824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346794#post1346794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea was that they wouldn't have to work Full-time if they didn't want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting oneself through law school is a big personal and financial investment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or again, hire some people to work in parallel if that is not possible.<br /> <br /> White Wolf/OPP isn't an indie developer. Hiring additional people/increasing the budget would probably be a sound investment, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your opinion lacks objectivity or much understanding of the necessary resource management of a company like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's unreasonable to complain about just how slowly the books are being put out, considering how integral they are to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complaints can be reasonable sometimes. Asserting that one knows better about how to get the result one wants is often less so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is just that there are ways to speed this up (without sacrificing quality)</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:12:40-08:00","id":1346829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346809#post1346809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OPP have sped up the process, though, including having different developers work on different projects. As was announced on the blog months ago, Crucible of Legends is developed by Monica and Neall, Lauren is one of the developers for MFS, and Robert and Eric develop Exigents. So that's three books developed at the same time. It's just too early to see the results because it's a fairly new change, but I think there are good reasons to be hopeful for the pacing going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear. I hope that does turn this around and speeds up the release pace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T13:16:51-08:00","id":1346830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346799#post1346799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah they do because they like angry fans on forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though it's hard to imagine producers of books that had such a massive in influence (Vampire, WereWolf, Exalted) in RPG culture are having trouble establishing themselves as a stable company. I wish my favorite hobby was in a better shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... OPP <i><b>IS </b></i>a Stable Company.. they are just really small in comparison to, say, Wizards of the Coast. However, in my opinion, their quality puts Wizards of the Coast to shame, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:24:52-08:00","id":1346854,"title":"","content":"OPP also isn't the original WW despite being run by Rich Thomas.<br /> <br /> It's smaller than oWW when it got started; though with a larger stable of freelancers. It's smaller than nWW before Paradox absorbed them back in after the behind-the-scenes troubles with V5; and doesn't have the massive financial backing of Paradox (relatively speaking).<br /> <br /> Keeping OPP stable means Rich has to keep work flow at something OPP can handle (and OPP has a huge amount of books it's working on for a company it's size, even if spread out around a lot of properties). Hiring people to do more has limits to what the company can absorb without straining their resources. And some of this is outside of OPP's control. OPP could get ten Exalted books ready by throwing lots of money at them... but WW still has to approve all of them; which slows down the process even with WW not seeming to have much editorial concerns over Exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T14:48:46-08:00","id":1346858,"title":"","content":"I imagine as well that Exalted is not their main priority in terms of resources, compared to all the Vampire, Werewolf and Mage stuff.<br /> Though I've never quite understood how the WW-OP interaction actually works.<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, saying all this... Onyx Path is a business. Consumers don't owe them loyalty. If other RPG companies produce games you like at a good quality at a faster rate (or more useful rate; like DnD, Exalted's not really a game that's easy to run with one or even two books, you really need at least three, but there are rpgs that can be run out of one book), it's not ridiculous to say &quot;I'm going to spend my money on a different company's products.&quot;<br /> <br /> But there's also not much point shouting at a small company that's trying its best. It's like... I guess it's like if you go to a small restaurant, and you have to wait ages because they don't have enough staff. You don't need to give a big tip. It's okay to go to a different restaurant in future. But it seems mean to shout at the waitress/waiter about it, and it's not going to help. They know the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:18:09-08:00","id":1346869,"title":"","content":"Didn't Paradox give Vampire to an outside company after WW or OP caused some major controversies with their writing? Losing Vampire is kinda huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:22:37-08:00","id":1346871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346869#post1346869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Paradox give Vampire to an outside company after WW or OP caused some major controversies with their writing? Losing Vampire is kinda huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>OPP is working on a few Vampire books right now and likely will be tapped for future Werewolf when that happens. White Wolf as a separate entity from Paradox stopped when the head of that company and some authors working on some of the V5e books built up a lot of controversy and eventaully published books that crossed too many lines.<br /> <br /> Paradox still has and is working on WoD stuff, but has more or less outsourced that to other companies. But OPP still has the rights to published stuff (they do) and make CofD and Exalted without much interference (which they also do).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:28:15-08:00","id":1346873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346858#post1346858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine as well that Exalted is not their main priority in terms of resources, compared to all the Vampire, Werewolf and Mage stuff.<br /> Though I've never quite understood how the WW-OP interaction actually works.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted Kickstarters are some of the fastest and highest-funding projects for OPP still, actually. Most all the books are at least Gold on DTRPG, as noted already. In fact, going through Rich Thomas' listed projects, Lunars was the best-funded project they had since...Dragon-Blooded actually. The sales on DTRPG and the KS record to me indicate it does good. This is even kind of seen when yout hink how many books are on the plate for Exalted compared to other singular lines.<br /> <br /> It's just as been stated a few times, they have other games and audiences, and they only have so much that can be generated in so much time in the current RPG business.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:31:55-08:00","id":1346875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals#post1346010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I cannot imagine running a game long-term as Storyteller and not having need of an Abyssal and Sidereal books.</div> </div> </div> </div>while I greatly look forward to the development rate continuing at its achieved pace and these books coming in the next few years, it seems self evident to me that complex Creation spanning epics can easily be run with the mechanics of Solars and Dragon-Blooded alone, and are greatly enhanced by the addition of the Lunars. Solars alone were a problem because the concept of the setting they were playing in required the Dragon-Blooded specifically as their usurpers and oppressors occupying their stolen throne - but at this point, if the game hadn\u2019t already referenced the other types of Exalted, it could function as a complete setting as is, so I disagree with that statement that the game is somehow not runnable in the long term in its current form.<br /> <br /> again, massively looking forward to seeing Sidereals and Abyssals when they get here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:36:41-08:00","id":1346876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346869#post1346869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Paradox give Vampire to an outside company after WW or OP caused some major controversies with their writing? Losing Vampire is kinda huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>OPP didn\u2019t lose anything, except when Paradox first bought the White Wolf IPs, launched the 5th Edition efforts via reconstituted \u201cWhite Wolf\u201d as a subsidary and so further development on CWoD stuff by OPP was called off beyond what had already been promised. The controversy you are thinking of was all \u201cWhite Wolf\u201d causing Paradox to lose faith in said subsidiary and turn to outside licensers (including OPP) for further development of 5th edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-08-2019, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:41:12-08:00","id":1346879,"title":"","content":"For antagonists I'm not sure how useful having the full books even is that much. The QC antagonists are just way easier to run, they have a nice little power boost by not being penalized for making decisive attacks and often times their charms are just like the ones printed in the books except a little stronger, so their straightforward strength helps make up for their lack of complex power. Not fully, of course, QCs are always going to be a bit weaker, but it's worth taking so much load off the ST.<br /> <br /> It's really just for mixed games, or games for unreleased splats that the books have a huge impact I think. I've played in five or six campaigns with just the corebook and it barely felt lacking at all for those games, although I am looking forward to Heirs to the Shogunate to help round out my upcoming DB campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:45:14-08:00","id":1346881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346829#post1346829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's good to hear. I hope that does turn this around and speeds up the release pace.</div> </div> </div> </div>As was said more parallel production is happening for supplements, but in terms of hardbacks for each Exalted type that is unlikely to change from 1 a year (already a massive positive turn around from the dark days before Vance and Minton took the helm), as Vance and Minton overseeing those themselves is key to consistent quality and mechanics there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:57:08-08:00","id":1346882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346794#post1346794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> White Wolf/OPP isn't an indie developer. Hiring additional people/increasing the budget would probably be a sound investment, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf is an imprint with strong name recognition from before the industry crash in the early 00s. There was a Paradox subsidiary that recently bore that name, but it is unclear to the extent to which it still exists at all.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path is a tiny company with no larger corporate owner with razor thin margins. By the standards of this industry it is stable, but is absolutely \u201cindie\u201d by the standards of the 90s comparing it to the heyday of classic White Wolf. That isn\u2019t a fair standard given the industry today of course - WotC is enjoying a Critical Roll and Stranger Things fueled boom, but that hasn\u2019t extended outside of D&amp;D. The rest of the industry while recovering from the lowest slump of the height of WoW in the mid 00s, is nowhere near where it was in the 90s, and there is a reason overall production is centered on pdf releases and work is overwhelmingly freelance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T23:05:49-08:00","id":1346948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346879#post1346879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For antagonists I'm not sure how useful having the full books even is that much. The QC antagonists are just way easier to run, they have a nice little power boost by not being penalized for making decisive attacks and often times their charms are just like the ones printed in the books except a little stronger, so their straightforward strength helps make up for their lack of complex power. Not fully, of course, QCs are always going to be a bit weaker, but it's worth taking so much load off the ST.<br /> <br /> It's really just for mixed games, or games for unreleased splats that the books have a huge impact I think. I've played in five or six campaigns with just the corebook and it barely felt lacking at all for those games, although I am looking forward to Heirs to the Shogunate to help round out my upcoming DB campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I found that a)5 DBs (3 of them monks) was not nearly enough QCs, and b)they were way too weak. Possibly the Core's antagonists were fine for Essence 1-2 games, but they weren't much good for the Essence 4-5 game I was running.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T06:14:35-08:00","id":1346998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346948#post1346948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I found that a)5 DBs (3 of them monks) was not nearly enough QCs, and b)they were way too weak. Possibly the Core's antagonists were fine for Essence 1-2 games, but they weren't much good for the Essence 4-5 game I was running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, E4-E5 I can see there being a problem. To be honest I had some problems at E3 as well but I think some of that may have had to do with inexperience with the system and failure to use it to its full potential. <br /> <br /> For the bad cases I did find myself using Solar/Abyssal/infernal antagonists, although solars butt heads with those all the time so it didn\u2019t really feel contrived. It was hard though, unless I was copying something I\u2019d seen a PC do extensively before, coming up with a big high Essence antagonist, learning all the intricacies of their charmset, and using it properly ended up really taxing. When you\u2019re already planning adventures and coming up with NPC intimacies and figuring out how they\u2019ll all react to the PCs and thinking up puzzles it\u2019s a lot of work even with the book. I think what we need is just some truly insanely powerful QCs. I can understand the reluctance, different people have different expectations of the game and what PCs should be like, and also putting a lot of effort in for the very top end of the game only might not feel worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T07:20:41-08:00","id":1347012,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree. I ended up using a circle of Solars (well, 5 Solars, 2 Lunars and 1 Liminal), because that was what charms were available. And Supernal meant I could use Essence 3-4 Solars who could still be a challenge (but a beatable one) to 6 Essence 5 Solars.<br /> <br /> But an Essence 3-4 Solar, while a fine challenge for PCs, is quite awkward, because 30 charms is a lot to pick and then keep track of, especially for a Dawn or Night (Twilights are easier to keep track of, since they're not using all of them at once; if it's a Crafter, for example, you just give the group some artefacts and don't worry. If it's a sorcerer, they'll probably cast 2-3 spells in a fight max).<br /> <br /> Stuff like Octavian and Ahlat are much easier to run, since they're a challenge for Solars but have less charms to keep track of. I'd like more of that. Hundred Devils and Adversaries have helped, with the giant volcano monster and Makarios, but I'd really like more.<br /> Some Essence 4-5 Dragonblood would be great (ones that are a bit simpler, but just as balanced, as ones using the normal rules), as would some Third-Circle Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm now running a much lower essence Lunars game (they've just reached E2), so this is less of a problem now, but my friends who run essence 4-5 games still have to outsource the NPCs (ie get players to each made one E4 dragonblood and then run them in a fight) as it's so much work. And then, well, they're not actually a very difficult challenge for E5 Solars. The Night Caste beat his evil Abyssal brother in 2 rounds, 2 seperate PCs were ambushed by Wyld Hunts and got away without much difficulty (one lost a demon).<br /> There's just not much that can challenge an E5 Solar (well, other than their own stupidity).<br /> <br /> This isn't always a problem (I mean, E5 Solars are supposed to be some of the most powerful things in the setting), but to have a fun game, you need to give them some challenge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T07:43:09-08:00","id":1347020,"title":"","content":"Part of your issue might also be having 8 PCs. If you run a fight that\u2019s like, Alhat, two of his super charged spirit aurochs, a battlegroup of Brides, the Bride\u2019s commander and a high Essence Immaculate that Alhat has wrangled onto his side you now have 14 people in the initiative track, and that\u2019s just not feasible. Not to mention the PCs still outnumber the antagonists by an extra third and are much more powerful than most involved. Run that same fight against 3-4 PCs and the tables will turn drastically.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem with really powerful QCs might be how much character strength relies on system mastery, and how varied characters and group sizes can be. If you publish a third circle demon that\u2019s appropriate for eight Essence 5 Solars who really know what they\u2019re doing that puts it really off limits to a lot of groups.<br /> <br /> You might have to do it like Tiamat in DnD, who\u2019s technically beatable by a 4 person party, I think, but it\u2019s functionally impossible. She\u2019s inhumanly smart, ruthless, and unbelievably powerful. In the campaign she shows up in though there are a bunch of side adventures you can do which take away a lot of her powers and make her much easier to fight. That\u2019s probably the best way to do it. So you can have this big thing with 100 health levels, who freely and reflexively clashes any attack against it with its full pool, who\u2019s got 28 soak and 15 hardness with legendary size and octavians power to not fill more than one group of health levels at a time, but then there\u2019s ways to deactivate those and make it possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T08:22:56-08:00","id":1347029,"title":"","content":"Yeah I must admit I'm impressed every time you describe your tables Wizard of Oz I would never be able to handle tables this size","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T08:23:08-08:00","id":1347030,"title":"","content":"Exigents being next will probably help in a few respects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T08:23:28-08:00","id":1347031,"title":"","content":"6 PCs. It was 8 NPCs on the enemy side. They tended not to fight all at once though, it was generally 2-3 enemy Solars/Lunars/Liminal vs 2-5 PCs.<br /> But when each of those 2-3 enemy NPCs have 30 charms... it's just a ton of planning, and then awkward to remember them all in the heat of battle.<br /> I mean, I didn't find it impossible, just awkward.<br /> What would have been impossible of course, would have been running an Essence 5 game with primary antagonists other than Solars or Second-Circle Demons (there's Ahlat of course, but I don't think it's easy to make him the only primary antagonist.)<br /> <br /> Nowadays, I tend to write out the NPCs in a way that makes them easy for me to run in the game, and since it's all DBs, there's a lot of copy-paste which reduces prep times (ie giving 3 the same basic melee charms). So that works. But then, this is for Essence 2 DBs with about 6-7 pertinent charms (I assume they also have 10 charms for doing paperwork, enjoying parties, sending coded messages, playing music, and that these don't need to come up). Quite different from a Solar Night Caste Assassin with 15 combat charms and 10 stealth charms.<br /> <br /> But anyway, getting back to the main point, it is now possible to use Essence 5 Dragonblood, even if a circle of them is pretty awkward, but when I was running a Solar game, there just wasn't the resources to make it feasible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-08-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T08:49:13-08:00","id":1347037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347029#post1347029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I must admit I'm impressed every time you describe your tables Wizard of Oz I would never be able to handle tables this size</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I'm finding my new game way easier to run (and thus more enjoyable). I have 6 players, but inevitably 1-2 can't come so the game is 4-5 at a time. They stay together most of the time, the PCs generally get on, they're Essence 2 which makes the game simpler, there are no sorcerers so I never have to adjudicate Workings, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:42:50-08:00","id":1347052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1346858#post1346858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onyx Path is a business. Consumers don't owe them loyalty. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think consumer loyalty is the issue. A bit of empathy and redirect for appropriate boundaries is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:51:04-08:00","id":1347053,"title":"","content":"That was kind of my point with the &quot;don't shout at the waiter/waitress&quot; analogy. If you feel there's a problem with the gameline, you can say it calmly, you can stop playing, but not shout at or insult the writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T09:51:09-08:00","id":1347054,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it might be better to focus more on the lower Essence/lower power where the game tends to be easier and more interesting, or if that would just end up a vicious cycle where nobody likes playing at the high end because there\u2019s no easily ran content, and thus there\u2019s no demand for it so none of that kind of content gets produced.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not personally familiar with high Essence Solar, or even DB or Lunar games, in third edition. From what you\u2019ve seen Wizard, would that also be really hard to run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T10:27:36-08:00","id":1347062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347054#post1347054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it might be better to focus more on the lower Essence/lower power where the game tends to be easier and more interesting, or if that would just end up a vicious cycle where nobody likes playing at the high end because there\u2019s no easily ran content, and thus there\u2019s no demand for it so none of that kind of content gets produced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having seen a variety of levels of 3rd edition played/run (I guess everything from 0xp to 475xp), I think that there's (now, maybe not when the game is released) plenty of material for low-level games. The only problem is that the Core Book (and previous editions) mention Sidereals, Liminals, Getimians, Abyssals, etc, and you might go &quot;wow, that's really cool, I want to use it!&quot; and it's pretty limited. But if you're happy with Solars, Lunars, Dragonblood, Sorcerers, Demons, Elementals, some Gods and a variety of wacky monsters, it's fine (now).<br /> <br /> Whereas at high levels, there's less available, and if you want to use Solars/Dragonblood/Lunars you have to do a lot of prep work.<br /> <br /> So, from my perspective, I would like to see the remaining Adversaries of the Righteous and Hundred Devils Night Parade focus on high-level challenges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m also not personally familiar with high Essence Solar, or even DB or Lunar games, in third edition. From what you\u2019ve seen Wizard, would that also be really hard to run? </div> </div> </div>Much easier now than it was.<br /> <br /> Of the three, I think high-level Dragonblood is the easiest to run, since you can challenge the group with low-level Anathema; for a circle of Essence 5 Dragonblood, a circle of E1-2 Solars is a tough encounter, but it's not one that's very hard for the ST to make.<br /> <br /> As to Solar and Lunar games... well, there's all sorts of factors. Who are your main antagonists, what kind of campaign is it (social or combat-heavy?), etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T10:48:18-08:00","id":1347065,"title":"","content":"The Exalted killed and cast down the most powerful beings in existence.<br /> <br /> The &quot;high end&quot; of Exalted has never been about &quot;bigger numbers&quot;, it's supposed to be about what you do with your power now victory is assured, assymetric warfare, heroic sacrifice, attrition encounters and fixing the world on a global, nay <i>dimensional</i> scale.<br /> <br /> Like the opening battle in Thor: Dark World. Everyone is struggling against an endless tide of evil, then Thor (the Solar) rolls up, routs the army, kills the undefeated champion in a single swing of his hammer then goes away to brood on how he is different from his companions and on the love he has lost and the family he has hurt. Now, yes, he eventually has a couple of battles with Dr. Who (an Abyssal) on a roughly even pegging where he struggles against such a mighty foe... but for the most part, Thor <i>hilariously</i> outclasses all opposition to him, breezing through the deadly warriors that have slaughted his allies as if they were made of tissue paper.<br /> <br /> You can always challenge the Exalted with more Exalted. Or wave after wave of lesser challenges. But the majority of high-end sessions shouldn't be a challenge. They should be the invincible monstrousities that even gods fear just absolutely face-rolling n00bs by the kingdom in an unstoppable juggernaut of awesome, underpinned by poignant moments of humanity, laughter and loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-08-2019, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T11:12:27-08:00","id":1347070,"title":"","content":"There's a challenge and a challenge.<br /> <br /> I don't run combat-heavy games.<br /> I like to do a serious fight, but one that the PCs will clearly win (as opposed to say fighting some human soldiers, which I'd just get a Dawn to make a single Attribute+Ability roll to defeat rather than bother running a combat) every 3-4 sessions. That was never much of a problem.<br /> <br /> I like to do a challenging fight (that needs to, in-genre, be really impressive, like fight some mighty heroes or a behemoth) that stretches the PCs and gives them the opportunity to make use of their 25 combat charms, or Death Ray, or whatever, and feel like a total badass because they defeated this extremely difficult and mighty foe, at the end of a story.<br /> <br /> The first type is fine (couple of e3 Dragonblood, battle group of first circle demons, a Solar, etc) for high-level circles.<br /> <br /> The second type I found quite difficult with just the Core Book. The only way to do it was to a)attack 1-2 PCs alone, which is boring for the other players), b)have Ahlat and 100 war-gods attack half the party while the other half were elsewhere, c)use a circle of experienced Solars, d)use the First and Forsaken Lion.*<br /> <br /> *To be fair, he was a social challenge, but one of the PCs thought he was a combat challenge, so grapped the other Lunar and ran away. Sadly. I was looking forward to the Lion's centaur-ghost underling Chiron becoming the Lunar's new sifu. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't a combat-heavy situation; it was mostly a game about politics, changing whole societies and the effects of such, etc. But if there's no awesome fights against mighty enemies, what's even the point of a Dawn? Or the sorceress with Death Ray? Or the Full Moon?<br /> <br /> Nowadays, there are actually rules for the kind of things who can challenge a circle of E5 Solars in a fight besides other Solars; Lunars, Dragonblood, a giant volcano monster. But there's not much that doesn't need a lot of preparation (there's a bit). Making an entire Hearth of E4 Dragonblood to take on your PCs is a lot of work, running it is a lot of work, and it'll probably get slow as you're checking stuff which makes the fight less fun.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm hoping to see more things on the lines of Ahlat and Octavian, or preferably even better, like Third-Circle Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll also say I'm not just talking about challenging the PCs at combat. It's also about challenging them in other arenas. That's a bit easier than for combat, but it was still an issue when there were no rules for, say, high-level Dragonblood and Lunar social charms and world-affecting magic. It's better now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T11:27:06-08:00","id":1347073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347065#post1347065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exalted killed and cast down the most powerful beings in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of them than a circle of players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T12:12:40-08:00","id":1347077,"title":"","content":"Solars and Primordials is probably an interesting example...<br /> <br /> I kind of feel like, considering the number of Primordials who died, a challenging but doable campaign for a circle of essence 4-5 Solars would be maybe a 2nd circle and a battle group of first-circles every few sessions, a third circle and minions as the final boss of a story, and a Primordial as the culmination of a campaign.<br /> <br /> That would make rough sense to me, in terms of the campaign setting.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, considering the conceits and background of the setting, I think a circle of Essence 4-5 Solars should be able to beat a Third-Circle demon, but not like every session, it should be difficult enough to only manage occasionally as the story finale, with sensible preparation, and maybe one of the PCs will lose a limb.<br /> <br /> (A third-circle demon is, more than literally anything else, what I'd like to see in Adversaries of the Righteous. And then another two.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-08-2019, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T12:47:51-08:00","id":1347083,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know if I like the idea that it\u2019s really ever possible for a circle of solars to single handedly bear a primordial. Third circle demon, maybe, but we\u2019re talking about the entire soul hierarchy. A primordial has like, what, 5-6 third circle demons, and if each of those have 5-6 second circle demons that makes about 25-36 second circles, and then near endless hordes of first circle demons. Also their infernal exalted, Amun\u2019s, and other allies. Which is also assuming that if you\u2019re going after She Who Lives In Her Name that The Ebon Dragon or Malfeas don\u2019t decide to get involved and start moving against you.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not a great idea for a campaign, but not something a group of Solars, even high Essence ones, can do without help. Primordials are a class of being that almost won a war against every single exalt working together at the same time. <br /> <br /> It would be nice to have some stats for that though if you want to run something like it, particularly since summon third circle demon is a spell that exists and is currently practically useless. It would also help the feeling that the writers of the charms section and the writers of the antagonist section were designing two entirely separate games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T13:11:16-08:00","id":1347087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347077#post1347077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(A third-circle demon is, more than literally anything else, what I'd like to see in Adversaries of the Righteous. And then another two.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I'd heard (nearly two years ago) there was a brand new Third Circle written up, but they have yet to be released. When I first heard of it, I though &quot;Oh, nice. I've really wanted one of those since forever. Hopefully it'll come out by the time my sorceress achieves Solar Circle Sorcery, and surely it'll at least come out before the campaign concludes...&quot;<br /> <br /> Nope. Incredibly maddening, especially when we end up getting serviceable but entirely straightforward and mechanically uninteresting conversion of previous edition creatures. What's the point of overpriced episodic content &quot;to get stuff out fast&quot; if you're going to save the most universally useful things for last?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T14:29:06-08:00","id":1347100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347083#post1347083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if I like the idea that it\u2019s really ever possible for a circle of solars to single handedly bear a primordial. Third circle demon, maybe, but we\u2019re talking about the entire soul hierarchy. A primordial has like, what, 5-6 third circle demons, and if each of those have 5-6 second circle demons that makes about 25-36 second circles, and then near endless hordes of first circle demons. Also their infernal exalted, Amun\u2019s, and other allies. Which is also assuming that if you\u2019re going after She Who Lives In Her Name that The Ebon Dragon or Malfeas don\u2019t decide to get involved and start moving against you.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s not a great idea for a campaign, but not something a group of Solars, even high Essence ones, can do without help. Primordials are a class of being that almost won a war against every single exalt working together at the same time.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to have some stats for that though if you want to run something like it, particularly since summon third circle demon is a spell that exists and is currently practically useless. It would also help the feeling that the writers of the charms section and the writers of the antagonist section were designing two entirely separate games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's where you are supposed to use the fact that, since you are Essence 4 Solar, you (hopefully) have a long story of people who owe you one because you helped them, and while they are fighting other invaders/blocking the gates of endless demons/distracting the 3rd circle demons that came in reinforcement, you are fighting the main soul or something like that.<br /> <br /> I try to think of show that have a finale like that, for example Shaman King, or last season of Samurai Jack. That's how I imagine it, the story of your life and of all the hard choices you had to make culminating to help you change the face of Creation for the ultimate challenge of your life. Not all campaigns of Solar Essence 4 should be like that of course, but I'd really like to have the opportunity to do it at least once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T15:19:07-08:00","id":1347111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347077#post1347077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars and Primordials is probably an interesting example...<br /> <br /> I kind of feel like, considering the number of Primordials who died, a challenging but doable campaign for a circle of essence 4-5 Solars would be maybe a 2nd circle and a battle group of first-circles every few sessions, a third circle and minions as the final boss of a story, and a Primordial as the culmination of a campaign.<br /> <br /> That would make rough sense to me, in terms of the campaign setting.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, considering the conceits and background of the setting, I think a circle of Essence 4-5 Solars should be able to beat a Third-Circle demon, but not like every session, it should be difficult enough to only manage occasionally as the story finale, with sensible preparation, and maybe one of the PCs will lose a limb.<br /> <br /> (A third-circle demon is, more than literally anything else, what I'd like to see in Adversaries of the Righteous. And then another two.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there would be some interesting discussion about how such a campaign might be presented, but my point was more that the War of the Gods should not really be treated as a baseline for what challenges the Exalted, as it is so frustratingly often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:04:14-08:00","id":1347186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347111#post1347111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure there would be some interesting discussion about how such a campaign might be presented, but my point was more that the War of the Gods should not really be treated as a baseline for what challenges the Exalted, as it is so frustratingly often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when you replied to John it made me think of how it actually would be reflected, and I actually think it is okay.<br /> <br /> I think more the issue is that people use the example badly. As you said, just because the Solars won the Primordial War, doesn't mean one circle of Solars should definitely be able to beat a Primordial so anything less shouldn't be a challenge.<br /> <br /> After all, it was 2 Primordials (the weakest, but still Primordials) 800-1000 Celestials and 10000 Dragonblood, with the support and backing of the entire host of heaven and probably most of the elementals, vs something in the region of 40-50 Primordials, and they managed to kill less than half. Plus of 800 Celestials, it's quite possible that thousands of Celestials died.<br /> <br /> So a Third Circle Demon should be something a circle of high-essence Celestials can beat, but it should absolutely not be easy. If it was, the Primordial War would have been easy to win, and I'm sure it's not supposed to have been. Once/story I think.<br /> And even a Yozi or Primordial should be beatable for a high-essence circle of Celestials... with the help of allies. Probably not something they can do by themselves (since in the Primordial War the Solars were working with the Lunars, the Sidereals, and the Dragonblood). Hence my suggestion that it could be the pinnacle of a whole campaign. First you'd have to kill some of its Third-Circles to weaken it, you'd need to gather allies to help fight it, you'd need to research its weaknesses, have your crafter build the weapon that exploits its weaknesses, convince its allies to abandon it, lure it into the right environment, and then fight.<br /> <br /> That's the kind of difficulty level I'd expect for E5 Solars.<br /> <br /> (Saying this, I'm not arguing that the current game must reflect the Primordial War, as some do. I'm just saying I think it's okay if it does, as long as you think that's through.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;high end&quot; of Exalted has never been about &quot;bigger numbers&quot;, it's supposed to be about what you do with your power now victory is assured, assymetric warfare, heroic sacrifice, attrition encounters and fixing the world on a global, nay <i>dimensional</i> scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know a lot of people say high-level Exalted is about PCs who can do anything but must deal with the consequences of their actions, and I'm going to be straight about this... it gets old. The PCs walk into yet another kingdom, overthrow the government, crush the rebels, social-fu the aristocracy. And then they do it again, and again. And of course there are countless social problems due to their ham-handed force, and then the players get frustrated because all they're trying to do is build a mighty empire and they keep having to run around fighting low-level problems that they easily social-fu or beat into submission when they find them...<br /> <br /> I don't mean that this isn't something that should be done at all. It should. And to some extent it is fun. But an <i>entire</i> campaign with no challenges (and I don't just mean combat challenges, as I said my games aren't very combat-heavy) gets boring.<br /> <br /> Nor am I saying Exalted should be a hard game. I like my players to think big. I like them to fight armies, create Kingdoms, overthrow the evil empire, etc, etc. I mean, in my new game (Lunars who've only just reached Essence 2, so they have a max of 1 Essence 2 charm), they're literally on their way right now to the Elemental Pole of Air to face Mela the Air-Dragon.<br /> <br /> But it shouldn't be a game where the answer to every challenge is &quot;you win easily&quot;.<br /> <br /> The current Essence 4-5 game I'm playing (well, it's on hiatus) is a lot of fun but actually quite challenging because our enemies constantly use misdirection and confusion, proxies, etc. It's an Investigation-based plot essentially, trying to work out what the High Priest Who Shall Not Be Described is actually up to, where he is, who's working for him and how do we stop him, how is he connected to the Worm Cult, etc. Even with my Investigation charms, it's difficult, and that makes it interesting. If I'd found that Nephwrack 2 games into the story arc and beaten him up in a couple of rounds it wouldn't have been nearly as fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2019, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:12:41-08:00","id":1347187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347087#post1347087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I'd heard (nearly two years ago) there was a brand new Third Circle written up, but they have yet to be released. When I first heard of it, I though &quot;Oh, nice. I've really wanted one of those since forever. Hopefully it'll come out by the time my sorceress achieves Solar Circle Sorcery, and surely it'll at least come out before the campaign concludes...&quot;<br /> <br /> Nope. Incredibly maddening, especially when we end up getting serviceable but entirely straightforward and mechanically uninteresting conversion of previous edition creatures. What's the point of overpriced episodic content &quot;to get stuff out fast&quot; if you're going to save the most universally useful things for last?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are very useful things in those books; some of the Exalted NPCs, big animals (for Lunars), Makarios, the Raksha whose name I forget.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I really, really want that third circle, and every time they release a wacky essence 1 monster or some human or god-blood NPC, I feel disappointed it's not the Third Circle Demon of the Ebon Dragon that Eric wrote.<br /> <br /> I mean, a lot of the wacky monsters are kind of fun or cool, but I've never actually got much use out of them. Partly because they're quite weak, but partly because they're a bit random and disconnected and don't come up so much in a campaign, unless you want a random encounter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T01:33:59-08:00","id":1347192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347083#post1347083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know if I like the idea that it\u2019s really ever possible for a circle of solars to single handedly bear a primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, I didn't mean single-handedly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A primordial has like, what, 5-6 third circle demons, </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, it was 8-25.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if each of those have 5-6 second circle demons </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, it was always 7.<br /> <br /> So we're talking like 100+ Second Circles.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm assuming that by the time your party has reached Essence 5, as you're probably not all playing murderhoboes, you probably have your own bound servitors, lower-level Solar allies, Lunar mates, etc. So they can battle some of this stuff, distracting it, while you strike at the main things.<br /> <br /> In our game that's only just reached E5, we don't have many, but in the game that's now about 475xp, if the PCs coordinated properly (rather than bickering), they could bring to the table:<br /> <br /> The PCs (essence 5 Dawn general/tank, Zenith preacher, social Eclipse, Solar Sorcerer Eclipse, Full Moon doctor, social Casteless)<br /> An e5 Full Moon sorcerer and his e5 Twilight crafter Solar Mate (retired PCs, still friends with PCs)<br /> Lower essence (I think 2-3) Dawn meleeist, Zenith raised by Dragon Kings, Twilight Alfred the Great expy, Full Moon general, his No Moon scheming lieutenant and Full Moon panther goon, Full Moon bear-man with an army of guerillas based in a thorn forest<br /> A Sidereal<br /> Several second circle demons<br /> A few Dragonblood<br /> A warstrider (currently no-one's using it, but they could learn easily)<br /> 20-30 flying fire-breathing monsters<br /> A hundred hypogriffs<br /> Dozens of fire mages<br /> Dozens of war golems<br /> A village of veteran ninja beastmen<br /> Thousands of tiger warriors<br /> Thousands of magically created elite soldiers<br /> <br /> So that's actually 16 Celestial Exalts. And if there was a Yozi or something, they could probably gather more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be nice to have some stats for that though if you want to run something like it, particularly since summon third circle demon is a spell that exists and is currently practically useless. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> I guess we've got a bit away from it with my point about Primordials, maybe that is a bit hard, but essentially I was saying:<br /> <br /> High-essence games still need challenges.<br /> A Third-Circle Demon is supposed to be a tough but doable challenge for a group of high-essence Solars.<br /> It would be much easier to run than a circle of high-Essence Dragonblood, which is the only real thing of a suitable power level there are currently rules for (there's also Ahlat I guess?).<br /> We really therefore could do with some Third-Circle Demons.<br /> Even, say, 2 quite different ones would give us plenty of examples/inspiration to design more to fit your exact campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would also help the feeling that the writers of the charms section and the writers of the antagonist section were designing two entirely separate games. </div> </div> </div>What do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2019, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T05:06:39-08:00","id":1347220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347186#post1347186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people say high-level Exalted is about PCs who can do anything but must deal with the consequences of their actions, and I'm going to be straight about this... it gets old. The PCs walk into yet another kingdom, overthrow the government, crush the rebels, social-fu the aristocracy. And then they do it again, and again. And of course there are countless social problems due to their ham-handed force, and then the players get frustrated because all they're trying to do is build a mighty empire and they keep having to run around fighting low-level problems that they easily social-fu or beat into submission when they find them...<br /> <br /> I don't mean that this isn't something that should be done at all. It should. And to some extent it is fun. But an <i>entire</i> campaign with no challenges (and I don't just mean combat challenges, as I said my games aren't very combat-heavy) gets boring.<br /> <br /> Nor am I saying Exalted should be a hard game. I like my players to think big. I like them to fight armies, create Kingdoms, overthrow the evil empire, etc, etc. I mean, in my new game (Lunars who've only just reached Essence 2, so they have a max of 1 Essence 2 charm), they're literally on their way right now to the Elemental Pole of Air to face Mela the Air-Dragon.<br /> <br /> But it shouldn't be a game where the answer to every challenge is &quot;you win easily&quot;.<br /> <br /> The current Essence 4-5 game I'm playing (well, it's on hiatus) is a lot of fun but actually quite challenging because our enemies constantly use misdirection and confusion, proxies, etc. It's an Investigation-based plot essentially, trying to work out what the High Priest Who Shall Not Be Described is actually up to, where he is, who's working for him and how do we stop him, how is he connected to the Worm Cult, etc. Even with my Investigation charms, it's difficult, and that makes it interesting. If I'd found that Nephwrack 2 games into the story arc and beaten him up in a couple of rounds it wouldn't have been nearly as fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly what I described.<br /> <br /> You're not going to fight an entire Wyld Hunt, or outwit Saturn, or seduce The Lover Clad every session. These types of challenges should be what play builds up to: nine sessions out of ten will not have these challenges. The 90% will be challenges which you could cake-walk, it'll be how you choose to apply your power. Do you break Loki free from the toughest prison in the Nine Realms (yawn, easy) or do you obey your father's commands and rally his armies? You can do either trivally, but you can't do both. How many resources do you expend on these tasks? How do you use your allies? How do you expend your Essence? Does the constant attrition of low level encounters wear you down and stretch you thin? Do your adversaries, knowing you'd breeze through them in a straight fight, switch to assymetric warfare -- faking their deaths and sneaking onto the throne of your kingdom in disguise? Are you saving New York City, or are you collecting learned allies who build artifacts that let you save all of existence from the Convergance?<br /> <br /> Running a fight against an entire Circle of Abyssals is a lot of work. But it shouldn't be happening except at the culmination of a story. And whether you beat them because you've raised a mighty kingdom, or gathered powerful gods to your banner, or crafted invincible artifacts (or whether you lose because you've wasted your time and squandered your power) is you reaping what you've sown with the thousand choices you made on all the trival encounters building up to that moment. And it you win, you deal with the fallout of dead allies and a growing legend and that impacts the next story. (And if you lose, you take it on the chin and deal with those consequences instead.)<br /> <br /> Thor doesn't spend all of The Dark World effortlessly winning and brooding over his phenomenal power. But that's how he spends most of the film as it builds to an epic finale. (And when he is challenged, it's by invisible beings making a sneak attack against civilians, or by a being of roughly equal power swinging an N/A artifact.)<br /> <br /> Would this be easier with published high-end enemies? Probably not. The power divergence between two Essence 5 Solars is massive. You're pretty much going to have to hand-craft your Malekith, breaking all the normal rules for PCs. Having a template that says &quot;Accuracy: 25 Damage: 30 (7)&quot; wouldn't help me run that encounter. The best cheat sheet is the PCs own character sheets -- refluff their abilities and throw that back at them.<br /> <br /> I'd really love to see stats for 3CDs but &quot;Today we're going to fight... Mara&quot; wouldn't help me. Might as well just add six dice to all Ahlat's pools and call him Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-09-2019, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T06:51:08-08:00","id":1347230,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you call &quot;trivial&quot;. Overall I don't agree with you, I don't feel like 9/10 games should be trivial. Or rather, they shouldn't feel trivial. Obviously I don't want my players to have chances to fail 40% of the time because this is not warhammer, but I don't want them to feel &quot;Well the road was easy&quot;. I want them to feel it was hard and well-earned, even if that doesn't mean they had huge chances of losses.<br /> <br /> I think it's possible we are saying the same thing without understanding each other, also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T06:57:00-08:00","id":1347232,"title":"","content":"I don't get the impression the idea is about &quot;You win, but consequences...&quot; so much as that 90% of Exalted games will be effectively a kind of training montage where you gather different strengths and weaknesses (artefacts, allies, special moves), but your survival is never really in doubt, that then prefigure the style of the remaining 10% of the game in which you have a denouement with some sort of epic foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T08:52:43-08:00","id":1347251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347232#post1347232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the impression the idea is about &amp;quot;You win, but consequences...&amp;quot; so much as that 90% of Exalted games will be effectively a kind of training montage where you gather different strengths and weaknesses (artefacts, allies, special moves), but your survival is never really in doubt, that then prefigure the style of the remaining 10% of the game in which you have a denouement with some sort of epic foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda.<br /> <br /> 90% of sessions are never going to end in a TPK. But it's more than a training montage: these are the sessions where the PCs are achieving. They're making allies. They're making enemies. They're single-handedly slaying armies and being awesome. It's about collecting resources, uncovering secrets, setting the stage -- but the important thing isn't &quot;training&quot;, it's the choices the PCs make, who they're helping, who they're hurting. Less &quot;yes but&quot; more &quot;yes and&quot;.<br /> <br /> 90% of sessions are about how awesome the PCs are and giving them the chance to shape the game world. This is important because it's building to something bigger, but it's also important in its own right because its most of the game.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347230#post1347230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you call &amp;quot;trivial&amp;quot;. Overall I don't agree with you, I don't feel like 9/10 games should be trivial. Or rather, they shouldn't feel trivial. Obviously I don't want my players to have chances to fail 40% of the time because this is not warhammer, but I don't want them to feel &amp;quot;Well the road was easy&amp;quot;. I want them to feel it was hard and well-earned, even if that doesn't mean they had huge chances of losses.<br /> <br /> I think it's possible we are saying the same thing without understanding each other, also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things should feel dramatic, absolutely. But the PCs are awesome and should &quot;win&quot; the vast majority of encounters. 90% of encounters should be based on &quot;what happens after the PCs win&quot;, not &quot;will the PCs win or lose&quot;.<br /> <br /> And this, outside of GrimDark and Horror games, is pretty much how most games should go. Then it becomes a question of scope and margins for success -- and that's what makes Exalted interesting to me. My level 5 D&amp;D Wizard <b>will</b> win the encounter with the Kobolds, but what does that mean for the story and the game world? Probably a lot less than my Twilight conquering an entire kingdom. The D&amp;D game is about collecting treasure until I can fight the dragon and clear the dungeon, and that's cool. Exalted is building to me conquering the world and ushering in ten thousand years of peace and prosperity, and how I do that is the interesting part of the story. It's the scope of what you've done and the scale of your actions.<br /> <br /> Yes there should be encounters that make the PCs go all-out, but they should be rare and they need to be tailored carefully. And if the PCs aren't going all-out, and are expected to win anyway, then the default antagonists are fine -- you've just got to use them interestingly. (And who says you can't Death Ray a Talon of mortal conscripts? Mwhahaha!)<br /> <br /> What you don't want, is the Oblivion Effect, where enemies level up alongside you and random bandits just happen to be the most powerful warriors in the world just so the PCs remain &quot;challenged&quot; (by random encounters that they're never supposed to lose and don't advance the story).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:08:45-08:00","id":1347255,"title":"","content":"Yeah ok I think we get each other, for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:11:04-08:00","id":1347287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347220#post1347220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is exactly what I described.<br /> <br /> You're not going to fight an entire Wyld Hunt, or outwit Saturn, or seduce The Lover Clad every session. These types of challenges should be what play builds up to: nine sessions out of ten will not have these challenges. The 90% will be challenges which you could cake-walk, it'll be how you choose to apply your power. Do you break Loki free from the toughest prison in the Nine Realms (yawn, easy) or do you obey your father's commands and rally his armies? You can do either trivally, but you can't do both. How many resources do you expend on these tasks? How do you use your allies? How do you expend your Essence? Does the constant attrition of low level encounters wear you down and stretch you thin? Do your adversaries, knowing you'd breeze through them in a straight fight, switch to assymetric warfare -- faking their deaths and sneaking onto the throne of your kingdom in disguise? Are you saving New York City, or are you collecting learned allies who build artifacts that let you save all of existence from the Convergance?<br /> <br /> Running a fight against an entire Circle of Abyssals is a lot of work. But it shouldn't be happening except at the culmination of a story. And whether you beat them because you've raised a mighty kingdom, or gathered powerful gods to your banner, or crafted invincible artifacts (or whether you lose because you've wasted your time and squandered your power) is you reaping what you've sown with the thousand choices you made on all the trival encounters building up to that moment. And it you win, you deal with the fallout of dead allies and a growing legend and that impacts the next story. (And if you lose, you take it on the chin and deal with those consequences instead.)<br /> <br /> Thor doesn't spend all of The Dark World effortlessly winning and brooding over his phenomenal power. But that's how he spends most of the film as it builds to an epic finale. (And when he is challenged, it's by invisible beings making a sneak attack against civilians, or by a being of roughly equal power swinging an N/A artifact.)<br /> <br /> Would this be easier with published high-end enemies? Probably not. The power divergence between two Essence 5 Solars is massive. You're pretty much going to have to hand-craft your Malekith, breaking all the normal rules for PCs. Having a template that says &quot;Accuracy: 25 Damage: 30 (7)&quot; wouldn't help me run that encounter. The best cheat sheet is the PCs own character sheets -- refluff their abilities and throw that back at them.<br /> <br /> I'd really love to see stats for 3CDs but &quot;Today we're going to fight... Mara&quot; wouldn't help me. Might as well just add six dice to all Ahlat's pools and call him Mars.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it sounds like, other than arguing about semantics (like the meaning of &quot;trivial&quot;), we're mostly agreeing. I too was saying that fighting an entire Circle of Abyssals or whatever is happening at the culmination of a story. (Though they should pop up individually or in terms of their influence during the story, of course.) I think we're only really disagreeing about the use of published resources.<br /> <br /> My original point is that, when the Core Book was out, all that there was available to challenge a high-level group was a Circle of Solars (which is what I ended up using) or a Circle of Abyssals using solar rules.<br /> <br /> And I felt I really needed more options than just a Circle of Solars to run more than, well, the campaign of fighting a rival circle of Solars.<br /> <br /> Now you can also use a load of high-Essence Dragonblood, which you didn't use to be able to. And this is still fiendishly complex, because of all the charms and Aura and stuff, though at least we now actually have rules for it (we didn't when I was running e5 Exalted). (It's also not actually very difficult for a whole circle of Solars, they basically have to ambush you one or two at a time.)<br /> <br /> A Third-Circle would be much easier to run, and people complaining about how difficult it is to run high-essence Exalted is something that's popped up quite a lot on this thread and forum.<br /> <br /> But mostly I just want more options than &quot;Circle of Solaroids&quot;, &quot;Circle of Dragonblood&quot;, &quot;different Circle of Solaroids&quot;. Especially as we've played Exalted so long. I actually promised my players no more Abyssal circles because they were so fed up with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having a template that says &quot;Accuracy: 25 Damage: 30 (7)&quot; wouldn't help me run that encounter. </div> </div> </div>No, that bit is piss easy, as you say you can just add 6 dice to Ahlat. The point is the charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not going to fight an entire Wyld Hunt,... These types of challenges should be what play builds up ... The 90% will be challenges which you could cake-walk, </div> </div> </div>Believe me, if they're not split up, for a circle of e5 Solars a Wyld Hunt is... not quite a cakewalk, but not really a challenge. The time my PCs did it, I think one of them took like 2 damage and that was it. Magma Kraken collapsing a building on their head and a battle group of Greenmaws tanked most of the Wyld Hunt, while the PCs killed the other Dragonblood and chopped through soldiers. I mean, it was fine as a fun session and fight, but I wouldn't really say it was a challenge.<br /> <br /> The only fights that were/are really a stretching challenge, would be the fights where they were significantly outnumbered by rival Solars, or when Ahlat and 100 war-gods ambushed 3 of them. (Two of them did run away once from the First and Forsaken Lion, because one thought he was trying to kill them, but really he just wanted to be friends. So I wouldn't really count that as a difficult fight per-se.)<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying the pacing of the game or its difficulty level was awful, because I thought a lot about it, saw the issues of the game coming, saw how easily they chopped through Dragonblood and anything weaker, and so put them up against either 2nd circle demons or Solars (they went after the Solars and didn't really bother with the demon cult).<br /> <br /> I'm just saying that it was quite restrictive, having to use the stuff from the Core Book (ie Solars), and a bit hard to run fights (because each of the 5 Solar NPCs had 30+ charms). And other people have mentioned the same issues.<br /> (Obviously, if you've found ways around this when running e5 Solar games, I'm willing to hear any advice.)<br /> <br /> Now there's also high-essence Lunars, or essence-5 Dragonblood, but I'd still like more options and antagonists that can be serious nemeses for high-essence Solars, and preferably ones where I don't have to remember/check between 100 charms during the fight (as well as motes, initiative, willpower, overwhelming, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying all this, I stopped running an e5 game partly because I found it too tricky (and also other reasons related to the story, characters, etc), and I'm now running an e2 Lunar game, so it's pretty fine. The first two stories the PCs faced off against an army led by 10 Dragonblood, and I didn't find running/making them too bad (especially with copy-paste) as they were all essence 2-3. And other reasonable challenges might be a circle of starting Solars, or a Second-Circle Demon, or an elemental Dragon (they are in fact travelling to face the Elemental Dragon of Air herself, which probably is an unreasonable challenge, but I believe in them). So I'm happy with the resources I have. I'm just giving advice/suggestions for others who are running e5 games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2019, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:27:00-08:00","id":1347291,"title":"","content":"Solars at the height of their power seem like the kind of thing the Realm should treat as requiring the nuclear option, rather than sending a typical Wyld Hunt against them. Something that the greatest weapons in their arsenal are directed against.<br /> <br /> They might not be able to use the Realm Defence Grid, but one of those war manses like the one in Greyfalls seems like it could provide some artillery support to the thousand-year daiklaves and warstriders.<br /> <br /> And the Bronze Faction is really remiss in letting them go in alone.<br /> <br /> How many years are your Essence 5 Solars supposed to have been in operation anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T12:28:24-08:00","id":1347312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347291#post1347291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars at the height of their power seem like the kind of thing the Realm should treat as requiring the nuclear option, rather than sending a typical Wyld Hunt against them. Something that the greatest weapons in their arsenal are directed against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. The Realm didn't just send the Wyld Hunt to take on Yurgen Kaneko, they sent whole Legions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How many years are your Essence 5 Solars supposed to have been in operation anyway? </div> </div> </div>It's a bit complicated. Over a few years they became major threats to the Realm, breaking in to the Imperial Manse, murdering one of the Realm's two ruling consuls, and using the Imperial Manse to cause devastation and chaos.*<br /> <br /> *Most of this isn't true, but it's what the Realm thinks.<br /> <br /> Then most of them kind of vanished for 25 years. They returned and operated for about a year before the Wyld Hunt (led by Cynis Danu, whose kung-fu teacher was murdered by one of the PCs*) came to the area to investigate rumours of Anathema, called by a local Dragonblood dynasty who were pissed that the PCs were meddling in local politics. They expected a handful of Essence 1 Solars maybe led by an Essence 4 Lunar, maybe not. What they got was 4 essence 4 Solars and 2 essence 4 Lunars, who'd been mostly keeping their powers on the downlow until then.<br /> <br /> *Again, not actually true.<br /> <br /> The PCs ambushed the Wyld Hunt, killing half, and the other half got away.<br /> <br /> Of course, now the Realm knows what it's dealing with (and the Dragonblood book is out), they're sending 3 Legions, and have ended their war with Ahlat's Empire so they can ally with him against us.<br /> <br /> We have had a couple of Wyld Hunt attacks, but not really at our main power base. A)because they'd die horribly if they tried, and B)because their plan is to divide and conquer, and doing that might make the PCs cooperate.<br /> <br /> One Wyld Hunt attack was when the Eclipse spymaster (who's the worst at combat) was spying in Kirighast, and the Wyld Hunt jumped out and tried to attack her. She had no backup here, so it was a sensible plan; although she escaped, none of them were in danger from her really.<br /> <br /> The other... I'm not sure if they were serious about killing her or not. It might have been. It started out as a kind of retaliatory attack as part of a Mutual Destruction thing. The Eclipse sorceress-queen destroyed Ahlat's fleet with Death Ray so he couldn't invade our central temple. So a Sidereal (we assume) used Cantata of Empty Voices on one of the queen's military outposts, killing hundreds of soldiers and some monsters. They then sent her a letter saying that every time she used sorcery to nuke their side, they'd use sorcery to nuke her side, so they ought to have a straight-forward war without spells of mass destruction.<br /> When she went to have a look at her outpost, a Wyld Hunt of Water Aspects (including a warstrider) ambushed her from the sea. They killed her dragon-mount and one or two of her bound Second Circle Demons, but she managed to teleport away and the other Second-Circles used Hurry Home to go after her.<br /> I'm not sure if this was a serious attempt to kill her or just part of the warning. I assume it was the former though, as it was a pretty good plan to ambush one Solar far from any other Solars.<br /> <br /> The Legions should start their attack within the next couple of months, I assume the Wyld Hunt will stay in the area for ambush attacks when they can get one Solar away from the others, but I assume that to attack the whole group, they'll want to be using a whole Legion.<br /> <br /> So anyway, the Wyld Hunt can be a challenge for one Solar PC at high-level (though it depends on the Solar of course), but for an entire Circle, well, that's what giant invasions are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T14:12:38-08:00","id":1347321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347192#post1347192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's maybe not quite THAT bad, but sometimes looking at the various antagonists makes it feel like there's a disconnect between what the writers of those antagonists expect the players to be able to do, and what they can do.<br /> <br /> There's just a bunch of enemies in the books, and supplements even, that have like, 6-7 dice to their attacks. Like the angler lizard, fog shark, hellboar, flickerfeather or pestletail. They're absolutely zero threat to the fighters, which is okay, but they're almost no threat at all to the people who aren't either. It only takes about 10% of your starting dots to get melee 3, pick up a sword, maybe a specialty and with the free Solar excellency you're just nearly immune to those attacks for less than your per-round mote regen.<br /> <br /> You might think &quot;Well 10% is kind of a lot.&quot; but I don't know if it is. If you're 90% social focused I'd say you're not a combat character, and I don't know how many non-combat focused characters I've seen with less than that, but not many. So in a group of PCs you have the weak social/mental characters who aren't threatened at all, and the big powerful combat characters who are even less than that.<br /> <br /> What's worse is Hellboars have all these abilities; Bone-Crunching Bite, Death Stomp, trample, Femur-Smashing Crunch. War ghosts have that cool ethereal flicker blade...with their 7 die attack. There's all these cool things I want to use them for as an ST and it's just not really working. The worst are abilities that key off decisive attacks, because for <i>those </i>to ever have a chance of working the enemies have to build up initiative, and then keep it for a whole turn until they can act again to try and use it.<br /> <br /> It's not just attacks, the ambush predators like claw striders have 6 dice to their stealth rolls and stuff. If we're saying a troupe of gorillas going apeshit on the party should be beneath the concerns of the Exalted, then fine, just don't waste my time and your wordcount to get my hopes up that I might have an interesting action scene with them. Rather than me trying and just having maybe one ape get lucky and hit in the first round of combat, every other one getting crashed, and then dead or driven off in round 2.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't use any antagonist in the book, there's ones that are good. A big pack of claw striders ambushing the party at night with environmental penalties might force them to spend some motes, which might be relevant later on. Or you might have a first age ruin with an entire battlegroup of Walking Statues, and their automation commander. Even then, the party isn't in danger, they'll just be actually spending motes, which might matter for the next scene that they're in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The other side of that is a lot of solar powers that seem to have been written for fun, but got kind of out of control because there's nothing really to battle that needs them. Like Divine Executioner Stance or Aegis of Invincible Might. Or the sail system, where the excellency is all you need to win basically any fight, and then you've just got like 20 charms that make it progressively more overkill, completely pointlessly.<br /> <br /> Bulding off of how difficult it is to land a decisive attack with initiative for a lot of enemies, there's all these charms in medicine and resistance that give you more health levels, or let you heal those health levels faster, but they're such a waste if you never take health level damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't even want my PCs to succeed 90% of the time, I want them to win MORE than 90% of the time, like 99% of the time, as long as they're not being completely suicidal in the battles they pick. What I do want is for them to actually have to think for a second to win rather than me just pointlessly rolling 7 dice to try and hit their parry of 8 over and over, and for there to be some back and forth. Like maybe PC take a level of health damage and now they're wounded for a day or two, or get slammed through the floor only to pick themselves up, dust off and win anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T15:28:44-08:00","id":1347331,"title":"","content":"Thanks I think you summed up what I expect from this game and what I failed to understand about the game for my first year of STing it. I got better at it now that I homebrew something to have better and more flexible NPC's but there is still more to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T22:19:16-08:00","id":1347403,"title":"","content":"Our current game has been interesting in terms of combat. We started out with a PvP tournament arc and that set the bar pretty high for combat, so everything since has been difficult but manageable (a lesser elemental dragon, a Wyld Hunt with a full wing of the Silent Legion and a Sidereal) or surprisingly easy (A less-prepared Wyld Hunt with two hundred above-average mortal battle groups, a lone abyssal vs. a lone solar) and most of the time the real conflict comes from our characters personal hangups about when and whom it is okay to fight.<br /> <br /> Essence 2 party, btw. One Night, two Twilights, one Zenith, one Full-Moon, one Dusk (formerly one Eclipse instead of the full-moon).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24172-sticks","name":"Sticks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T01:17:29-08:00","id":1347422,"title":"","content":"I can see that; if the PCs started out fighting the most powerful combatant type in the world (Solars), they probably invested more and more in combat. I've noticed that the nature of the game pushes PCs in different directions; if you do a lot of combat they'll end up strong in combat and weak in socialising, and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> I play two Essence 5 games, and in one the players are <i>way</i> better at combat than the other (and built more optimally generally), because the game has just involved a lot more danger. But also, partly because they're each so individually powerful, they cooperate less. And they're more traumatised. So the conflict is frequently between the PCs, whereas the other game... well, people don't always agree, but when they don't they tend to ignore each other rather than go against each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T01:41:46-08:00","id":1347425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347321#post1347321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's maybe not quite THAT bad, but sometimes looking at the various antagonists makes it feel like there's a disconnect between what the writers of those antagonists expect the players to be able to do, and what they can do.<br /> <br /> There's just a bunch of enemies in the books, and supplements even, that have like, 6-7 dice to their attacks. Like the angler lizard, fog shark, hellboar, flickerfeather or pestletail. They're absolutely zero threat to the fighters, which is okay, but they're almost no threat at all to the people who aren't either. It only takes about 10% of your starting dots to get melee 3, pick up a sword, maybe a specialty and with the free Solar excellency you're just nearly immune to those attacks for less than your per-round mote regen.<br /> <br /> You might think &quot;Well 10% is kind of a lot.&quot; but I don't know if it is. If you're 90% social focused I'd say you're not a combat character, and I don't know how many non-combat focused characters I've seen with less than that, but not many. So in a group of PCs you have the weak social/mental characters who aren't threatened at all, and the big powerful combat characters who are even less than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean. Though it's less the charms (well, there is the excellency, and I find low-combat characters spam the excellency as it's all they've got to spend motes on) than the character creation system for Solars, I think. By which I mean how incredibly easy it is to get an enormous Parry at character creation, if you know what you're doing.<br /> <br /> This might be partly the old World of Darkness issue, where NPCs are written for players who don't know the system that well, and don't build very effective characters. I once ran a game for a whole group who'd never played Exalted before, and I was shocked by how low their Defences were compared to my normal players.<br /> <br /> Whereas the normal players, when they play Solars, basically always have a Defence of at least 5, which plus a stunt needs more dice to hit than most NPCs.<br /> <br /> One thing I've enjoyed about my Lunar game is that, due to the different character creation system (it looks similar, but the subtle changes make a big difference) the character's attack pools and Defences are much more reasonable. My 6 Lunar PCs have Defences of 6, 4, 4, 4, 3, 3, and not all of them started with defensive excellencies. Plus they can't raise it more than 1 or 2 without an appropriate stunt.<br /> Thus, things like bears can actually hit them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's worse is Hellboars have all these abilities; Bone-Crunching Bite, Death Stomp, trample, Femur-Smashing Crunch. War ghosts have that cool ethereal flicker blade...with their 7 die attack. There's all these cool things I want to use them for as an ST and it's just not really working. The worst are abilities that key off decisive attacks, because for <i>those </i>to ever have a chance of working the enemies have to build up initiative, and then keep it for a whole turn until they can act again to try and use it. </div> </div> </div>I think the thing with a lot of the animals is they're actually designed primarily with Lunars in mind. A Hellboar isn't actually designed to be a challenge to a combat-competent Solar, it's there to be a suit for a Lunar that gives the Lunar a bunch of abilities. And the Lunar can just use their own Strength or Dex + Brawl, plus excellencies.<br /> <br /> Some animals (Tyrant Lizard) are designed to be challenges for groups of Solars, and some are there because it's just useful stats, and don't have a load of special abilities (horse, wolf, etc). But mostly they're there for Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other side of that is a lot of solar powers that seem to have been written for fun, but got kind of out of control because there's nothing really to battle that needs them. Like Divine Executioner Stance or Aegis of Invincible Might. Or the sail system, where the excellency is all you need to win basically any fight, and then you've just got like 20 charms that make it progressively more overkill, completely pointlessly.<br /> <br /> Bulding off of how difficult it is to land a decisive attack with initiative for a lot of enemies, there's all these charms in medicine and resistance that give you more health levels, or let you heal those health levels faster, but they're such a waste if you never take health level damage. </div> </div> </div>Continuing the above point, I think the thing is that Solar games are expected to battle Abyssals, Sidereals, experienced Dragonblood, giant monsters, etc. Whereas what you've got in the Antagonists section is... well, mostly not. It does have some stuff there that's appropriate (Octavian, Ahlat, the Immaculate Monks) but a lot of things there (like the War Ghost you mentioned) are only really supposed to be fighting Solars as a battle group (and I actually found that Battle Groups of Elite Soldiers, especially with a Commander, really can be a big threat to Solars, they just go down quite quickly against multiple Solars).<br /> <br /> But the book doesn't really explain that half the charms in there are designed primarily for fighting stuff in other books (a lot of which isn't out yet, like Abyssal Sail which I guess is what high-essence Solar sail is for).<br /> <br /> Also, because the book doesn't have a ST section talking about this kind of thing, people go &quot;Hmmm, I want to be an amazing admiral, I'll take 10 sail charms&quot; and don't realise that 1 Sail charm plus the excellency is going to win them 95% of sailing encounters that aren't against Exalted admirals.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... maybe I didn't explain that well. I mean that it's not very clear to some, maybe, that taking 3 or 4 charms in an Ability means you are utterly amazing at it compared to most, and anything above that is really only for challenging the world's greatest heroes and biggest threats. Which I guess is because Exalted's power level is so much higher than most games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even want my PCs to succeed 90% of the time, I want them to win MORE than 90% of the time, like 99% of the time, as long as they're not being completely suicidal in the battles they pick. What I do want is for them to actually have to think for a second to win rather than me just pointlessly rolling 7 dice to try and hit their parry of 8 over and over, and for there to be some back and forth. Like maybe PC take a level of health damage and now they're wounded for a day or two, or get slammed through the floor only to pick themselves up, dust off and win anyway. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, exactly that. I got a bit frustrated with my Solar game because they just barged through most stuff utterly unworried about what anyone else thought of them, because they knew they could win basically every situation. So they became kind of bullies, tbh. (I don't just mean combat challenges, I mean other stuff as well, although the fact that they knew the local King had absolutely no way to oppose them in terms of soldiers did bleed into the non-combat stuff, as some of them tended to just intimidate everyone.)<br /> <br /> My Lunar PCs do it a bit as well, but they're not as bad, perhaps because of the characters or perhaps because they know they can't just succeed at everything without even trying. Or it may just be because they're lower essence. I've never played 3rd ed 0xp Solars, maybe this isn't such an issue.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't want them to actually fail. I just want them to have to put a little bit of effort and thought in rather than wandering into the throne room and saying &quot;I'm in charge now, what you going to do about it?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T01:43:00-08:00","id":1347426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347321#post1347321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's maybe not quite THAT bad, but sometimes looking at the various antagonists makes it feel like there's a disconnect between what the writers of those antagonists expect the players to be able to do, and what they can do.<br /> <br /> There's just a bunch of enemies in the books, and supplements even, that have like, 6-7 dice to their attacks. Like the angler lizard, fog shark, hellboar, flickerfeather or pestletail. They're absolutely zero threat to the fighters, which is okay, but they're almost no threat at all to the people who aren't either. It only takes about 10% of your starting dots to get melee 3, pick up a sword, maybe a specialty and with the free Solar excellency you're just nearly immune to those attacks for less than your per-round mote regen.<br /> <br /> You might think &quot;Well 10% is kind of a lot.&quot; but I don't know if it is. If you're 90% social focused I'd say you're not a combat character, and I don't know how many non-combat focused characters I've seen with less than that, but not many. So in a group of PCs you have the weak social/mental characters who aren't threatened at all, and the big powerful combat characters who are even less than that.<br /> <br /> What's worse is Hellboars have all these abilities; Bone-Crunching Bite, Death Stomp, trample, Femur-Smashing Crunch. War ghosts have that cool ethereal flicker blade...with their 7 die attack. There's all these cool things I want to use them for as an ST and it's just not really working. The worst are abilities that key off decisive attacks, because for <i>those </i>to ever have a chance of working the enemies have to build up initiative, and then keep it for a whole turn until they can act again to try and use it.<br /> <br /> It's not just attacks, the ambush predators like claw striders have 6 dice to their stealth rolls and stuff. If we're saying a troupe of gorillas going apeshit on the party should be beneath the concerns of the Exalted, then fine, just don't waste my time and your wordcount to get my hopes up that I might have an interesting action scene with them. Rather than me trying and just having maybe one ape get lucky and hit in the first round of combat, every other one getting crashed, and then dead or driven off in round 2.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't use any antagonist in the book, there's ones that are good. A big pack of claw striders ambushing the party at night with environmental penalties might force them to spend some motes, which might be relevant later on. Or you might have a first age ruin with an entire battlegroup of Walking Statues, and their automation commander. Even then, the party isn't in danger, they'll just be actually spending motes, which might matter for the next scene that they're in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The other side of that is a lot of solar powers that seem to have been written for fun, but got kind of out of control because there's nothing really to battle that needs them. Like Divine Executioner Stance or Aegis of Invincible Might. Or the sail system, where the excellency is all you need to win basically any fight, and then you've just got like 20 charms that make it progressively more overkill, completely pointlessly.<br /> <br /> Bulding off of how difficult it is to land a decisive attack with initiative for a lot of enemies, there's all these charms in medicine and resistance that give you more health levels, or let you heal those health levels faster, but they're such a waste if you never take health level damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't even want my PCs to succeed 90% of the time, I want them to win MORE than 90% of the time, like 99% of the time, as long as they're not being completely suicidal in the battles they pick. What I do want is for them to actually have to think for a second to win rather than me just pointlessly rolling 7 dice to try and hit their parry of 8 over and over, and for there to be some back and forth. Like maybe PC take a level of health damage and now they're wounded for a day or two, or get slammed through the floor only to pick themselves up, dust off and win anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is what I'm complaining about.<br /> <br /> You are playing Exalted. Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're saying a troupe of gorillas going apeshit on the party should be beneath the concerns of the Exalted&quot;?<br /> <br /> No. We're saying an army of a thousand barbarians who've drilled for war since birth, equipped with the finest weapons and armor in Creation, mounted on the backs of Tyrant Lizards are beneath the concerns of the Exalted. (At character creation, this is obviously hyperbole. For an Essence 5 Solar Circle, I'm being literal and sincere.)<br /> <br /> Look at the difficulty chart on page 185. The Exalted rule.<br /> <br /> You're playing the people who cast down the gods of the gods. Not Robert Baratheon. Pigs should not be a meaningful threat to you.<br /> <br /> The point of most antagonists is how dangerous they are to mortals and to each other. Not how trivial they are to the PCs. Which is why the Might abstraction exists -- there's a world of difference between a war ghost and a blood ape, but to the PCs? Not so much.<br /> <br /> I realize my references are dated, but the PCs are Marcus Hamiliton and the Antagonists are Illyria. They might have interesting abilities but really, they're just not that cool.<br /> <br /> Antagonists are set pieces used to either show how amazing the PCs are, or to force some kind of concequence (like spent motes). They're quick characters used to gague your abilities by (PS: you are awesome).<br /> <br /> Now if an Abyssal puts you in your -4s, then his pack of ghostly followers becomes a threat as you try to escape. Burning motes to detect ambushing claw striders leaves you down for when their Lunar mistress attacks. Hellboars suck... untill you're facing a magically enhanced familiar.<br /> <br /> If every random person who died could challenge a Solar, death would be one heck of an upgrade and the Primordials wouldn't have stood a chance in the War. If a gorrilla could match a god of war... that'd be a pretty pathetic god. <br /> <br /> You might be able to handily beat a Bride... wanna go totemic in front of the Satrap's guards? Yes you saved the village from zombies. This time. What happens next time the dead rise? How do the villagers feel about their new hero? What do they expect from you? Are you spending motes in a Shadowland before you adventure into the Underworld proper? What are the concequences of your actions?<br /> <br /> The word count argument I get. NPCs might have been better off getting the same treatment as Weapons and Armor -- Weak, Competent, Elite with one QC stat block (just like in 1E) and Tags to differentiate a tiger from a battle-ready soldier.<br /> <br /> A troupe of gorrillas, in and of themselves, is a trivial challenge the PCs shouldn't have to spend a thought on. They should be scattered and cast down by round two. I don't want a two hour fight against some flea bitten vermin. Scratch off the Excellency motes and throw the next challenge at me. On session ten when I fight Harambe The Gorrilla God and his endless army of the Souls of Righteous Gorrillas Past <i>then</i> I can be challenged, thrown to the ground, forced to use Aegis, maybe take some health levels, maybe the Eclipse takes a Critical (and the Twilight gets something to heal). But a level of damage on a trivial random encounter? No way! Being wounded is definitely a concequence of one of the 1-in-10 fights, it shouldn't be a bread-and-butter thing. How often is Superman wounded? How often is The Terminator wounded? If you really want to knock the PCs prone, have all the NPCs gang up on the weak one and use a grapple gambit. But frankly, I don't see why you'd want to.<br /> <br /> Use the Skip It rules on 212. 7 dice can't hit Parry 8 (not enough to win), so Skip It. System working as intended.<br /> <br /> At the beginning of Castlevania 64, lightning hits a tree which becomes the first obstacle you face in the game. You're supposed to trivially overcome this obstacle by pressing the jump button once -- it's about setting the scene and raising the drama, not dealing damage to you. Likewise the wild gorrillas at the foot of an ancient and foreboding temple should be narrated as an interesting and significant thing... but it shouldn't be a head scratcher, the Exalted should deal with them in one, maybe two, rolls. Narrate the drama. Tell a good story. But mechanically, it's two stunts maximum -- that troupe should be a single Size 1 Poor Drill battlegroup unless you've got a very compelling reason to want to drag this out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347425#post1347425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, exactly that. I got a bit frustrated with my Solar game because they just barged through most stuff utterly unworried about what anyone else thought of them, because they knew they could win basically every situation. So they became kind of bullies, tbh. (I don't just mean combat challenges, I mean other stuff as well, although the fact that they knew the local King had absolutely no way to oppose them in terms of soldiers did bleed into the non-combat stuff, as some of them tended to just intimidate everyone.)<br /> <br /> Again, I don't want them to actually fail. I just want them to have to put a little bit of effort and thought in rather than wandering into the throne room and saying &quot;I'm in charge now, what you going to do about it?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you've posted apart from this.<br /> <br /> I want trivial threats to be trivial, and the story to be about whether the Solars stay good people or become bullies. That's the point. I explicitly, expressly, absolutely want Solars to be able to steamroller mortal kingdoms and slap down a &quot;what are you going to do about it&quot; because this is the <i>central theme</i> on which Exalted is based. That you can do this is the point of the game. And as I can do it, I'd rather do it in one roll than spend an entire four hour session slogging it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1st Edition Corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is a cinematic game [...] most combats aren't gritty, life-or-death struggles for the hero, where every sword blow may be the last. That sort of tension is reserved for the real fights, when the protagonist faces off against the real villains [...] The average enemy the hero faces is a nameless, expendable bad guy. These opponents' purpose in combat is to get beaten up or killed in order to provide a visual spectacle, complicate the narrative and demonstrate how badass the protagonist is. [...] Storytellers shouldn't be surprised when the PCs battle through hordes of [NPCs] without serious injury. The rules are set up to make it happen that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 11-10-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T09:07:09-08:00","id":1347482,"title":"","content":"I wholly agree, John.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:02:33-08:00","id":1347492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347426#post1347426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this is what I'm complaining about.<br /> <br /> You are playing Exalted. Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're saying a troupe of gorillas going apeshit on the party should be beneath the concerns of the Exalted&quot;?<br /> <br /> No. We're saying an army of a thousand barbarians who've drilled for war since birth, equipped with the finest weapons and armor in Creation, mounted on the backs of Tyrant Lizards are beneath the concerns of the Exalted. (At character creation, this is obviously hyperbole. For an Essence 5 Solar Circle, I'm being literal and sincere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of agree here, though &quot;beneath the concerns of the Exalted&quot; kind of sounds like it's utterly irrelevant. When our Dawn was attacked by his own Tiger Warriors riding flying, fire-breathing giant lizards with almost the stats of Tyrant Lizards, it was a concern. Obviously he beat them, but he did have to spend some motes. And then there was the political fallout, morale effect on his infantry when they'd been attacked by their own allies, etc.<br /> <br /> If your point is that an army of barbarians on Tyrant Lizards isn't a serious threat to a circle of Essence 5 Solars, I agree (unless, of course, they're all non-combat focused).<br /> <br /> It's just that I think, when people start saying like anything mortal is &quot;trivial&quot; or &quot;beneath their concern&quot; it's not really good for the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pigs should not be a meaningful threat to you. </div> </div> </div>Definitely. And I think that's why I agree with DrLoveMonkey about how the rules for Solars and Antagonist sections are like for different games; but I don't think the answer is that hellboars and gorillas should be more of a threat, I think that they're just not important for Solar games. That's why 2nd ed gave most animals a very, very small section.<br /> Anything smaller than a dinosaur* isn't generally important unless it's actually a Lunar or its a familiar you're going to buff.<br /> <br /> *Except horses, which are important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why the Might abstraction exists -- there's a world of difference between a war ghost and a blood ape, but to the PCs? Not so much. </div> </div> </div>I agree with you there: I'm never going to run a PC vs a War Ghost as a proper combat, they're only going to be fighting 30 War Ghosts. But I can see DrLoveMonkey's point about how frustrating it is that they have these cool abilities that they basically aren't going to use (as Battle Groups just use Might, not offensive/defensive charms).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The word count argument I get. NPCs might have been better off getting the same treatment as Weapons and Armor -- Weak, Competent, Elite with one QC stat block (just like in 1E) </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea.<br /> The only thing in the Antagonists section that doesn't have Essence 2+ that I've actually found useful is mortal soldiers, which work that way, as they come in three levels; Militia, Battle-Ready Soldiers, and Elite Soldiers.<br /> I use them for all kinds of encounters, even for things that aren't mortal soldiers (for example, when Ahlat ambushed the PCs backed up by 100 minor War-Gods, they were Elite Soldiers with Elite Drill and Might).<br /> I wouldn't be that bothered if wolves, gorillas, war golems, etc, were based off these stats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and Tags to differentiate a tiger from a battle-ready soldier. </div> </div> </div>That'd work well for Lunars as well actually.<br /> <br /> I mean, the shapeshifting rules actually do work well for Lunars... once the players have worked out all the numbers, which I've found most find very tricky. I ended up just writing out the actual used stats and excellency caps for some of my players' main animal forms. (It's the excellency caps that mainly confuse them, though there are other bits. And obviously when you've got 10 forms that doesn't make it easier.)<br /> <br /> The exception for this trickiness is low-level animals, which effectively end up being a couple of merits and special attacks because your own stats are better. For example, if my Lunar takes her totem form, she basically gets Tiny, Camouflage, and a poison bite, but she's still using all her own stats (which is way less confusing than when other players turn into gorillas or bears or whatever).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use the Skip It rules on 212. 7 dice can't hit Parry 8 (not enough to win), so Skip It. System working as intended. </div> </div> </div>I use this all the time and strongly encourage others to do so. My STs have started using it too, which has worked well.<br /> <br /> Last session, for example, I turned into a bear on top of a thatched house, and fell through the roof on top of the leader of the extremists trying to purge the moderate members of our revolution. Then of course his goons opened up on me with their AK-47s. But a Full Moon vs 3 monkeys with assault rifles is going to just involve a lot of rolling and then I'll win anyway, so he just had me roll once.<br /> <br /> And that's how I run 60% of the fights in the game, because they're just set-piece fights.<br /> <br /> But, again, I can see DrLoveMonkey's frustration that 70% of the stuff in the Core Book's antagonist section has a bunch of cool moves and abilities and rules that, if you run a Solar game well, are hardly ever going to come up, because they're there to challenge mortals or be a Lunar-suit.<br /> And I can also see why it might get new STs to go &quot;oh, presumably all these animals are there because a circle of Solars vs 5 wolves is a challenging encounter&quot; which it is not supposed to be. Whereas if you actually want to give your Solar circle a difficult challenge you need to use Octavian, Ahlat, or stuff that's in completely different books (most of which still aren't out).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with everything you've posted apart from this.<br /> <br /> I want trivial threats to be trivial, and the story to be about whether the Solars stay good people or become bullies. That's the point. I explicitly, expressly, absolutely want Solars to be able to steamroller mortal kingdoms and slap down a &quot;what are you going to do about it&quot; because this is the <i>central theme</i> on which Exalted is based. That you can do this is the point of the game. And as I can do it, I'd rather do it in one roll than spend an entire four hour session slogging it out. </div> </div> </div>I guess this is a slightly different point from some of my others.<br /> <br /> So, at Essence 1, I think taking over a petty mortal kingdom should take a few sessions (and probably won't be very difficult).<br /> <br /> At Essence 5, taking over a mortal kingdom... yeah, sure, steamroll it, its just on the way to your big fight with the circle of Abyssals or Dragonblood or whatever, which is the actual plot.<br /> I just found that I, personally, did not enjoy watching them steamroll mortal kingdoms. It's all very well saying &quot;will they become righteous kings or bullies? What will they do with their power? Isn't this an interesting thing to explore?&quot; but then they become bullies, and I didn't enjoy it that much (not to say I hated the game, there were plenty of bits I did enjoy, just not that).<br /> What they could have been doing at Essence 5, that I'd have enjoyed more I think, is invading the Realm or casting down Deathlords or battling a circle of Infernals, but at the time none of that was really available.<br /> Now that Dragonblood is actually available, my friend who's taken over the game is able to run the PCs battling a massive Realm invasion (also the Realm is allied with Ahlat who's leading a conspiracy of Gods who want to conquer the South, and have their own circle of Exigents), but I couldn't really do that because there weren't really rules for making loads of Dragonblood including high-essence ones.<br /> <br /> Also, tbh, our previous 2nd ed game (which went from 0xp to 500xp) ended up with massive world-shaping events, and I think people wanted to do a smaller, more pulp-focused game, rather than stopping another Deathlord destroying the world. But that wasn't suitable for Essence 4 characters, honestly. Rather than starting a 3rd ed game with their old characters in the same area 25 years later, I should have just started an entirely new game in that area 25 years later, with 0xp characters. It would have worked better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as I can do it, I'd rather do it in one roll than spend an entire four hour session slogging it out. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I don't think I'd want to do it one roll, there should be a few more scenes to showcase local politics (so people can get use out of all their socialise or bureaucracy charms, for one thing), and opportunities for PCs to consider issues and ethics, but I on't really want to spend ages doing it.<br /> The problem was sometimes I let a player take over stuff with just a few rolls in downtime rather than running 3 games of that one PC running around putting out various issues (easily), and then other players complained I'd made it too easy for that player and I should have run properly all the different social problems that PC would face. Which would have taken ages while the other players would be sat around doing nothing, and no-one would really have enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so this point and the above one are partly about the game, but partly about me and my players. I just don't enjoy &quot;Essence 5 Solars interact with mortal kingdoms&quot; the way it's supposed to work (at least, more than once or twice; there were bits I enjoyed of them seizing control of puppet kingdoms, it just got old), and I'd really rather run &quot;Essence 1 Solars interact with mortal kingdoms&quot; or &quot;Essence 5 Solars take on the (Elder?) Gods themselves&quot;.<br /> I'm not saying &quot;Essence 5 Solars take on mortal kingdoms&quot; should be hard, I'm just saying it's not the game for me.<br /> <br /> I was quite happy with my Essence 1-2 Lunars (sort of) saving a mortal kingdom from conspirators, saving it (sort of) from Raksha, and then using their influence to decide which mortal became the new Queen. And I'm quite happy that they're now going to tackle the Elemental Dragon of Air.<br /> It's just the first one I wouldn't have enjoyed if they'd been Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2019, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:44:35-08:00","id":1347503,"title":"","content":"Couple comments:<br /> <br /> 1) Eh, invoking 1e's &quot;Mooks&quot; section is kind of a double edged thing, because 1e was trying to specifically sell its audience on an action movie trope (Disposable Ninja #325, etc), and 1e was often pretty specific on who should *never* be treated as a &quot;Mook&quot; (to mixed reaction, e.g. Dragonblooded). People may disagree about who should be a &quot;Mook&quot; even if they agree there should be some.<br /> <br /> 2) It's kind of a weird thing about Exalted now that I think about it that there has never really been a &quot;high level&quot; adventure book in all it's years. 90% of material (Caste Books, 1e's Direction books) is focused on fairly low Essence games. <br /> <br /> Quite proper as I think as a priority as this is probably where the main interesting inspirations of Exalted lie - &quot;Walk The Earth!&quot; / Vanilla Exalted Sword &amp; Sorcery / pulp adventuring (Ninja Scroll, Rurouni Kenshin, Conan, Elric, and whatnot), where Solar characters are uniquely powerful enough to be destabilizing to the power structure without backing and able to be champions or leaders to oppressed mortals, and be the nail that stands up but is not beaten down, but not really strong enough to easily dispense of local powers like The Perfect or the Linowan or the Lintha Family or the Forest Witches and the like. That's where the heart and soul of the vision of game really is.<br /> <br /> But it does create a problem that there really isn't too much there for when experience accumulation pushes characters higher than this! This doesn't seem by design!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:47:25-08:00","id":1347504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347426#post1347426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;We're saying a troupe of gorillas going apeshit on the party should be beneath the concerns of the Exalted&quot;?<br /> <br /> No. We're saying an army of a thousand barbarians who've drilled for war since birth, equipped with the finest weapons and armor in Creation, mounted on the backs of Tyrant Lizards are beneath the concerns of the Exalted. (At character creation, this is obviously hyperbole. For an Essence 5 Solar Circle, I'm being literal and sincere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think before we continue the discussion we need to pin down exactly what we mean by trivial here. When I say I want my players to battle a troupe of gorillas, I don't mean then when an angry forest god incites a furious anger in a group of nearby apes, who then decide to express that anger by trying to beat the PCs to a pulp, I don't want them to look sorrowfully at their character sheet and say &quot;But...I really like my character, I don't want her to die...maybe we should just run?&quot; I don't want a group of gorillas have any real chance at all, and I mean like 1 in 10,000 of winning that fight, if even that high.<br /> <br /> Even DnD is like that. Last session I ran the level 5 party ran in to a group of a dozen goblins, the wizard was pissed at them because her last encounter with them was so annoying that she snapped her fingers and incinerated them all in a fireball in round 1, rolling enough damage that even passing their saving throw dealt more than their total HP. In fact, I think, in the past two or three years of playing DnD 1-2 times a week I can only remember one battle that the PCs ever actually lost? They rarely felt <i>trivial </i>though, even if victory was completely assured somebody got hit at some point, I got to use some of the monsters cool abilities.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, I know, it's selfish, but the ST is a player too, and the antagonists are the storyteller's characters that they get to have fun with. I like when my players annihilate, absolutely destroy, a group of enemies, but I like it even more when at some point in the fight the lithe chain fighter sweeps out the barbarian's legs and he tumbles to the ground, and then right after he goes Hulk to her Loki.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347426#post1347426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want trivial threats to be trivial, and the story to be about whether the Solars stay good people or become bullies. That's the point. I explicitly, expressly, absolutely want Solars to be able to steamroller mortal kingdoms and slap down a &quot;what are you going to do about it&quot; because this is the <i>central theme</i> on which Exalted is based. That you can do this is the point of the game. And as I can do it, I'd rather do it in one roll than spend an entire four hour session slogging it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the two things are mutually exclusive. Going back to DnD again, I've had parties of all levels spend entire sessions doing nothing but debating the various courses of action and weighing what the consequences and the costs of each. What parts of themselves are they willing to give up to achieve their goals? In fact, I think it was made even better by the idea that at least some of those consequences were not easily solved.<br /> <br /> In Exalted it can often feel like Gamora asking Thanos &quot;What did it cost?&quot; and he just shrugs and says &quot;Nothing.&quot; If you want to talk about consequences, the consequences actually have to matter or else it's totally uninteresting.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're making a game where anything less than a third circle demon is not worth busting out the dice for, then I can get into that, probably not for very long campaigns but I can for a bit. Just don't write this absolutely enormous setting, detailing all the places that don't matter, and giving stats for things that never come into play. Pigs shouldn't be a threat, agreed, so don't write a huge setting book detailing all the different kinds of pig farms, filled with different kinds of pigs that have different stats which are all too low to matter, and full of interesting pig-based abilities that sound really cool and fun for me, and don't matter a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T10:49:25-08:00","id":1347505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347503#post1347503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple comments:<br /> <br /> 1) Eh, invoking 1e's &quot;Mooks&quot; section is kind of a double edged thing, because 1e was trying to specifically sell its audience on an action movie trope (Disposable Ninja #325, etc), and 1e was often pretty specific on who should *never* be treated as a &quot;Mook&quot; (to mixed reaction, e.g. Dragonblooded). People may disagree about who should be a &quot;Mook&quot; even if they agree there should be some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone play 4th edition DnD? The Minion system I think always worked better than most of the &quot;mook&quot; rules for Exalted.<br /> Minions had very competitive defences and attacks, but had 1hp and did a few points of damage. It wasn't a matter of rolling again and again and achieving nothing, but also they died like chumps and just wore you down a bit, rather than actually killing you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) It's kind of a weird thing about Exalted now that I think about it that there has never really been a &quot;high level&quot; adventure book in all it's years. 90% of material (Caste Books, 1e's Direction books) is focused on fairly low Essence games. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Glories of the Most High probably doesn't count. Return of the Scarlet Empress maybe?<br /> <br /> And there was the Deathlords, but they were so insanely powerful (often with nearly every single Solar/Abyssal charm, and Sidereal Martial Arts) that they didn't even fit well for Essence 5 games, plus even if you did beat them (which I've seen, partly because the ST found it difficult to remember the entire charmset in the middle of combat) they possibly have plot-immunity and just come back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it does create a problem that there really isn't too much there for when experience accumulation pushes characters higher than this! This doesn't seem by design! </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think is the main problem I found, and probably why I'm finding an Essence 2 game way easier to run than an Essence 5 game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2019, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T11:02:53-08:00","id":1347513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347504#post1347504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think before we continue the discussion we need to pin down exactly what we mean by trivial here. When I say I want my players to battle a troupe of gorillas, I don't mean then when an angry forest god incites a furious anger in a group of nearby apes, who then decide to express that anger by trying to beat the PCs to a pulp, I don't want them to look sorrowfully at their character sheet and say &quot;But...I really like my character, I don't want her to die...maybe we should just run?&quot; I don't want a group of gorillas have any real chance at all, and I mean like 1 in 10,000 of winning that fight, if even that high.<br /> <br /> Even DnD is like that. Last session I ran the level 5 party ran in to a group of a dozen goblins, the wizard was pissed at them because her last encounter with them was so annoying that she snapped her fingers and incinerated them all in a fireball in round 1, rolling enough damage that even passing their saving throw dealt more than their total HP. In fact, I think, in the past two or three years of playing DnD 1-2 times a week I can only remember one battle that the PCs ever actually lost? They rarely felt <i>trivial </i>though, even if victory was completely assured somebody got hit at some point, I got to use some of the monsters cool abilities.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, I know, it's selfish, but the ST is a player too, and the antagonists are the storyteller's characters that they get to have fun with. I like when my players annihilate, absolutely destroy, a group of enemies, but I like it even more when at some point in the fight the lithe chain fighter sweeps out the barbarian's legs and he tumbles to the ground, and then right after he goes Hulk to her Loki.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think that the two things are mutually exclusive. Going back to DnD again, I've had parties of all levels spend entire sessions doing nothing but debating the various courses of action and weighing what the consequences and the costs of each. What parts of themselves are they willing to give up to achieve their goals? In fact, I think it was made even better by the idea that at least some of those consequences were not easily solved.<br /> <br /> In Exalted it can often feel like Gamora asking Thanos &quot;What did it cost?&quot; and he just shrugs and says &quot;Nothing.&quot; If you want to talk about consequences, the consequences actually have to matter or else it's totally uninteresting.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're making a game where anything less than a third circle demon is not worth busting out the dice for, then I can get into that, probably not for very long campaigns but I can for a bit. Just don't write this absolutely enormous setting, detailing all the places that don't matter, and giving stats for things that never come into play. Pigs shouldn't be a threat, agreed, so don't write a huge setting book detailing all the different kinds of pig farms, filled with different kinds of pigs that have different stats which are all too low to matter, and full of interesting pig-based abilities that sound really cool and fun for me, and don't matter a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you underlined one of my main complaint about the game : The ST is a player too, and he doesn't want to spend 5 hours of preparation, reading, and conception of a scenario or a setting for nothing. Your second and 3rd paragraph in particular really resonate with me, because lots of the time I think I had a lot of cool ideas with my scenario and setting but when the time came for them to go into action mechanically they did not deliver accordingly mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T11:38:46-08:00","id":1347521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347321#post1347321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's maybe not quite THAT bad, but sometimes looking at the various antagonists makes it feel like there's a disconnect between what the writers of those antagonists expect the players to be able to do, and what they can do.<br /> <br /> There's just a bunch of enemies in the books, and supplements even, that have like, 6-7 dice to their attacks. [snip] They're absolutely zero threat to the fighters, which is okay, but they're almost no threat at all to the people who aren't either. It only takes about 10% of your starting dots to get melee 3, pick up a sword, maybe a specialty and with the free Solar excellency you're just nearly immune to those attacks for less than your per-round mote regen.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do agree with you that the creatures in the book, presented as antagonists, should be a challenge to at least <i>some</i> Solars, I think you're kind of exaggerating the problem here. First, I think the lower dice pools you're talking about for the antagonists are the exception, rather than the rule - going through the animals in the Antagonists chapter, there are 25, of which 17 (68%) have dice pools of 8 or more. If you discount the animals that are obviously intended to be there as color or as stats for a familiar or mount or something (which I'd include the cat, horse, and raiton in), the percentage climbs even higher. And most of the weaker animals can get an immediate boost if you put them in a battlegroup - you only need 2 hellboars on the battlefield to immediately give them +1 to their dice pool, and let them attack twice a round, after all.<br /> <br /> Second, I think you're kind of overestimating the effects of a small dip into combat for the PCs, too. Someone with Dex 3 and Melee 3, with a specialty in defense and a medium weapon, has a parry of 5, which can be boosted by 2 for 4 motes. A parry of 7 is good, for sure, but there's lots of antagonists who can roll better than that. You might need a 14-die pool to have a 50% chance of overcoming it, but the pool system in Exalted is pretty swingy, what with double-10s and such. I don't know the stats offhand, but it wouldn't <i>shock</i> me to learn that something like a 10-die pool had only a little less than 50% chance of beating Parry 7. And penalties to defense are pretty common and generally easy to apply. Overwhelming is the obvious one, of course, but there's plenty of others for taking various actions (both flurrying and taking any miscellaneous action both reduce Defense by 1, for example), and I feel it's reasonable to apply defense penalties for things like fighting on rough terrain or in poor conditions like pouring rain or heavy fog. All of those will bring that non-specialist's Parry back into the range where they're pretty easy to hit even for the lower-pool creatures. <br /> <br /> <br /> All that said, I do definitely agree with you that it should be possible to challenge a Circle of Solars with non-Exalted antagonists, and that this is desirable. Battling great beasts, for instance, has a lot of narrative resonance in the sources that Exalted draws on - half of Herakles' labors, for example, involved him dealing with things that were basically big animals, with few obvious supernatural powers beyond size. And the pulp tradition has plenty of such fights being portrayed as impressive feats too - Conan fighting a great ape barehanded, for instance. And 2e really swung the needle far too far in the other direction, making the vast majority of mortal opponents absolutely trivial, and essentially endorsing the &quot;you must be this magical to ride&quot; attitude. Personally, one of the reasons I liked 3e to begin with was the promise that fighting mortal antagonists would be <i>meaningful</i>. <br /> <br /> So, with that in mind, here's some tricks I've found to be useful when designing fights between a Solar circle and non-Exalted/powerful spirit opponents:<ul><li>Don't be afraid to add dice! The QCs in the book represent typical examples, but it's perfectly reasonable, especially with the animals and other QCs where there's only one example, to have tougher creatures. I think adding up to 4 dice to attack, combat movement, and other relevant skills like stealth, is justifiable by assuming this particular specimen is just a bit more skilled, smarter, or just plain meaner. Another 4-6 dice can be justified by outright magic like mutations or other supernatural buffs.</li> <li>Also don't be afraid to spend willpower! Spending a point gives an automatic success on a roll or boosts a static value by 1, both of which can make a big difference.</li> <li>When fighting a whole Circle, use multiple opponents, and by multiple opponents, I mean multiple <i>targets</i>. The action economy means that if there's only a single target on the battlefield, even if that is a battlegroup representing 10 actual opponents, that the Circle will tend to overwhelm it with attacks, and it won't get to do anything interesting before going down. My rule of thumb is that for every combat-focused character in the Circle there should be one serious opponent, and one more opponent for the rest of the Circle, ideally one capable of being a danger to all of them, like a battlegroup or something capable of area-effect attacks. For example, my own group currently has a Dawn Caste who's heavily Melee-focused, a Night with excellent Archery, and an Alchemical who's currently got a charm loadout that makes him a grapple-monster, while the Twilight and Eclipse aren't really combat-heavy at all. Against them, I'd usually throw 4 distinct targets.</li> <li>Use battlegroups heavily. If you've got two characters who are basically identical on the battlefield, they should always be in a battlegroup. It saves you time and energy as an ST, and the bonuses battlegroups get are nice.</li> <li>To combine the above point and the first one, a good combat challenge is often a battlegroup of &quot;typical&quot; creatures from the Antagonists chapter, and one or two bigger, tougher specimens, the &quot;alphas&quot; of the group. A sounder of three average hellboars, for instance, lead by a bigger, meaner old sow with +4 to her attack, can be a serious threat even to someone who's dipped into a combat ability.</li> <li>Also be willing to apply penalties fairly liberally. Lots of Solar charms let you ignore penalties, but that's only helpful if those penalties are imposed in the first place. To avoid people feeling like they've &quot;wasted&quot; charms, the ST has got to be using them in the first place.</li> </ul><br /> There are a few more things I'd suggest to make mortal antagonists a bit more of a serious threat, but they veer into house rules territory, so I'll discuss them over in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1338477-exalted-3e-homebrew-combat-mechanics\">the thread for that</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T11:44:53-08:00","id":1347523,"title":"","content":"Wizard, I basically agree with you. I enjoy STing for Bad Guys (I think Evil is Fun and Redemption Arcs are awesome), but apart from that, I don't have anything else constructive to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347504#post1347504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think before we continue the discussion we need to pin down exactly what we mean by trivial here. When I say I want my players to battle a troupe of gorillas, I don't mean then when an angry forest god incites a furious anger in a group of nearby apes, who then decide to express that anger by trying to beat the PCs to a pulp, I don't want them to look sorrowfully at their character sheet and say &quot;But...I really like my character, I don't want her to die...maybe we should just run?&quot; I don't want a group of gorillas have any real chance at all, and I mean like 1 in 10,000 of winning that fight, if even that high.<br /> <br /> Even DnD is like that. Last session I ran the level 5 party ran in to a group of a dozen goblins, the wizard was pissed at them because her last encounter with them was so annoying that she snapped her fingers and incinerated them all in a fireball in round 1, rolling enough damage that even passing their saving throw dealt more than their total HP. In fact, I think, in the past two or three years of playing DnD 1-2 times a week I can only remember one battle that the PCs ever actually lost? They rarely felt <i>trivial </i>though, even if victory was completely assured somebody got hit at some point, I got to use some of the monsters cool abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble parsing this one. You got to use cool abilities of monsters incinerated in a single fireball?<br /> <br /> The general principle of wearing down spell slots more-or-less applies to Exalted. A kobold isn't going to challenge a level 15 Wizard. Exalted start play at level 15.<br /> <br /> I'm defining trivial as winning with one or two rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, yes, I know, it's selfish, but the ST is a player too, and the antagonists are the storyteller's characters that they get to have fun with. I like when my players annihilate, absolutely destroy, a group of enemies, but I like it even more when at some point in the fight the lithe chain fighter sweeps out the barbarian's legs and he tumbles to the ground, and then right after he goes Hulk to her Loki.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the two things are mutually exclusive. Going back to DnD again, I've had parties of all levels spend entire sessions doing nothing but debating the various courses of action and weighing what the consequences and the costs of each. What parts of themselves are they willing to give up to achieve their goals? In fact, I think it was made even better by the idea that at least some of those consequences were not easily solved.<br /> <br /> In Exalted it can often feel like Gamora asking Thanos &quot;What did it cost?&quot; and he just shrugs and says &quot;Nothing.&quot; If you want to talk about consequences, the consequences actually have to matter or else it's totally uninteresting. </div> </div> </div>Whilst the PCs have motes, I feel like you're wearing down the wrong resources. Thanos didn't give up his highest level spell slot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand if you're making a game where anything less than a third circle demon is not worth busting out the dice for, then I can get into that, probably not for very long campaigns but I can for a bit. Just don't write this absolutely enormous setting, detailing all the places that don't matter, and giving stats for things that never come into play. Pigs shouldn't be a threat, agreed, so don't write a huge setting book detailing all the different kinds of pig farms, filled with different kinds of pigs that have different stats which are all too low to matter, and full of interesting pig-based abilities that sound really cool and fun for me, and don't matter a bit. </div> </div> </div>Perform a Working on that pig and make them a Solar's familiar and see if they matter. Throw a mortal against the pig and see if it matters.<br /> <br /> Jeeze, I feel disingenuous defending the terribad NPC design choices in the Corebook, but I do at least see the rationale. (I mean, I agree 100% with you, but I see what Holden &amp; Morke were shooting for -- you need an entry level if you're going to have room to grow.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T11:55:04-08:00","id":1347526,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is the thing, I think probably the Core Book antagonist section was fine for Essence 1 characters (from the sound of it, Kelly's found the animals in there useful, though maybe DrLoveMonkey's experience is different). It just isn't much good for a high-experience campaign.<br /> <br /> Which leads back to the Adversaries and Hundred Devils Night Parade books, which have loads of cool creatures... for low-level games. And only a bit for high-level games, which I really think is the area that needs to be expended on.<br /> I'd say the only things useful for high-level games are Makarios and the giant lava-behemoth (though I haven't seen that in action, it might get blown apart by Death Ray, not sure). I've got a hard drive full of cool pdfs I've literally never used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I enjoy STing for Bad Guys </div> </div> </div>I did sometimes. Not all the time. It might have helped if they were more consistent on whether they were bad guys or not. In some ways the most amusing character is the most overtly evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2019, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T12:04:27-08:00","id":1347528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347503#post1347503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple comments:<br /> <br /> 1) Eh, invoking 1e's &amp;quot;Mooks&amp;quot; section is kind of a double edged thing, because 1e was trying to specifically sell its audience on an action movie trope (Disposable Ninja #325, etc), and 1e was often pretty specific on who should *never* be treated as a &amp;quot;Mook&amp;quot; (to mixed reaction, e.g. Dragonblooded). People may disagree about who should be a &amp;quot;Mook&amp;quot; even if they agree there should be some.<br /> <br /> 2) It's kind of a weird thing about Exalted now that I think about it that there has never really been a &amp;quot;high level&amp;quot; adventure book in all it's years. 90% of material (Caste Books, 1e's Direction books) is focused on fairly low Essence games. <br /> <br /> Quite proper as I think as a priority as this is probably where the main interesting inspirations of Exalted lie - &amp;quot;Walk The Earth!&amp;quot; / Vanilla Exalted Sword &amp; Sorcery / pulp adventuring (Ninja Scroll, Rurouni Kenshin, Conan, Elric, and whatnot), where Solar characters are uniquely powerful enough to be destabilizing to the power structure without backing and able to be champions or leaders to oppressed mortals, and be the nail that stands up but is not beaten down, but not really strong enough to easily dispense of local powers like The Perfect or the Linowan or the Lintha Family or the Forest Witches and the like. That's where the heart and soul of the vision of game really is.<br /> <br /> But it does create a problem that there really isn't too much there for when experience accumulation pushes characters higher than this! This doesn't seem by design!</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I agree with 1E<br /> <br /> 2. What about the 2E Celestial Direction books? Malfeas and Yu Shen were excellent settings with appropriate NPC enemies. (Underworld was a bit swingier.)<br /> <br /> I realise Holden and Morke wanted to shift the focus back to Creation... but the Corebook speaks for itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T13:25:13-08:00","id":1347544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347521#post1347521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with that in mind, here's some tricks I've found to be useful when designing fights between a Solar circle and non-Exalted/powerful spirit opponents:</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these ideas. It also definitely isn't the whole corebook, like claw striders for example in a pack have 8-12 dice on their attack roll with 3 autosuccesses and can pay willpower to add damage to their raw decisive attack. If you've got 4 PCs and 7 claw striders ambushing them there's likely to be at least somebody who gets hit with a swipe at some point. You've also got some like the Benthic Knifetooth, that seem like they kind of suck, but then you read their merits and when they're actually dangerous is stealth attacking swimmers from deep under water, getting 3 autosuccesses to that roll as well.<br /> <br /> They're not totally useless, but there's way too many for my taste that aren't great. It's not even just animals either, buck-ogres, ghostfishers, manticores, bonesiders there's a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347523#post1347523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble parsing this one. You got to use cool abilities of monsters incinerated in a single fireball?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that was a case where the fight was over in one round because a PC grabbed the throttle and punched it, because that's the kind of thing wizards do. They hold out their hand, speak arcane words, and a dozen foes, along with anything flammable in the room, become ash. It's not a cantrip though, there was an actual choice to be made about using that ability.<br /> <br /> However, the fight, I think 3-4 fights before that, was one against 20 stirges. Now, stirges are CR1/8 creatures with 2hp, they're not mega deadly beasts. Unfortunately when that encounter happened the wizard was just flat out of fireballs, and indeed any AoE spells. So what ensued was an actual scene where the stirges used their special blood drain ability to puncture the PCs and drill their beaks into their flesh. Then there were some cool parts like when the paladin dropped his shield so he could dual wield and slice half a dozen of the little mosquito bats off the cleric, the warlock activated Armor of Agathys and ran through a big section of the flock, freezing solid any of them who dared touch him, our dragonborn maneuvered into the perfect position to just fry another big swath of them out of the air.<br /> <br /> Then afterwards the party did a thorough check to make sure they didn't miss anything, blocked the door and spent a bit of time pulling out the needles and bandaging up to get back to 100%. They weren't at death's door or anything, but the healers in the party got to have their awesome moment too as the minor wounds got washed away by divine light.<br /> <br /> What's the point in resistance charms that let you regenerate health levels, or medicine charms that do the same, if you're only ever going to use them once every few months when the only actually interesting fight gets rolled?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347523#post1347523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whilst the PCs have motes, I feel like you're wearing down the wrong resources. Thanos didn't give up his highest level spell slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, what I'm talking about is foes that barely even call for motes to be spent. Like if your circle is facing off against a group of buck-ogres or something. Buck-ogres are cool! They're enormous monsters that wield two-handed weapons in each hand and have a pair of heads. I'd love to have an action scene where a few buck-ogres show up, one swings its axe that goes wide, then pulls its tetsubo around and knocks one of the Solars back towards a tree, whereupon that Solar plants her feet, leaps back towards it and slams her fist in its chest with a Heaven Thunder Hammer and knocks it to the fucking moon.<br /> <br /> What I get instead is everyone rolls initiative, the PCs go first and crash the hell out of everything on the battlefield, the buck ogre swings around to no effect, god help you if you actually use its Dual Strikes ability and start making attacks with 4-5 dice due to flurry penalties. Then maybe another round of withering attacks just to be sure, again the buck ogres all swing, nothing connects, and then the PCs all launch a round of decisive attacks and it's over. If they're not using their cool charms, because they don't have to, and all the antagonists cool abilities are pointless, the fight gets super anemic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347523#post1347523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jeeze, I feel disingenuous defending the terribad NPC design choices in the Corebook, but I do at least see the rationale. (I mean, I agree 100% with you, but I see what Holden &amp; Morke were shooting for -- you need an entry level if you're going to have room to grow.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I can see that, make one or two things to be the baseline, it's what 99.99% of Creation is made off, look at how easily the PCs overcome it. What I think is bad is saying that PCs start at level 15, and then writing the dozens or even hundreds of Monster Manual entries from levels 1-14, with all these interesting quirks and stuff, all just to prove a point of how your character is above it all.<br /> <br /> The same goes for the social systems, or even the setting documents. Like there's so much detail talking about the intricacies of the Realm and how it functions, and Threshold nations like Vaneha, or the peoples of the Dreaming Sea with the Children of Ten Fathers and the dangers of labyrinthine streets of Champoor if all it is is a sandcastle to be knocked down. Why do I care about Vaneha and what it's like if all I'm going to do is wander into the capital and declare myself its new emperor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T13:39:35-08:00","id":1347548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347544#post1347544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that was a case where the fight was over in one round because a PC grabbed the throttle and punched it, because that's the kind of thing wizards do. They hold out their hand, speak arcane words, and a dozen foes, along with anything flammable in the room, become ash. It's not a cantrip though, there was an actual choice to be made about using that ability.<br /> <br /> However, the fight, I think 3-4 fights before that, was one against 20 stirges. Now, stirges are CR1/8 creatures with 2hp, they're not mega deadly beasts. Unfortunately when that encounter happened the wizard was just flat out of fireballs, and indeed any AoE spells. So what ensued was an actual scene where the stirges used their special blood drain ability to puncture the PCs and drill their beaks into their flesh. Then there were some cool parts like when the paladin dropped his shield so he could dual wield and slice half a dozen of the little mosquito bats off the cleric, the warlock activated Armor of Agathys and ran through a big section of the flock, freezing solid any of them who dared touch him, our dragonborn maneuvered into the perfect position to just fry another big swath of them out of the air.<br /> <br /> Then afterwards the party did a thorough check to make sure they didn't miss anything, blocked the door and spent a bit of time pulling out the needles and bandaging up to get back to 100%. They weren't at death's door or anything, but the healers in the party got to have their awesome moment too as the minor wounds got washed away by divine light.<br /> <br /> What's the point in resistance charms that let you regenerate health levels, or medicine charms that do the same, if you're only ever going to use them once every few months when the only actually interesting fight gets rolled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they literally keep you alive when you fight gods of death. You don't need superhuman ability to survive being mauled by a house cat. <br /> <br /> 1 Strige per PC is not a threat. You can deal with that with Cantrips. The same principle applies to Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, what I'm talking about is foes that barely even call for motes to be spent. Like if your circle is facing off against a group of buck-ogres or something. Buck-ogres are cool! They're enormous monsters that wield two-handed weapons in each hand and have a pair of heads. I'd love to have an action scene where a few buck-ogres show up, one swings its axe that goes wide, then pulls its tetsubo around and knocks one of the Solars back towards a tree, whereupon that Solar plants her feet, leaps back towards it and slams her fist in its chest with a Heaven Thunder Hammer and knocks it to the fucking moon.<br /> <br /> What I get instead is everyone rolls initiative, the PCs go first and crash the hell out of everything on the battlefield, the buck ogre swings around to no effect, god help you if you actually use its Dual Strikes ability and start making attacks with 4-5 dice due to flurry penalties. Then maybe another round of withering attacks just to be sure, again the buck ogres all swing, nothing connects, and then the PCs all launch a round of decisive attacks and it's over. If they're not using their cool charms, because they don't have to, and all the antagonists cool abilities are pointless, the fight gets super anemic. </div> </div> </div>So don't fight Solars with Buck Orges.<br /> <br /> Use a battlegroup of Buck Orges using the battlegroup mass attack to murder civilians, whilst attacking the PCs wih Cataphracts. Expend something which isn't motes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same goes for the social systems, or even the setting documents. Like there's so much detail talking about the intricacies of the Realm and how it functions, and Threshold nations like Vaneha, or the peoples of the Dreaming Sea with the Children of Ten Fathers and the dangers of labyrinthine streets of Champoor if all it is is a sandcastle to be knocked down. Why do I care about Vaneha and what it's like if all I'm going to do is wander into the capital and declare myself its new emperor? </div> </div> </div>Because that's why and how they'll resist you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T15:14:14-08:00","id":1347561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347312#post1347312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So anyway, the Wyld Hunt can be a challenge for one Solar PC at high-level (though it depends on the Solar of course), but for an entire Circle, well, that's what giant invasions are for.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, that makes more sense.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Still, the query of facing a whole circle of Solars at that power represents the end of a continuous cycle of failure states that has moved well past the point of Wyld Hunts struck me as a point at which powerful Dragon Blooded groups might need to adjust their standards towards reconciling with the existence of those Exalted, at least in the short term.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It was a short step from there to the picture of some grand prince of the Raksha doing obeisance before their thrones, which expanded off into the picture of Solars at the level of such grandeur and achievement standing astride the most elaborate and overwrought court. More than just a meeting place for various factions and powers in which they can compete and intrigue and face the Solars at the heart of things with more subtle, nebulous threats, it struck me as the foundation for challenges of a different kind; to build things, to bring people together, to forge and promote and guide systems that might affect the world in new ways. I feel as though approaching such challenges would be less absolute than facing things off in combat, narratively and mechanically engaging while still being an exercise in the repeated subject of &quot;power great enough that the more important question is how you use it rather than can you use it&quot;.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It hit the same snag that I find in imagining a lot of scenarios focused around Exalted:</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Dawn Caste is barely functional in peace time.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh sure, I can imagine things that a member of the Dawn Caste might do. Patrol borders and marches, supervise defensive networks and keep garrison troops at their peak, even just themselves exist as a constant deterrent by virtue of the offensive power they're known to possess.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Things concerned with maintaining a stability rather than being presented with challenges, things that don't really play off of the core defining skills of the Dawn Caste. Things that strike me as just about okay for a character, but don't seem the most satisfying for the player behind them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It seems to me that the Dawn Caste is the only thing in the entire game with that issue. Even the Full Moon and Chosen of Battles are broader, but the Dawn only seems to have a use when there's an enemy before it. It doesn't know what to do in the exclusive company of friends.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This has always struck me as a bit of an issue, and I can't help but wonder if it's one that spreads out and interferes with the rest of the Solars. If it would not seem as big a deal for play to eventually reach a point at which a lot of people trying to fight them becomes generally unviable if there wasn't this one Caste that exists to demand a fight.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T17:31:36-08:00","id":1347575,"title":"","content":"Couple of pages old but I'm going to clear up some of the higher-level Onyx Path stuff:<br /> <br /> White Wolf's staff of ~50 could fit on a bus. Many people were surprised that the company was that &quot;small.&quot;<br /> <br /> Onyx Path's full-time staff can fit in a single car: Rich Thomas is the creative director, Lisa Thomas is the office manager, Mike Chaney is the art director, and Matt McElroy is our operations manager. Literally everyone else is a freelancer.<br /> <br /> Despite this, we manage four of our own game lines (Scarred Lands, Scion, They Came from Beneath the Sea!, and my own Trinity Continuum), two partner games (Cavaliers of Mars and Pugmire), two licensed non-WW games (Dystopia Rising: Evolution and Legendlore), and 18 licensed WW games (Vampire: The Masquerade, Werewolf: The Apocalypse, Mage: The Ascension, Wraith: The Oblivion, Changeling: The Dreaming, Exalted, Chronicles of Darkness, Vampire: The Requiem, Werewolf: The Forsaken, Mage: The Awakening, Promethean: The Created, Changeling: The Lost, Hunter: The Vigil, Geist: The Sin-Eaters, Mummy: The Curse, Demon: The Descent, Beast: The Primordial, Deviant: The Renegades). That's a total of 26 games, unless I miscounted somewhere. Our output is crazy high for a company of our size. (And, IMO, our quality is also crazy high given the number of things we work on.) And yes, while we're a fairly stable company, as others have pointed out, pretty much everyone in the industry is an indie company compared to Wizards of the Coast.<br /> <br /> Paradox-owned White Wolf published the first three books for Vampire 5th Edition, but it wasn't &quot;taken away&quot; from us. Our license hasn't changed and continues to include Vampire, but they wanted to publish those books in-house to make their own mark on the line. Following those three books, WW was re-absorbed back into Paradox, and management over the Vampire RPG line was handed over to Modiphius.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path has continued our license to publish Vampire material through this process. q.v. Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Prince's Gambit, and the upcoming Chicago by Night and Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T18:28:38-08:00","id":1347585,"title":"","content":"And just to illustrate that Wizard of Oz's examples aren't the only instance of high-level play, the game in which I play has just had some of the PCs reach Essence 4 and, to test out Robin's new artifact weapon, I threw her and another PC into a playtest fight. They did battle against a Dragon-Blooded commander (who never directly attacked them), his two elite soldiers, and a battle group of battle-ready soldiers. Despite the Lunar PC getting to throw on her warform before combat started, the elite soldiers had Crashed the Lunar and chewed through half her health, and were starting to turn their attention on Robin's unarmored self before I called it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T19:48:56-08:00","id":1347604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347548#post1347548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they literally keep you alive when you fight gods of death. You don't need superhuman ability to survive being mauled by a house cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if it's not another two months until the next time you bother firing up the combat system for an actual fight though, right? Otherwise you're still pretty much good. You only really need to heal your grievous wounds in a single night if the next day or two might be something critical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347548#post1347548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So don't fight Solars with Buck Orges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, obviously, and if it was just the buck-ogre that would be kind of sad, but I wouldn't really care all that much. The annoying thing is there's a lot of them. Hungry ghosts, ancestor ghosts, black hollows, ghostfishers, giant constrictors, tiger's eyes, cockatrices, it's not just random animals. There are things that aren't those, of course. A group of Greenmaws is okay, Bloodapes are solid, but I really wish I could use the other two thirds of the antagonists. Exalted's beastiary isn't exactly the largest in the industry, so taking a big chunk out of it isn't ideal.<br /> <br /> My plan for my next campaign is to maybe use some of them but with ideas like Kelly suggested, spending willpower like candy, maybe giving the Cataphract antagonist a pair of cockatrice pets in the vein of guard dogs. Maybe making a kind of super-ghostfisher. They're DBs so less powerful charms, but also they can wield artifacts and soldiers and stuff brazenly so it might be just as bad.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue is that a lot of these antagonists are written to not show up solo. Manticores specifically hunt alone, cockatrices seem to be loners, dogs of the unbroken earth don't really look the type to be pack hunters. So even when the foes start to get into reasonably dangerous territory you'll get the PC beatdown due to action economy. I need like a <i>pack </i>of Dogs of the Unbroken Earth or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347548#post1347548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's why and how they'll resist you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That implies that there will be some kind of resistance though. If the city of Paragon is nothing more than a house of cards to be swept aside by the wake of your character's passing, then it doesn't really matter and we should be saving word counts for the next free primordial that happens upon Creation while wondering the Wyld and decides to conquer it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T01:17:44-08:00","id":1347634,"title":"","content":"Also I'd like to point out another difficulty I had managing units that are of average power (ie, below player characters, but not a damn useless human) to try to balance a little fights against PC, and that is that players also have allies and summoned units of their own, and they have it more often (in my experience) than your NPCs. Usually any PC taking sorcery will like to have summon elemental or demon, because they are cool. They will have usually 1 retainer per group at least, maybe 1-2 allies as well, usually someone has a battle group of his own with Command, and I don't even count the fact they might simply have NPCs met through the game that have legit reasons to help them during some fight. That can make the &quot;Well it's fine I only have to account for 3-4 players&quot; to &quot;Well I actually have 9 characters on the player character's hands, that's a lot&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you logically evolve your position to 1) Every fight is damn long because if you want to balance this you have a fight with something like 15 characters total, which is way too much for me, or 2) well fellow players your summoned unit actually sucks so I'm not counting them for the fight, they are in the background but that means that 2) a) player invested in ressources and they actually don't really show up in play and 2) b) What legitimacy have you to put a big summoned unit like a greenmaw or something against the player when you just ditched their own greenmaw ?, or you do (my preferred option but it can feel very forced upon the players sometimes) 3) use non-vital PC units as a ressource to be &quot;spent&quot; on some challenges that justify them not participating in combat (Your greenmaw ? He can't fight, he is trying to keep together the crumbling bridge so you can escape !), resembling to some extent 2) a) but usually less frustrating the player","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:23:10-08:00","id":1347669,"title":"","content":"For that instance I usually reach a kind of compromise. If one of the characters is a real hardened focused commander who\u2019s weapon is more his battlegroup than his daiklave then he should enter combat with it. Otherwise if they\u2019ve got a bunch of NPC allies and young Dragonblooded retainers and stuff with them, then when they reach a scene that they might all contribute on I just focus down on the PCs. In the background there\u2019s a bigger battle going on, and each round that might have some effect on what\u2019s happening, like by creating environmental effects or something, but otherwise the forces the PCs brought just cancel some of the forces the NPCs brought and they have to fight the remainder.<br /> <br /> Besides, keeping powerful NPCs with you is almost the worst use for them I can think of. You\u2019re five Solar exalted, you don\u2019t really need help. On the other hand you can\u2019t be in two places at once. You should just assume you\u2019re going to achieve victory wherever you go, and keep the NPCs in critical places where you are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:40:09-08:00","id":1347671,"title":"","content":"Yes agree with you, there are solutions. But they are not self-evident, there is few tools in the books to find them, and it's a lot of &quot;Oh actually that didn't work, next time I'll know better&quot; that new ST will (I think) have some time to find their balance.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, these solutions have limits : Telling someone &quot;well the spell you took to summon fighting elementals/the retainer dragon blooded you took will do some things in the background that are actually useless/cinematic/counterbalanced by the summons of the ennemies I just made up for precisely that reason&quot; can feel frustrating to some people, and rightly so I believe. I believe in particular players realizing they invested in a lesser fighting ally just to feel it actually cancel something the ST would not have added if they didn't take it in some sort of zero-sum game can become the worst offender. I'm not saying there are no solutions, I'm saying the solutions themselves are not so easy to find out on your own, and they bring their own problems (I recognize said problem are lessened, though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:29:03-08:00","id":1347676,"title":"","content":"Yeah it\u2019s particularly a problem I\u2019m concerned about for my upcoming game. When your whole group is Dynasts they\u2019re all pretty justified in going everywhere with a battlegroup of guards and retainer or two in tow, and when you multiply that by four or five it gets to be a LOT. One player I know was rolling around the idea of having a size 1-2 battlegroup and two retainers, one a commander and another a super elite mortal champion as part of his standard retinue. I ran a few test combats with him using that setup and he took down some pretty serious opposition in very short order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:39:59-08:00","id":1347678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347604#post1347604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if it's not another two months until the next time you bother firing up the combat system for an actual fight though, right? Otherwise you're still pretty much good. You only really need to heal your grievous wounds in a single night if the next day or two might be something critical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try fighting those Buck Ogres on a -2 Wound Penalty. I'll wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:49:18-08:00","id":1347679,"title":"","content":"Yeah that is totally implayable I feel you. I think in general in your case you have 2 obvious options :<ul><li>Letting the player use all his combat options, which makes 1 player having basically 4-5 controlled unit for himself. Drawback : Way too long to play, generally too powerful, difficult to balance with matching opposition that doesn't take too many units either.</li> <li>Telling the players : Actually your units are not strong enough so they'll be cinematic/props for most of the fights we are gonna do. Drawback : Why invest so much (I think we are at about 7-8 dots of merits at least in your case) if it's just a mechanical prop for fights ?</li> </ul><br /> I get that there are numerous considerations that follows (the 8 dots of merits can do more useful things than fight : guard cities, run administrations, etc ...) but that's not what the player wants. I guess the straightforward answer is : you are the hero, others are not. If you want other stuff to follow in battle, they are battle group and that's it, and you command them. And I guess it's kind of fair, but it's not so easy to grasp for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T07:57:24-08:00","id":1347682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347678#post1347678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try fighting those Buck Ogres on a -2 Wound Penalty. I'll wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but in this specific case it's pretty boring. Having -2 wound penalty because you were wounded fighting Pretty Strong Boss, Abducter of Abysses, Devourer of The Maw at the issue of the campaign, and it being a penalty when you then fight ducking Buck Ogres 1 and 2 which are now &quot;challenging encounter&quot; seems pretty bad scenario design.<br /> <br /> I think what DrMonkeyLove is looking for is basically the same thing than me : Intermediary fights that pose a challenge, but not a threat to lose, building the tension for when you reach Big Boss. And I must say for the moment, I have never seen or successfully done myself a scenario where I do this in an interesting way, and I believe it is due to the way the game is balanced, and the basic antagonists are designed. And I believe we are legitimate looking for this kind of mechanics, because it feels in genre (source : every bad shonen I ever read)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T09:23:38-08:00","id":1347699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347682#post1347682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but in this specific case it's pretty boring. Having -2 wound penalty because you were wounded fighting Pretty Strong Boss, Abducter of Abysses, Devourer of The Maw at the issue of the campaign, and it being a penalty when you then fight ducking Buck Ogres 1 and 2 which are now &amp;quot;challenging encounter&amp;quot; seems pretty bad scenario design.<br /> <br /> I think what DrMonkeyLove is looking for is basically the same thing than me : Intermediary fights that pose a challenge, but not a threat to lose, building the tension for when you reach Big Boss. And I must say for the moment, I have never seen or successfully done myself a scenario where I do this in an interesting way, and I believe it is due to the way the game is balanced, and the basic antagonists are designed. And I believe we are legitimate looking for this kind of mechanics, because it feels in genre (source : every bad shonen I ever read)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But if a Circle of Abyssals are the Big Boss, then fight a pair of Nephwracks, with their War Ghost Battlegroup and couple of Mortwright slaves as the Dragon. Maybe throw in an Undead Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> If Ahlat's the Big Boss, have Fakhura as the Dragon.<br /> <br /> You can blow through hordes of zombies, spine chains and hungry ghosts as faceless minions, step things up for a lieutenant fight then step things up again. I get the frustration that a spine chain isn't, in any way, a step-up over a zombie. But a nephwrack is. And an Abysal is another step up, which scales all the way with the PCs. Be nice to have more useful Abysals and fewer useless zombies, but the options are there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T10:19:26-08:00","id":1347707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347678#post1347678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try fighting those Buck Ogres on a -2 Wound Penalty. I'll wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buck-Ogres might be kind of a bad example just because they\u2019re so atrocious. As long as your 10% invested guy picked up dipping swallow he can spend a net 1m per turn and have 7 defense to the buck ogres 7-8 dice attacks, before the ogres wound penalties. Or if he wants to be super safe spend 3 motes a turn for 8 defence. <br /> <br /> Really Solars have enough super early charms that remove all penalties that the real danger of being in your -2s is just that you might only be a couple of health levels from incapacitated. Maybe at that point a big school of fog sharks might become more scary? You\u2019re still perfectly safe, they\u2019d have to survive a round of withering attacks from your whole circle with enough initiative to try and launch a decisive, and even with double 8s they have a really hard time hitting your max defense. It might make people sit up and pay attention enough to put some effort into knocking them down though, which is what I\u2019m looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:22:29-08:00","id":1347733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347699#post1347699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be nice to have more useful Abysals and fewer useless zombies, but the options are there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would also be nice if there weren\u2019t so many really cool things that aren\u2019t powerful enough to meaningfully use. Right now I\u2019m sitting here looking at a giant underworld monster the size of a redwood with a ghostly creepy anglerfish decoy, a rooster-lizard with blazing eyes that sees into your soul and burns you from the inside out, an intelligent lion-man-scorpion and a dozen other really cool things that I can\u2019t ever see myself using. Or if I did, I\u2019d never get to actually see the parts of them that are really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T16:19:42-08:00","id":1347784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347682#post1347682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but in this specific case it's pretty boring. Having -2 wound penalty because you were wounded fighting Pretty Strong Boss, Abducter of Abysses, Devourer of The Maw at the issue of the campaign, and it being a penalty when you then fight ducking Buck Ogres 1 and 2 which are now &quot;challenging encounter&quot; seems pretty bad scenario design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what makes narrative sense.<br /> It's possible that the boss is a Lunar warlord leading an army of wyld creatures, so the circle used the skills at their disposal to sneek into the enemy camp and take on the Lunar first. Then they fought buck ogres in the aftermath of their assassination because the army didn't automatically implode without its leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-11-2019, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:20:28-08:00","id":1348492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1347575#post1347575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of pages old but I'm going to clear up some of the higher-level Onyx Path stuff:<br /> <br /> White Wolf's staff of ~50 could fit on a bus. Many people were surprised that the company was that &quot;small.&quot;<br /> <br /> Onyx Path's full-time staff can fit in a single car: Rich Thomas is the creative director, Lisa Thomas is the office manager, Mike Chaney is the art director, and Matt McElroy is our operations manager. Literally everyone else is a freelancer.<br /> <br /> Despite this, we manage four of our own game lines (Scarred Lands, Scion, They Came from Beneath the Sea!, and my own Trinity Continuum), two partner games (Cavaliers of Mars and Pugmire), two licensed non-WW games (Dystopia Rising: Evolution and Legendlore), and 18 licensed WW games (Vampire: The Masquerade, Werewolf: The Apocalypse, Mage: The Ascension, Wraith: The Oblivion, Changeling: The Dreaming, Exalted, Chronicles of Darkness, Vampire: The Requiem, Werewolf: The Forsaken, Mage: The Awakening, Promethean: The Created, Changeling: The Lost, Hunter: The Vigil, Geist: The Sin-Eaters, Mummy: The Curse, Demon: The Descent, Beast: The Primordial, Deviant: The Renegades). That's a total of 26 games, unless I miscounted somewhere. Our output is crazy high for a company of our size. (And, IMO, our quality is also crazy high given the number of things we work on.) And yes, while we're a fairly stable company, as others have pointed out, pretty much everyone in the industry is an indie company compared to Wizards of the Coast.<br /> <br /> Paradox-owned White Wolf published the first three books for Vampire 5th Edition, but it wasn't &quot;taken away&quot; from us. Our license hasn't changed and continues to include Vampire, but they wanted to publish those books in-house to make their own mark on the line. Following those three books, WW was re-absorbed back into Paradox, and management over the Vampire RPG line was handed over to Modiphius.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path has continued our license to publish Vampire material through this process. q.v. Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Prince's Gambit, and the upcoming Chicago by Night and Cults of the Blood Gods.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you are saying here. The company is extremely small, very few people work on Exalted, meaning that every single book takes an incredible amount of time before it is released.<br /> <br /> I have one question though, because I don't understand why there is this seemingly vast, stop gap in development though. What I mean is that as far as I understand, and please correct me if I am wrong, art for various books are only ordered many months after the manuscript is written. It seems terribly ineffective to me, I am one of those who wants the Exalted books as fast as humanly possible (I think all of us do), and it is strange I think that Heirs of the Shogunate, for instance, which as far as I understand it is a finished book by now, doesn't even seem to be in Arts direction.<br /> I don't understand the logic of this, as it obviously means that the books takes way longer before they are released etc.<br /> It is tragic that the books takes so exceptionally long before they are released, so I wonder why art is not worked on far earlier in the process, as I reckon that might save us 3-4 months at least. But I may be wrong. I am not the expert here, you guys are. But I do wonder about these matters indeed, being one of the many impatient Game Masters waiting for books I had honestly thought would be released long ago (though I know better now of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":".  Spacing 11-14-2019, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:45:03-08:00","id":1348495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1348492#post1348492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one question though, because I don't understand why there is this seemingly vast, stop gap in development though. What I mean is that as far as I understand, and please correct me if I am wrong, art for various books are only ordered many months after the manuscript is written. It seems terribly ineffective to me, I am one of those who wants the Exalted books as fast as humanly possible (I think all of us do), and it is strange I think that Heirs of the Shogunate, for instance, which as far as I understand it is a finished book by now, doesn't even seem to be in Arts direction.<br /> I don't understand the logic of this, as it obviously means that the books takes way longer before they are released etc.<br /> It is tragic that the books takes so exceptionally long before they are released, so I wonder why art is not worked on far earlier in the process, as I reckon that might save us 3-4 months at least. But I may be wrong. I am not the expert here, you guys are. But I do wonder about these matters indeed, being one of the many impatient Game Masters waiting for books I had honestly thought would be released long ago (though I know better now of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>Art development is a parallel track to manuscript development. The art is being produced during the period of time while the manuscript goes through editing, post-editing development, and layout. It doesn't delay the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:53:35-08:00","id":1348497,"title":"","content":"Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1120\" data-vbnamecard=\"1120\">Eric Minton</a>, for clarifying that. I am very happy to be mistaken !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T10:10:02-08:00","id":1348505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnus K</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1348492#post1348492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have one question though, because I don't understand why there is this seemingly vast, stop gap in development though. What I mean is that as far as I understand, and please correct me if I am wrong, art for various books are only ordered many months after the manuscript is written.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what Eric already said, that art direction happens concurrently with a bunch of other production, bear in mind that art direction really <i>can't </i>proceed until the manuscript is already in a reasonably firmed-up state. Art direction is not just a matter of saying &quot;it would be cool to have a picture of this character! Hey, [ARTISTNAME], could you make a picture of that, please?&quot; In order to commission an art piece for a book, you've got to know how big it's going to be, which in turn means having at least a rough idea of how the layout is going to look, and that, in turn, means having a basically-completed manuscript. If you started art direction when the book was still getting manuscript bits turned in, you'd end up with situations where a piece of text was longer than expected, or shorter, or just had to be cut entirely, which would change what sort of art would fit in. And you can't tell an artist &quot;sorry, the book ended up not needing that bit after all. So we're not going to pay you.&quot; Artists, understandably, don't like that.<br /> <br /> So in order to do your art direction, you've got to have the complete manuscript, more-or-less as it's going to print, and have a pretty clear idea of how it's going to be arranged, even if that's not totally finalized. Only then can you start commissioning your art pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T01:34:42-08:00","id":1350404,"title":"","content":"While I too would love to have all the books out now, and yes, it's probably hurting some groups, i have two thoughts. <br /> <br /> 1. Not only do writers like money, they love the little ego boost that comes from people buying their stuff. I write, and I know this to be true. No writer sits on something or doesn't write quickly if they have a choice. Hell, many writers I know, given a chance between watching a movie and writing, choose to write.<br /> <br /> BUT...<br /> <br /> 2. When people talk about the era of lots of splats coming out, I'd also note that due to the speed, lots of well, problematic rules issues arose. Sure we got a lot of books, but often they were like that big fancy car that drops the transmission a day after you buy it. Fast is not always good, and writers only have so much time in the day. <br /> <br /> I just expect that it's coming as fast as it can, and until then just kitbash or focus on campaigns that do currently have support--I'm getting ready to launch a DB campaign in the Blessed Isle that probably isn't going to have ANY non-DB exalted show up, and it'll last me the next six months, easy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T05:20:02-08:00","id":1350423,"title":"","content":"Something I was meaning to add is that I've also noticed how a lot of Storytellers appear to have hamstrung themselves.<br /> <br /> In terms of content for NPCs we don't currently have splat books for, the obvious answer to &quot;how do I represent this power?&quot; is to use Solar Charms and cut them back a little then occasionally add a few new features. That's how the previous editions did basically everything.<br /> For example, a Lunar character in my game had this on her pre-Fangs at the Gate character sheet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flowing Body Evasion-</b> as Seven Shadow Evasion, no reset condition (upgrade later?) allows the character to shapeshift reflexively when activated.<br /> <br /> I'm actually pretty happy with it as a rudimentary adaptation of a charm from MoEP: Lunars into 3<sup>rd</sup> edition based on familiar precedents because I don\u2019t hold myself to game developer standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:52:09-08:00","id":1351023,"title":"","content":"Well, after seeing this forum post, I figured it was time to dust off the old account and chime in. I am one of those that did not make the transition to the latest edition of exalted, mainly in that I played Abyssals and Infernals. I liked the alchemicals and dearly wanted to see them get some actual screen time rather than being a throwaway final splat before the edition wheel turned yet again. I am one of those who waited and am still waiting, for this current edition to take notice of me, before I pay a considerable amount of money to get those hefty books.<br /> <br /> I doubt I am alone. I have no proof of course, but I would imagine that there were a fair few like me who held back, because of all the troubles and who were not content to simply reskin solars to play the game they wanted. After how things like necromancy were always a second class citizen compared to magic, I wanted to see the Abyssals actually given equal, but different standing and an actual share of the exalted storyline. Quite why Dragon blooded got such attention is beyond me, but I wont take that away from their fans in the current edition....I just know that all that material is not for my exalted, where dragon bloods are meant to be the antagonists.<br /> <br /> So, there are certainly some of us who have been left behind, but who are watching and waiting. Checking the forums a few times each year, thinking &quot;hey, maybe they finally got round to abyssal&quot; and finding yet another book about items, the dragon blooded or some other thing that isn't the main splats. I wish the new writers well and hope that I may well see the maiden of the mirthless smile and her merry cohort once again....fighting an uncaring sun and preparing to bring this whole sorry saga of creation to its merciful end.<br /> <br /> I`ll likely see you all next year and who knows what we may find, but till then my Soulsteel Grand Daiklaive rests easy in my hand and goodness knows what is going on in Autochthon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","user":"Silvercat18","date":". 11-26-2019, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4104-silvercat18","name":"Silvercat18","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4104_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T11:57:12-08:00","id":1351084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351023#post1351023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am one of those who waited and am still waiting, for this current edition to take notice of me, before I pay a considerable amount of money to get those hefty books.<br /> <br /> I doubt I am alone. I have no proof of course, but I would imagine that there were a fair few like me who held back, because of all the troubles and who were not content to simply reskin solars to play the game they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a few friends in this boat who aren't interested in 3rd Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T13:55:45-08:00","id":1351114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silvercat18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351023#post1351023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, after seeing this forum post, I figured it was time to dust off the old account and chime in. I am one of those that did not make the transition to the latest edition of exalted, mainly in that I played Abyssals and Infernals. I liked the alchemicals and dearly wanted to see them get some actual screen time rather than being a throwaway final splat before the edition wheel turned yet again. I am one of those who waited and am still waiting, for this current edition to take notice of me, before I pay a considerable amount of money to get those hefty books.<br /> <br /> I doubt I am alone. I have no proof of course, but I would imagine that there were a fair few like me who held back, because of all the troubles and who were not content to simply reskin solars to play the game they wanted. After how things like necromancy were always a second class citizen compared to magic, I wanted to see the Abyssals actually given equal, but different standing and an actual share of the exalted storyline. Quite why Dragon blooded got such attention is beyond me, but I wont take that away from their fans in the current edition....I just know that all that material is not for my exalted, where dragon bloods are meant to be the antagonists.<br /> <br /> So, there are certainly some of us who have been left behind, but who are watching and waiting. Checking the forums a few times each year, thinking &quot;hey, maybe they finally got round to abyssal&quot; and finding yet another book about items, the dragon blooded or some other thing that isn't the main splats. I wish the new writers well and hope that I may well see the maiden of the mirthless smile and her merry cohort once again....fighting an uncaring sun and preparing to bring this whole sorry saga of creation to its merciful end.<br /> <br /> I`ll likely see you all next year and who knows what we may find, but till then my Soulsteel Grand Daiklaive rests easy in my hand and goodness knows what is going on in Autochthon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid you'll likely be waiting a couple of years.<br /> <br /> Next year Lunars will be released and Exigents will be kickstarted. Then probably in 2021 Exigents will be released and Sidereals will be kickstarted.<br /> Definitely the currently planned order is Solars (done), Dragonblood (done), Lunars (written and the text released to backers, in editing and art direction), Exigents, Sidereals. They haven't announced what it'll be after Sidereals, but I assume it'll be Abyssals. I guess they might do Infernals instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:13:19-08:00","id":1351118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351114#post1351114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm afraid you'll likely be waiting a couple of years.<br /> <br /> Next year Lunars will be released and Exigents will be kickstarted. Then probably in 2021 Exigents will be released and Sidereals will be kickstarted.<br /> Definitely the currently planned order is Solars (done), Dragonblood (done), Lunars (written and the text released to backers, in editing and art direction), Exigents, Sidereals. They haven't announced what it'll be after Sidereals, but I assume it'll be Abyssals. I guess they might do Infernals instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals likely after Sidereals since well, they were more well, intrinsict to the game's history and setting. Plus it seems like the devs have thought on more with them and the Underworld in a way that a refresh would be nice novelty to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:14:03-08:00","id":1351119,"title":"","content":"Infernals are pretty likely the second to last splat. If anything I'd say Getimians go after Sidereals (or along them), then Abyssals and Liminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:14:37-08:00","id":1351120,"title":"","content":"Oh, it's just occurred to me, do you Abyssal fans know they recently released a short pdf with an example Abyssal NPC?<br /> <br /> It doesn't really let you make an Abyssal circle or something, just thought you might find it interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:22:55-08:00","id":1351123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351119#post1351119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infernals are pretty likely the second to last splat. If anything I'd say Getimians go after Sidereals (or along them), then Abyssals and Liminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last it came up, Getimians and Liminals aren't getting full KS'd splats, but they're going to be released very near their related splats, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T14:30:06-08:00","id":1351126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351123#post1351123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last it came up, Getimians and Liminals aren't getting full KS'd splats, but they're going to be released very near their related splats, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah that's more or less what I was referencing, they're still splatbooks even if not hardcover stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T15:49:30-08:00","id":1351144,"title":"","content":"Well, if they're shorter, they might not slow down the main splat books so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:12:19-08:00","id":1351149,"title":"","content":"I actually wonder how long Exigent's is going to be. Is it going to be really long because of how deep they're going to go into it, or actually pretty short because they don't need to do much more than fluff and mechanical guidelines? Or just say &quot;Well, we'll go as deep as we can in the space of about a regular splatbook and leave it there.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:28:13-08:00","id":1351155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351149#post1351149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually wonder how long Exigent's is going to be. Is it going to be really long because of how deep they're going to go into it, or actually pretty short because they don't need to do much more than fluff and mechanical guidelines? Or just say &quot;Well, we'll go as deep as we can in the space of about a regular splatbook and leave it there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that it's not just fluff and mechanical guidelines, but four whole Exigents statted up with full Charmsets... sounds like it's gonna be on the long side. In fact, it seems to be the reason why it will not have any space for MAs or Artifacts (besides Janest's scythe I suppose). Lunars was in Development when the KS happened and Exigents is way behind as of now. I just hope the KS happens during Q1 next year still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:41:02-08:00","id":1351158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351155#post1351155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Considering that it's not just fluff and mechanical guidelines, but four whole Exigents statted up with full Charmsets... sounds like it's gonna be on the long side. In fact, it seems to be the reason why it will not have any space for MAs or Artifacts (besides Janest's scythe I suppose). Lunars was in Development when the KS happened and Exigents is way behind as of now. I just hope the KS happens during Q1 next year still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents is likely just structured very differently from Lunars. Drafts to Redlines to Secondd Drafts might go faster or slower as need be. It's going to be a pretty mechanics heavy book and complex, and also pretty important for future releases, so it taking longer is kind of expected. In the interrum at least, we'll probably get <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> and the finished Lunars book, so I think there will at least be stuff to chew on while waiting on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:48:38-08:00","id":1351159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351158#post1351158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exigents is likely just structured very differently from Lunars. Drafts to Redlines to Secondd Drafts might go faster or slower as need be. It's going to be a pretty mechanics heavy book and complex, and also pretty important for future releases, so it taking longer is kind of expected. In the interrum at least, we'll probably get <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> and the finished Lunars book, so I think there will at least be stuff to chew on while waiting on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heirs is merely in development as of now and it's been about... two years, now? Don't think that's getting to us anytime soon. And finished Lunars will probably only entertain for as long as art and re-balanced Charms here and there can. I hope it doesn't take longer than Q1 because that's when I go visit my internetless friends and bring them a new splat of Exalted each year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:49:13-08:00","id":1351487,"title":"","content":"I think five years (and counting) is a very long and absurd wait. I understand that the Exalted team is in no shape to deliver the books faster. I understand that time invested into development is correlated with quality of the final product. But I also think that Ex3 is overdesigned. <br /> <br /> Some of my friends call Ex3 &quot;Exalted Charm edition&quot; because of the insane number of charms in the core, and how many of them are about playing some stupid mini-game about re-rolling certain numbers, and counting some as two successes, and then checking if condition A or B was met in order to add X bonus to initiative, which factors into your ability to deal damage, and also determines the order of action, but wait, there's more, because in some conditions you can have more or less overwhelming, and depending on the element of the charm you used, you could or could not use some aura dependent shit bla bla bla bla bla...<br /> <br /> With a game soooo convoluted, obviouly making a new supplements will take longer. You know what is the book I've been waiting for forever? Heirs to the Shogunate... I thought it was a supplement, but it's taking the same amount of time as WFHW did to come out. I don't care for backer charms. I just want to read about the new DB clans and strange groups out there. I don't need a thousand more charms at this point.<br /> <br /> I do want to read the new ideas about the setting, and Abyssals, Liminals, Getimians etc are concepts that I would love to know and be able to use. Abyssals of course are homebrewable... but Getimians? I don't care about their mechanics so much as I care about what they actually are and want, not just a teaser preview. I think it's absurd to continue having all this concepts ten years ahead of us. <br /> <br /> I would prefer if Ex3 prematurely ended... I know that would be horrible for a number of reasons, but, at least I wouldn't feel trapped anymore in an edition I don't fully like for the nex 30 years. I would be more excited if we had the hope of getting a new lighter game that was easier to write. That way maybe more than three people in the world could be able to design mechanics and stuff to keep the game alive and running.<br /> <br /> Yes... I'm not the most optimistic about this subject. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:55:41-08:00","id":1351488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351158#post1351158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exigents is likely just structured very differently from Lunars. Drafts to Redlines to Secondd Drafts might go faster or slower as need be. It's going to be a pretty mechanics heavy book and complex, and also pretty important for future releases, so it taking longer is kind of expected. In the interrum at least, we'll probably get <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> and the finished Lunars book, so I think there will at least be stuff to chew on while waiting on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Alistair said, the finished Lunars book is just art and some tweaks.<br /> <br /> But before Exigents (well, before the finished version anyway) there'll be Across the Eight Directions, which should be full of cool fluff. Probably not much for crunch-monkeys, but then, as Gonzo said, there's plenty of that as-is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:02:44-08:00","id":1351500,"title":"","content":"I'll join this particular chorus briefly. I'm also mostly waiting for <i>Heirs</i>. And I'm looking leerily at Exigents moving up the development queue. At this rate, I feel there's a very real chance of us hitting an Exigents KS with <i>Heirs </i>still unreleased. People will be encouraged to pledge for backer charms, rally behind stretch goals to build a companion, when there are two already lodged in the production queue. That seems excessive - I was willing to be a little lenient with the Lunars KS because they were still figuring this stuff out, but a repeat performance of that?<br /> <br /> I'm actually getting annoyed at Crucible of Legends and Across the Eight Directions too, just because it feels like the devs/writers are being scattershot here. When I'm waiting for a book like Heirs, one I paid to have some content in, hearing that the team are working on other projects just makes me feel like a rube. Like they've taken the money and are gonna get to it when they feel like, not before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:40:31-08:00","id":1351510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351500#post1351500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll join this particular chorus briefly. I'm also mostly waiting for <i>Heirs</i>. And I'm looking leerily at Exigents moving up the development queue. At this rate, I feel there's a very real chance of us hitting an Exigents KS with <i>Heirs </i>still unreleased. People will be encouraged to pledge for backer charms, rally behind stretch goals to build a companion, when there are two already lodged in the production queue. That seems excessive - I was willing to be a little lenient with the Lunars KS because they were still figuring this stuff out, but a repeat performance of that?<br /> <br /> I'm actually getting annoyed at Crucible of Legends and Across the Eight Directions too, just because it feels like the devs/writers are being scattershot here. When I'm waiting for a book like Heirs, one I paid to have some content in, hearing that the team are working on other projects just makes me feel like a rube. Like they've taken the money and are gonna get to it when they feel like, not before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the coreobok was in layout for a year. And Onyx Path has shown to be just pretty bottle-necked at things like art and layout since ever. What's notable for instance is that <i>The Realm</i>, a book pretty light on crunch, did take a while to make as well. And both <i>Accross the EIght Directions </i>and <i>Crucible of Legends</i> are being made with their own budgets, separate from the Kickstarters. In the latter's case, it even has a different developer than the usual Eric or Robert, and there's been an effort to try and get more people who can write Exalted so they can do more projects.<br /> <br /> Mind, this isn't able to be reflected in a release list unless you include entire known credit lists. But remember thatwith how OPP is structured, the only stuff that doesn't exist until it is KS'd is the Companions and art. <i>Accross the Eight Directions</i> was likely planned, proposed, approve,d and contracted before <i>Heirs</i> was. And due to how Kickstarters work, what even went into <i>Heirs</i> isn't known until everything is gathered from backers, things are outlined and total wordocunt budget for those goals is put together.<br /> <br /> Also note that the teams do overlapping projects because well, at times they do things that overlap. If Eric and Robert, the developers, are not writing a particular section in <i>Heirs</i>, they could be redlining what drafts are coming in with At8D. While At8D is in Second Drafts, there's to authors, there's not actually a lot they can even <i>do</i> with it, so they work on developing Heirs (rewriting and editting stuff) while waiting for At8D drafts to come in. And while doing that, they can get art notes ready or have art pieces contracted, or be prototyping maps.<br /> <br /> I think a thing to remember is that books creation isn't quite zero-sum. Halting all work on At8D and CoL won't speed-up <i>Heirs</i>, and if it does, not to an amount that necessarily means much. It's at this point in the area where Eric and Robert tend to have a lot of thier onw personal time put into it beyond editting and contracting. The other stuff where they are at in the process, while still taking work (not all drafts come in at once) probably isn't the same sorta work.<br /> <br /> Kind of note that the other step they typically have a lot of work to do (Redlines) Is <i>not</i> what htey're worrying about with <i>Crucible of Legends</i> because they ahve another dev from them (Neall). They have to coordinate, but note again, getting people to actually work on things probably helps here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T10:48:03-08:00","id":1351512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351487#post1351487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think five years (and counting) is a very long and absurd wait. I understand that the Exalted team is in no shape to deliver the books faster. I understand that time invested into development is correlated with quality of the final product. But I also think that Ex3 is overdesigned. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Again, layout for a year. There's not like...anything the current team can do that since that's in a way a different department.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351487#post1351487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... With a game soooo convoluted, obviouly making a new supplements will take longer. You know what is the book I've been waiting for forever? Heirs to the Shogunate... I thought it was a supplement, but it's taking the same amount of time as WFHW did to come out. I don't care for backer charms. I just want to read about the new DB clans and strange groups out there. I don't need a thousand more charms at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a show that it's not just Charms that take time, but actually making the rest of the book. Note <i>The Realm</i> took about as long as WFHW did as well. In the end fo the day, you still have some amount of words that need to be budgetted, laid-out, editted, and developed. Would simpler mechanics help? Sure. Then again, <i>Scion</i> <i>2e</i> was promised the same year originallya s <i>Exalted 3e</i>'s KS, and didn't actually come out until 2018. So simpler systems don't by their nature, result in faster game devlopment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351487#post1351487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do want to read the new ideas about the setting, and Abyssals, Liminals, Getimians etc are concepts that I would love to know and be able to use. Abyssals of course are homebrewable... but Getimians? I don't care about their mechanics so much as I care about what they actually are and want, not just a teaser preview. I think it's absurd to continue having all this concepts ten years ahead of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why we're getting <i>CoL</i> a bit. Exalted 3e was made probably assuming a more aggressive potential schedule than before. (Note that the devs before could get ab ook turned-aorund in like 8 months with things like Shards shown). Different circumastances on the game, what's neeed of it, the company, and the industry mean things just don't do that as they did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351487#post1351487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would prefer if Ex3 prematurely ended... I know that would be horrible for a number of reasons, but, at least I wouldn't feel trapped anymore in an edition I don't fully like for the nex 30 years. I would be more excited if we had the hope of getting a new lighter game that was easier to write. That way maybe more than three people in the world could be able to design mechanics and stuff to keep the game alive and running.<br /> <br /> Yes... I'm not the most optimistic about this subject. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think on it this way. If we were to reboot and have Exalted 4e KS next year? I am skeptical we would seen any of this anytime faster. Look at the wordcount of setting between WFHW and <i>The Realm</i>. Now think about the fact that if you do a new edition, unless you really wanna have folks using books with outdated mechanics, having to contract to mor eor less do that all over in less than a few years. Basically the solution you want is probably at this point, a game dead for a few years, not the stuff you want sooner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T11:03:33-08:00","id":1351514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351510#post1351510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note that the teams do overlapping projects because well, at times they do things that overlap. If Eric and Robert, the developers, are not writing a particular section in <i>Heirs</i>, they could be redlining what drafts are coming in with At8D. While At8D is in Second Drafts, there's to authors, there's not actually a lot they can even <i>do</i> with it, so they work on developing Heirs (rewriting and editting stuff) while waiting for At8D drafts to come in. And while doing that, they can get art notes ready or have art pieces contracted, or be prototyping maps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. It makes sense to have multiple things in the queue. If it weren't for Exigents I'd probably be less bitter. But we've had complete draft text for Lunars, three new books enter the queue, one a fatsplat, and the Realm complete all since Heirs was announced. Without being able to look inside the Devs heads or actively follow what specifically they're currently working on, it feels like Heirs was the backburner project - especially since an entire splat book will seemingly make it all the way through the process before it arrives (Lunars)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T11:40:01-08:00","id":1351515,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if just throwing out setting info without charms would be that much faster.<br /> <br /> It feels like a totally different skill set, where you need to make cultures, peoples, and groups interesting to be a part of and interesting to interact with, making then feel human, which involves partially then following their own beliefs and partially points where their beliefs collapse but they don't acknowledge it or have excuses, and devoting the correct amount of workspace between answers and open-endedness to let players and STs hook into those societies and do interesting things with them.<br /> <br /> In comparison for me, I find writing charms to be much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T11:52:00-08:00","id":1351519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351514#post1351514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I know. It makes sense to have multiple things in the queue. If it weren't for Exigents I'd probably be less bitter. But we've had complete draft text for Lunars, three new books enter the queue, one a fatsplat, and the Realm complete all since Heirs was announced. Without being able to look inside the Devs heads or actively follow what specifically they're currently working on, it feels like Heirs was the backburner project - especially since an entire splat book will seemingly make it all the way through the process before it arrives (Lunars)</div> </div> </div> </div>Something to consider is lead-in.<br /> <br /> <i>The Realm</i> was started around the same time as WFHW. It actually has a lot of the same authors and I think material even might have moved between them. In effect it was written as additional chapters for <i>Dragon-Blooded</i>. That said, note that it didn't come out until after the KS'd book. Because in the end, they were on parralel tracks...one started a bit after the other. ANd one came out after the other.<br /> <br /> No work on <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> was started before the KS came out. The devs needed an oultine, final count of rewards, and feedback from backers before things could even get started. So keep this in mind. <i>The Realm</i> and WFHW were more or less bieng worked on for about 18 months when they came out. <i>Heirs</i> didn't really start being written until June (according to MMNs). Since you know, working on finsihing DBs probably took priority still. In this context, we're still kind of well in, but still a ways away. Mind, it looks like it'll take more than 18 months, (no clue where art/alyout is). And in addition, note that when <i>Heirs</i> was being outlined, Lunars probably was already contracted and outlined. Going over the Monday Meeting Notes, FatG first-shows up in April as First Drafts. Note that at this time, <i>Heirs</i> is still probably being outlined. And while <i>Heirs</i> is likely not as big a book asFatG, it is not enough to make it's lead-time much different. See WFHW and <i>The Realm</i>.<br /> <br /> All and all, it's just a matter of first in, first out. Lunars had work starting up pretty much just as DBs was wrapping up. Heirs didn't get booted up until a couple months after that. My guess is that with this timing in mind, <i>Heirs</i> is likely due a bit after <i>Lunars</i> is out. Note that it's the most ahead of the other books too (CoL and At8D's current stages won't affect Lunars much).<br /> <br /> Looking at things we also have Redlines right now for <i>Exigents </i>and <i>Many-Faced Strangers</i>. Which yeah, might slow down <i>Heirs</i>. But note that MFS is also paid-for and something they proably want moving along. And Exigents is something they have a clear temporal deadline theyw anna hit (Q1). It is gonna be annoying that the companion isn't out before the first KS, but in the end, they ahve what looks to be an 18-20 month start-to-finish cycle. THey can't quite do the 9-month turnarounds of 2e anymore due to manpower, resources and other bottlenecks (layout being the big one). It just happens that they overlap in a way that looks this way, mostly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:15:05-08:00","id":1351522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351519#post1351519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at things we also have Redlines right now for <i>Exigents </i>and <i>Many-Faced Strangers</i>. Which yeah, might slow down <i>Heirs</i>. But note that MFS is also paid-for and something they proably want moving along. And Exigents is something they have a clear temporal deadline theyw anna hit (Q1). It is gonna be annoying that the companion isn't out before the first KS, but in the end, they ahve what looks to be an 18-20 month start-to-finish cycle. THey can't quite do the 9-month turnarounds of 2e anymore due to manpower, resources and other bottlenecks (layout being the big one). It just happens that they overlap in a way that looks this way, mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the ultimate question for me. Does it compound? Because with this turnaround of splats relative to companions you're going to end up with more of the latter in the queue and subsequent ones taking longer. Heirs began to some degree after WFHW wrapped, took us through that hitting publication and through Exigents getting first draft. And only now is MFS starting to get work. So how long till MFS hits? Unless there's a big change up Exigents will lead to another companion book too, that'll be in the queue. Will we get MFS before 2021 and Sidereals? Heirs was the only companion in the queue before - turnarounds gonna get longer if anything <br /> <br /> Eh. I'll hope I'm wrong for now. But if Exigents hits KS before Heirs is out that's not 'the first KS'. It's the third driving stretch goals and content with the companion model prior to us seeing what that produces. Hard to get excited for this when we've no idea of what the results look like and the turnaround time is this long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:30:23-08:00","id":1351525,"title":"","content":"Is Exigents even getting a KS? I thought only mainline splatbooks were, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:44:22-08:00","id":1351527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351525#post1351525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Exigents even getting a KS? I thought only mainline splatbooks were, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exigents is a mainline splatbook and is indeed getting a KS. It'll be structured differently though since well, Exigents as a book is a very differently strucutred splatobook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:50:54-08:00","id":1351528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351522#post1351522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the ultimate question for me. Does it compound? Because with this turnaround of splats relative to companions you're going to end up with more of the latter in the queue and subsequent ones taking longer. Heirs began to some degree after WFHW wrapped, took us through that hitting publication and through Exigents getting first draft. And only now is MFS starting to get work. So how long till MFS hits? Unless there's a big change up Exigents will lead to another companion book too, that'll be in the queue. Will we get MFS before 2021 and Sidereals? Heirs was the only companion in the queue before - turnarounds gonna get longer if anything</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not. Again, it seems to be that it's not a matter of total books, it's just that some books take more time than others, and some things take more work than others. The pace is consistent, that pace just happens to create overlaps due to the way well, time works. If you do a KS every 12-14 months, but a book takes 18-20 months to make, you invariably just end up with the overlap happening. And again, all of this assumes that just not doing Exigents until Heirs were done, would get Heirs any earlier htan when Exigents' Kickstarter would have been.<br /> <br /> Look at it this way. Assuming a say, 20-month turnaround, Heirs might be available as a draft in probably February or March. More likely it's looking like April or May. The Exigents KS if in Q1 will probably be in March. If they weren't working to try to get Exigents out by then, my guess is Heirs would still not have been ready until January or February. This is, note, barring layout, which can take who fucking knows how long as that seems to be the biggest variable on these.<br /> <br /> Simply put, we'd get it sooner, but probably not enough sooner with the fact that if Exigents weren't being started until now, it wouldn't be being KS'd until ater next year or the year after. At least as I see it, the shifts in time aren't enough to jusitfy backburning things. Things are being dealt with as what's most effecient, and with an idea that RPG lines are kind of like sharks and so have to keep moving or die a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351522#post1351522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I'll hope I'm wrong for now. But if Exigents hits KS before Heirs is out that's not 'the first KS'. It's the third driving stretch goals and content with the companion model prior to us seeing what that produces. Hard to get excited for this when we've no idea of what the results look like and the turnaround time is this long</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is they'd sooner just delay Exigents if it starts looking bad, but you either basically don't do a KS earlier (and folks start fearing line pace slips) or you do it before Heirs and hope Heirs is out soon enough to not cause issues. Barring &quot;just write less stuff&quot; there's not a lot that can be done. And note, this is going to likely have been the case regardless on other books. You are seeing a bit why the orignal game took a while. If you wanna just work on one thing at a time, be prepared to not have a lot come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T12:53:26-08:00","id":1351529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351515#post1351515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if just throwing out setting info without charms would be that much faster.<br /> <br /> It feels like a totally different skill set, where you need to make cultures, peoples, and groups interesting to be a part of and interesting to interact with, making then feel human, which involves partially then following their own beliefs and partially points where their beliefs collapse but they don't acknowledge it or have excuses, and devoting the correct amount of workspace between answers and open-endedness to let players and STs hook into those societies and do interesting things with them.<br /> <br /> In comparison for me, I find writing charms to be much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of in context of this, there's a lot of thought that's gone into the setting presentation of 3e. The devs do a lot of going through and tidying things up and lining them up. There have been times where the gameline has had a bit of a &quot;rubberstamp dev&quot; thing going on where whatever they wrote settingwise goes. And that can create some cool, but you also often just end up with shit like <i>Kingdom of Halta</i>, &quot;Paragon as Dictator Apologia&quot; or, &quot;House of Succulant Tears&quot; about.<br /> <br /> As you note, writing good setting is a different skillset as writing good crunch. And it is not necessarily any faster to do one or the other. Again, see <i>The Realm</i> and while it had a relatively faster turn-around, wasn't necessarily well, fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T13:51:06-08:00","id":1351538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351514#post1351514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I know. It makes sense to have multiple things in the queue. If it weren't for Exigents I'd probably be less bitter. But we've had complete draft text for Lunars, three new books enter the queue, one a fatsplat, and the Realm complete all since Heirs was announced. Without being able to look inside the Devs heads or actively follow what specifically they're currently working on, it feels like Heirs was the backburner project - especially since an entire splat book will seemingly make it all the way through the process before it arrives (Lunars)</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is... for me, despite paying for Heirs, I'm glad that it's on the backburner because the game needs Lunars far, far more than it needs Heirs. But I can see why you'd be annoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T14:09:48-08:00","id":1351541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351528#post1351528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not. Again, it seems to be that it's not a matter of total books, it's just that some books take more time than others, and some things take more work than others. The pace is consistent, that pace just happens to create overlaps due to the way well, time works. If you do a KS every 12-14 months, but a book takes 18-20 months to make, you invariably just end up with the overlap happening. And again, all of this assumes that just not doing Exigents until Heirs were done, would get Heirs any earlier htan when Exigents' Kickstarter would have been.<br /> <br /> Look at it this way. Assuming a say, 20-month turnaround, Heirs might be available as a draft in probably February or March. More likely it's looking like April or May. The Exigents KS if in Q1 will probably be in March. If they weren't working to try to get Exigents out by then, my guess is Heirs would still not have been ready until January or February. This is, note, barring layout, which can take who fucking knows how long as that seems to be the biggest variable on these.<br /> <br /> Simply put, we'd get it sooner, but probably not enough sooner with the fact that if Exigents weren't being started until now, it wouldn't be being KS'd until ater next year or the year after. At least as I see it, the shifts in time aren't enough to jusitfy backburning things. Things are being dealt with as what's most effecient, and with an idea that RPG lines are kind of like sharks and so have to keep moving or die a lot of the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> My guess is they'd sooner just delay Exigents if it starts looking bad, but you either basically don't do a KS earlier (and folks start fearing line pace slips) or you do it before Heirs and hope Heirs is out soon enough to not cause issues. Barring &quot;just write less stuff&quot; there's not a lot that can be done. And note, this is going to likely have been the case regardless on other books. You are seeing a bit why the orignal game took a while. If you wanna just work on one thing at a time, be prepared to not have a lot come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's not 1 for 1, that there's work overlap, many things in the queue at once. I get that. But Lunars went from beginning to completion after Heirs, WFHW was put through editing and layout, and Exigents is looking ready for draft if the KS hits first. That's a lot of work, and this stuff with Exigents and Lunars absolutely required dev time. I find it hard to buy that Crucible and Eight Directions went with no attention from the Devs either. Those things got attention to flourish and build the queue while Heirs sat on the vine.<br /> <br /> That ain't a crime. That ain't fraud. There's arguments to be made for getting the splats out, keeping the line active, I know. But it still translates to a thing people paid money for being pushed back, in favour of launching more Kickstarters for similar products. That feels like something to be sore about, even if it's not someone's fault or something to attribute blame over. If the companions keep getting further and further behind the Kickstarters, why should I care about stretch goals or a charm slot for something that could end up like 24 months off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T14:27:32-08:00","id":1351544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351538#post1351538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is... for me, despite paying for Heirs, I'm glad that it's on the backburner because the game needs Lunars far, far more than it needs Heirs. But I can see why you'd be annoyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm absolutely biased here - I paid heavily for a charm slot in Heirs to celebrate a game and my best friend's character. Went in as hard as I could because I wanted that, and to support the new dev team. But I held my tongue when Lunars hit KS, I feel all these complaints <i>can </i>basically apply that far back, but was trying to be reasonable - a book takes time to make, it's important to keep the line going, all the same stuff Blaque said. Exigents being in drafts and feeling likely to launch in KS before Heirs hits is just a bridge too far to me. That's two more Kickstarters that use stretch goals and high pledges to drive the building of a companion book before we've seen what the first one even looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T14:50:55-08:00","id":1351547,"title":"","content":"I see advantages to Heirs coming out after Fangs at the Gate. It provides an opertunity to factor the Lunars into what gaps in the Dragon-Blooded charmset need to be filled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T15:37:00-08:00","id":1351550,"title":"","content":"I mean, having read the last pages, I remain really conflicted about this edition. On the one hand, I don't really want to discourage the writers from ploughing on with their admirable dedication to it, and the goal of having &quot;Exalted, careful, really competent mechanically speaking (and novel, too!) edition&quot; is in many ways better than 1e and 2e's &quot;Here in quick time, lots of mechanics probably broken&quot;.... but on the other if it were anything other than a legacy edition, it's hard to see these timescales attracting an audience. Even if they are necessary to get things done &quot;right&quot;. Because if you were a new audience, 1e and 2e's timescales of &quot;In about 2 years *everything* that you are interested in will be done and it will be complete and together and you'll probably see something new every 3-6 months&quot; as the lead in is one thing, while &quot;In 7 years *everything* that you are interested in will be done&quot; is like... who actually wants to commit to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T15:47:13-08:00","id":1351551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351550#post1351550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, having read the last pages, I remain really conflicted about this edition. On the one hand, I don't really want to discourage the writers from ploughing on with their admirable dedication to it, and the goal of having &quot;Exalted, careful, really competent mechanically speaking (and novel, too!) edition&quot; is in many ways better than 1e and 2e's &quot;Here in quick time, lots of mechanics probably broken&quot;.... but on the other if it were anything other than a legacy edition, it's hard to see these timescales attracting an audience. Even if they are necessary to get things done &quot;right&quot;. Because if you were a new audience, 1e and 2e's timescales of &quot;In about 2 years *everything* that you are interested in will be done and it will be complete and together and you'll probably see something new every 3-6 months&quot; as the lead in is one thing, while &quot;In 7 years *everything* that you are interested in will be done&quot; is like... who actually wants to commit to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I got to agree. I have thankfully managed to make my players love Exalted and my campaign will probably last for years, but I started my current campaign last year. Previously I have tried to start up Exalted, but players have been put off by the time schedules of released material and have wanted to play other RPGs. I am lucky with my current crop a the moment. But there is a reason why Exalted is not sold in gaming bookstores that I have found in my country anymore. Exalted 3ed is pay to print for me. I have always been a fan of Exalted since 1ed, but had I started RPG now a couple of years ago, I probably wouldn't have known about Exalted. It has become very niche and the very slow release of source books is probably the greatest problem when it comes to attracting players.<br /> <br /> That having been said, for better or worse, I hope the project continues for many years. I have come to love Exalted (which is of course also the reason this is so frustrating).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24253,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","user":"Magnus K","date":". 11-28-2019, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24253-magnus-k","name":"Magnus K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T16:05:42-08:00","id":1351552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351550#post1351550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it were anything other than a legacy edition, it's hard to see these timescales attracting an audience. </div> </div> </div> </div>But it isn't, so what does it matter?<br /> <br /> I admit, I don't know much about other roleplaying games out there, but I don't think that many companies of Onyx Path's size are managing as many properties as Onyx Path does. Properties that were born in a much more prosperous era and ensure despite the logistical constraints precisely because of the dedication they acquired in that era. Maybe that means they're a bit overstretched, but which fanbase do you want to go to asking them to agree to their favourite line being discontinued to relieve that burden?<br /> <br /> If not, what does it get us to complain that things weren't like this before the 08 recession, or discussion on idealised alternate realities? Or I suppose detrimental ones if we talking about a circumstance where everything Onyx Path is making is brand new and all have to sell themselves on that? Hey, I guess it would be easier for people to let go of Scion, and then Neall could give more of his time to Exalted, so maybe it <i>would</i> work out better. You've hit the nail right on the head there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T17:10:19-08:00","id":1351562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351550#post1351550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> if it were anything other than a legacy edition, it's hard to see these timescales attracting an audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, funnily enough, I think if this were a new IP there would be a lot less people putting off playing until more stuff was out. Admittedly the Storyteller guide is way long overdue, but splats don't matter that much. If all you heard about DBs or Lunars was from the corebook you might be interested in playing them when they come out, but for you Exalted is basically Solars: The RPG. As an ST you'd want the guide and quick characters for antagonists. It's only if you've got a super vested interest in Alchemicals, and they're your favourite Exalt and the only one that you're really interested in playing at all that you are just going to wait for them.<br /> <br /> Either that or you're not into Exalted at all, which is fine too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T18:46:58-08:00","id":1351565,"title":"","content":"I've already said everything I've wanted to about my deepseated sorrow for how far away Infernals are, my unceasing regret about Devil-Tigers being nixed (no I do not consider point-buy Shintais to be a replacement for the concept even though it will actually have mechanics coupled to it) and why I think making them ability-based diminishes one of the splat's most unique traits on other forums. So instead I'll just say I hope Basphomy In Verdigris shows up as one of the antagonist NPCs being released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T19:31:46-08:00","id":1351570,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure Bas got nipped to make room for the new devs' own iconic Infernals. I personally don't mind her being or not in 3e, but I do sure as hell prefer them being Ability-based and Devil Tigers no longer being a thing because their concept (separating themselves from Yozi trees to make their own Charms) is no longer valid (their Charms are already not those of the Yozis, only Yozi-inspired, and they can already make custom Charms of their own like all other splats sans Sidereals can) while preserving the best parts of the Devil Tiger trees (Inner World and your personal pantheon of demons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T23:20:44-08:00","id":1351603,"title":"","content":"As for the health of the game, Exalted 3e remains as I understand still one of the continuously better selling games on DTRPG over its lifetime. You don't quite get to Adamantine on just initial sales. It's still in the 100 bestselling titles for the game too. And Lunars was the best-selling KS on OPP since Dragon-Blooded, which was to my understanding the best since Exalted 3e.<br /> <br /> Exalted could be better, sure. But it's not like, dying or barely on the vine despite the speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T23:55:26-08:00","id":1351605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351570#post1351570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure Bas got nipped to make room for the new devs' own iconic Infernals. I personally don't mind her being or not in 3e, but I do sure as hell prefer them being Ability-based and Devil Tigers no longer being a thing because their concept (separating themselves from Yozi trees to make their own Charms) is no longer valid (their Charms are already not those of the Yozis, only Yozi-inspired, and they can already make custom Charms of their own like all other splats sans Sidereals can) while preserving the best parts of the Devil Tiger trees (Inner World and your personal pantheon of demons).</div> </div> </div> </div>Last we knew (which was admittedly two years ago), they felt Basphomy was a viable candidate for an Infernal sig. They may change their minds (or have changed their minds), but as it stands, she has a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T01:23:52-08:00","id":1351613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351552#post1351552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it isn't, so what does it matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of what that comparison and framing suggests. I'm interested in how we've got where we have got, and interested in deconstructing the idea of whether the schedule of 3e is effective in terms of appealing to a new audience, or an existing one. Does the release schedule make sense or has it been reliant on residual goodwill? And so on. Is it something a developer would choose to do, or is it a way of implementing a game design that is a legacy from when they had the resources to produce it (or at least thought they did)? (And I guess, at the extreme Is &quot;Exalted 3e&quot; in some senses even a good idea, compared to fronting another, much simplified creative product without as many splats and facets?).<br /> <br /> Hey, it's not something I am going to wax on for pages and pages of self posting on the subtle nuances of in minute detail or anything, only a simple, short, question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351562#post1351562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, funnily enough, I think if this were a new IP there would be a lot less people putting off playing until more stuff was out. Admittedly the Storyteller guide is way long overdue, but splats don't matter that much. If all you heard about DBs or Lunars was from the corebook you might be interested in playing them when they come out, but for you Exalted is basically Solars: The RPG. As an ST you'd want the guide and quick characters for antagonists. It's only if you've got a super vested interest in Alchemicals, and they're your favourite Exalt and the only one that you're really interested in playing at all that you are just going to wait for them.<br /> <br /> Either that or you're not into Exalted at all, which is fine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if it were a new IP, probably would be far less popular. Leaving aside overall climate of what is popular (more favorable to 1e and 2e than 3e I think), and assuming those are neutral, then you may have fewer people who didn't put off playing, but a larger number of people who simply didn't find it carried their interest to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T02:27:55-08:00","id":1351616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351570#post1351570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure Bas got nipped to make room for the new devs' own iconic Infernals. I personally don't mind her being or not in 3e, but I do sure as hell prefer them being Ability-based and Devil Tigers no longer being a thing because their concept (separating themselves from Yozi trees to make their own Charms) is no longer valid (their Charms are already not those of the Yozis, only Yozi-inspired, and they can already make custom Charms of their own like all other splats sans Sidereals can) while preserving the best parts of the Devil Tiger trees (Inner World and your personal pantheon of demons).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the distant future when Infernals' kickstarter gets...kickstarted, I am fully prepared to throw enough money into the internet to get her in if she wasn't already added. The idea of what is basically Conan the Barbarian and Thulsa Doom's lovechild as a NPC is too good to pass up for the kind of games I want to play and run.<br /> <br /> I can't disagree more about the rest. I <b><i><u>absolutely despise</u></i></b> the idea of Infernals being cutoff from the Yozi trees because to me it was one of the coolest things about them in gameplay and fluff. The idea their charms are merely &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; make them feel like by far the weakest of the Solaroids when the Solars are arete incarnate, the Abyssals are on a path to Oblivion itself, whereas suddenly I'm supposed to believe Infernals are stuck with pale imitations of the powers of entities already degraded and mutilated after losing a war with the Exalted Host in their prime. It's extremely disappointing to consider you aren't even using the genuine powers that built Creation. I also have to say, for me the best part of the Devil Tiger tree was the idea of extreme transhumanist apotheosis surpassing the Primordials themselves, not any individual gimmick-especially when even Solars have the power to create spirits at E5 or Supernal Occult.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the mechanics of it, but the premise of some of the core conceits is extremely alienating. Which is a shame because I do like the rest of the ideas thrown around like the lack of a Reclaimation and point-buy shintais.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T04:33:54-08:00","id":1351628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351616#post1351616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The idea their charms are merely &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; make them feel like by far the weakest of the Solaroids when the Solars are arete incarnate, the Abyssals are on a path to Oblivion itself, whereas suddenly I'm supposed to believe Infernals are stuck with pale imitations of the powers of entities already degraded and mutilated after losing a war with the Exalted Host in their prime.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're kind of crossing the streams a little, third edition's Abyssals are supposed to have charms that are &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; while &quot;the path to Oblivion itself&quot; is second edition's empty rhetoric for evil palette-swapped Solars.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T06:37:21-08:00","id":1351635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351628#post1351628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're kind of crossing the streams a little, third edition's Abyssals are supposed to have charms that are &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; while &quot;the path to Oblivion itself&quot; is second edition's empty rhetoric for evil palette-swapped Solars.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I think I was misremembering some of the 2e writer quotes? Actually speaking of while I don't know how Abyssal players feel about the &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; thing I have to say I personally do find it very odd. Why would the Neverborn mandate their Creation-killing superweapons borrow a template from older, deader ones that don't have their Exaltation with them anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T07:00:00-08:00","id":1351641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351635#post1351635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, I think I was misremembering some of the 2e writer quotes? Actually speaking of while I don't know how Abyssal players feel about the &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; thing I have to say I personally do find it very odd. Why would the Neverborn mandate their Creation-killing superweapons borrow a template from older, deader ones that don't have their Exaltation with them anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading too much into the phrasing &quot;x-inspired&quot;. The Solar Charmset is Sol-inspired, the Sun doesn't have Excellent Strike, but that doesn't make Solars &quot;pale imitations&quot;. The same will go for Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> There will be as much overall power and sheer will of their creators in the Abyssals/Infernals as before, the Abyssals will simply focus more on Death Knight themes while the Infernals will draw from the overall alienness and transhumanism of the Yozis rather than pigeonhole themselves into specific Yozis. In effect, you could argue that every Infernal will be a Devil Tiger since all of them will transcend the individual Yozis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T07:14:07-08:00","id":1351643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351641#post1351641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're reading too much into the phrasing &quot;x-inspired&quot;. The Solar Charmset is Sol-inspired, the Sun doesn't have Excellent Strike, but that doesn't make Solars &quot;pale imitations&quot;. The same will go for Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> There will be as much overall power and sheer will of their creators in the Abyssals/Infernals as before, the Abyssals will simply focus more on Death Knight themes while the Infernals will draw from the overall alienness and transhumanism of the Yozis rather than pigeonhole themselves into specific Yozis. In effect, you could argue that every Infernal will be a Devil Tiger since all of them will transcend the individual Yozis.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, theming the Deathknights around the Lords rather than Oblivion is potentially a dilution. Past comments have given me the vibe that Ex3 wants to downplay exterior threats to the world, to the point that it's no longer clear if the physical Void is an actual place or not. So I'm worried Abyssals won't be able to match Solar perfection thematics and might just come across as mini Deathlords.<br /> <br /> Then again, trying to tie all nine into the charmset might help keep it broad at least?<br /> <br /> *shrugs* We're too far out for serious mechanical concerns. I'm more worried about the general thematics - potentially dropping Oblivion as anything more than philosophy, keeping the Neverborn more incoherent, ditching Resonance and de-emphasising Redemption in favour of Abyssals being pretty much free to do whatever. The overall direction is very... God Tier VtM to me. &quot;You're a monster! But... you're really cool, so don't bother getting too worked up about it.&quot; Not something that has my interest as an Abyssals fan, though I suspect I'm a minority here.<br /> <br /> Also, still cracking up over the idea we have to take Eye seriously now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T07:26:02-08:00","id":1351648,"title":"","content":"1st ed Eye was a serious (and better) character. He was actually a really good antagonist, because he was the weakest Deathlord, meaning he was an extremely powerful but not OP threat. And he had all his mad necromancy experiments, zombie plague, etc.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I'm also fine with Abyssals being mini-Deathlords, because while I'm over-used to the Deathlords now, they were actually pretty cool when I first read them.<br /> <br /> <br /> On Exalted generally... so, no-one in my gaming group in my city seems to have ever heard of Exalted (I play Exalted on Skype with my friends from University, we got into it from Vampire, not my friends in my city; we play Exalted every week, alternating between 4 different Exalted games, which I honestly think is a bad system but no-one wants to pick one game to stop, for now at least). Obviously people mostly play DnD, but there are plenty of other games played; Numenera, some superhero games, Paranoia, Shadowrun, etc. Most of the older players are familiar with some of White Wolf's games, like Vampire, but not Exalted. But recently I met an old friend who had started playing 3rd ed, having no familiarity with it. He said the players quite enjoyed it, but the ST found it really hard to challenge them, so they stopped playing. They're going to give it another try in a few months, now more books are out.<br /> I can see that being quite common, but I don't know for sure. That's just my anecdotal experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-29-2019, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T07:37:45-08:00","id":1351655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351648#post1351648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st ed Eye was a serious (and better) character. He was actually a really good antagonist, because he was the weakest Deathlord, meaning he was an extremely powerful but not OP threat. And he had all his mad necromancy experiments, zombie plague, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wiz, I love ya, but woow I disagree. 1e Eye and 2e Eye, to me, are basically the same character - only 2e frames him with less reverence. Which is something that I like with the Ghosts of the First Age angle - one of the Deathlords being this broken guy who is lashing out not really thinking it through... I joke about him, but feel he has potential as a straight up tragic figure, rather than the brooding gothic villain type.<br /> <br /> Still. Not as bad as 1e Lover! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I never expected the 2e version to be an <i>improvement </i>on something.<br /> <br /> @general health of the game: It feels like Ex3 is getting less play by post attention than Ex2 really got? Take that with a grain of salt - I'm in a couple of PbP Exalted games myself, but they were prominent in Ex2 and feel slim on the ground these days. (Yeah, PbP is a minor market share - it's just the bit I hang out in.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T08:28:50-08:00","id":1351664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351635#post1351635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I think I was misremembering some of the 2e writer quotes? Actually speaking of while I don't know how Abyssal players feel about the &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; thing I have to say I personally do find it very odd. Why would the Neverborn mandate their Creation-killing superweapons borrow a template from older, deader ones that don't have their Exaltation with them anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Neverborn could do whatever they wanted they'd make the Black Lantern Corps and call it a day. Problem is that's less a splat book and more a two page antagonist entry with notes on how to tailor it to make more of them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T08:42:18-08:00","id":1351666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351512#post1351512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends. Again, layout for a year. There's not like...anything the current team can do that since that's in a way a different department.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think this is a show that it's not just Charms that take time, but actually making the rest of the book. Note <i>The Realm</i> took about as long as WFHW did as well. In the end fo the day, you still have some amount of words that need to be budgetted, laid-out, editted, and developed. Would simpler mechanics help? Sure. Then again, <i>Scion</i> <i>2e</i> was promised the same year originallya s <i>Exalted 3e</i>'s KS, and didn't actually come out until 2018. So simpler systems don't by their nature, result in faster game devlopment.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is why we're getting <i>CoL</i> a bit. Exalted 3e was made probably assuming a more aggressive potential schedule than before. (Note that the devs before could get ab ook turned-aorund in like 8 months with things like Shards shown). Different circumastances on the game, what's neeed of it, the company, and the industry mean things just don't do that as they did.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Think on it this way. If we were to reboot and have Exalted 4e KS next year? I am skeptical we would seen any of this anytime faster. Look at the wordcount of setting between WFHW and <i>The Realm</i>. Now think about the fact that if you do a new edition, unless you really wanna have folks using books with outdated mechanics, having to contract to mor eor less do that all over in less than a few years. Basically the solution you want is probably at this point, a game dead for a few years, not the stuff you want sooner.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Blaque, all your comments have been very enlightening to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:35:38-08:00","id":1351682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351605#post1351605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last we knew (which was admittedly two years ago), they felt Basphomy was a viable candidate for an Infernal sig. They may change their minds (or have changed their minds), but as it stands, she has a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, last we knew from Vance and Minton, they said they wanted to make their own sigs and leave Bas out. That was less than two years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:36:59-08:00","id":1351684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351544#post1351544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm absolutely biased here - I paid heavily for a charm slot in Heirs to celebrate a game and my best friend's character. Went in as hard as I could because I wanted that, and to support the new dev team. But I held my tongue when Lunars hit KS, I feel all these complaints <i>can </i>basically apply that far back, but was trying to be reasonable - a book takes time to make, it's important to keep the line going, all the same stuff Blaque said. Exigents being in drafts and feeling likely to launch in KS before Heirs hits is just a bridge too far to me. That's two more Kickstarters that use stretch goals and high pledges to drive the building of a companion book before we've seen what the first one even looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, Lunars was already outlined and had writers assigned with First Drafts started when the Dragon-Blooded KS ended. Heirs had some pre-work to do, so things are just working in order received.<br /> <br /> The companion books don't get manuscript previews like the main KS books, so it seems like there is a longer wait. This is something that they could maybe consider for books included in Kickstarters. The Realm was probably in a similar state as WFHW when the KS was the ongoing, but we didn't see it for the some off year later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:49:00-08:00","id":1351686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351616#post1351616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the distant future when Infernals' kickstarter gets...kickstarted, I am fully prepared to throw enough money into the internet to get her in if she wasn't already added. The idea of what is basically Conan the Barbarian and Thulsa Doom's lovechild as a NPC is too good to pass up for the kind of games I want to play and run.<br /> <br /> I can't disagree more about the rest. I <b><i><u>absolutely despise</u></i></b> the idea of Infernals being cutoff from the Yozi trees because to me it was one of the coolest things about them in gameplay and fluff. The idea their charms are merely &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; make them feel like by far the weakest of the Solaroids when the Solars are arete incarnate, the Abyssals are on a path to Oblivion itself, whereas suddenly I'm supposed to believe Infernals are stuck with pale imitations of the powers of entities already degraded and mutilated after losing a war with the Exalted Host in their prime. It's extremely disappointing to consider you aren't even using the genuine powers that built Creation. I also have to say, for me the best part of the Devil Tiger tree was the idea of extreme transhumanist apotheosis surpassing the Primordials themselves, not any individual gimmick-especially when even Solars have the power to create spirits at E5 or Supernal Occult.<br /> <br /> I can't speak to the mechanics of it, but the premise of some of the core conceits is extremely alienating. Which is a shame because I do like the rest of the ideas thrown around like the lack of a Reclaimation and point-buy shintais.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may despise the idea, but it's what's happening so far, and I'm very much glad it is. Solars are not &quot;arete incarnate&quot; and that alone; their Charms are inspired on the legend, archetypes and aesthetic of the Unconquered Sun, who IS arete incarnate (or as close as you can get to it). Lunar Charms are inspired by Luna in the same vein, Abyssal Charms are inspired by the legend and motifs of the Deathlords in 3e, Dragon-Blooded Charms are inspired by the archetypal elements, and so on. They are no &quot;Pale imitation&quot;, the same way Solars, Lunars, Abyssals and literally every other splat isn't. In fact, it's pretty nonsensical to equate &quot;inspired&quot; with &quot;imitation&quot;. An Infernal Brawler may become a crimson razor-wind gale that kills by contact, or a towering berserker who punches green sunfire into people and boils their blood from within, and both of those are inspired by Yozis and Demons, yet they are not Charms that Adorjan or Malfeas have in their imaginary sheets.<br /> <br /> As for Devil Tiger, since they're not meant to be transhuman or anything like that in 3e as far as I know - at least, not any more than the other splats also are -, the lack of that option seems pretty fitting for their premise. So, agree to disagree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T11:53:36-08:00","id":1351695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351682#post1351682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, last we knew from Vance and Minton, they said they wanted to make their own sigs and leave Bas out. That was less than two years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I missed that one, where did they say it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T12:24:24-08:00","id":1351699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351695#post1351695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I missed that one, where did they say it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I'm not mistaken, in the main Exalted Discord. Has been a while since I actively checked for it, but I was there when they said it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T12:50:07-08:00","id":1351706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351635#post1351635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, I think I was misremembering some of the 2e writer quotes? Actually speaking of while I don't know how Abyssal players feel about the &quot;Deathlord-inspired&quot; thing I have to say I personally do find it very odd. Why would the Neverborn mandate their Creation-killing superweapons borrow a template from older, deader ones that don't have their Exaltation with them anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssals are going to have powers inspired in form and function by the Deathlords because they're due for something a bit more compelling to represent the powers of being dread sorcerer-warriors of old risen from the grave, and the Deathlords are right there for it.<br /> <br /> Like, whatever might be said about representations of their personalities, motives or place in the wider setting, basically all of the written Deathlords are pretty damn solid as ideas for vivid kings of the undead. Taking the First and Forsaken Lion's thing of being painfully bolted inside of his armour and using it as the basis for scary ghost chains and locking people in death traps to turn them into zombie knights, that's the kind of thing I'm amazed in retrospect they never had before.<br /> <br /> In-character and in design Abyssals have always first and foremost been gothic hero archetypes coming directly from the Solars, and I think that's ultimately a stronger literary and mythic reference for them than trying to come up with some pure Exalted of the Neverborn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm worried Abyssals won't be able to match Solar perfection thematics and might just come across as mini Deathlords.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> The thing is that &quot;perfection thematics&quot; is really just ultimately a post-hoc rationalization and categorization of what Solars are. I don't think that when Grabowski was designing them he was thinking about how to make people who embodied some abstract ideal of perfection; I think he was trying to make powers to represent big ticket culture heroes crossed over with larger than life anime protagonists. They're not felling giants with a single well placed sling stone because they embody perfection, embodying perfection is just a way of describing being able to do that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> So the competing Abyssal image is coming from things like gothic horror, Byronic hero narratives, death mythology, maybe a bit of heavy metal aaaaannnddd a slightly different brand of junky 90s OVA imports.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't disagree more about the rest. I</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i><u>absolutely despise</u></i></b><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> the idea of Infernals being cutoff from the Yozi trees because to me it was one of the coolest things about them in gameplay and fluff. The idea their charms are merely &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; make them feel like by far the weakest of the Solaroids when the Solars are arete incarnate, the Abyssals are on a path to Oblivion itself, whereas suddenly I'm supposed to believe Infernals are stuck with pale imitations of the powers of entities already degraded and mutilated after losing a war with the Exalted Host in their prime. It's extremely disappointing to consider you aren't even using the genuine powers that built Creation. I also have to say, for me the best part of the Devil Tiger tree was the idea of extreme transhumanist apotheosis surpassing the Primordials themselves, not any individual gimmick-especially when even Solars have the power to create spirits at E5 or Supernal Occult.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> So the powers of the Yozis are really cool and something to aspire to when they're approached purely, and degraded and mutilated from having already lost a war with the Exalted Host in their prime when it's... rhetorically convenient?<br /> <br /> I'll tell you now, nobody <i>ever</i> built Creation using Green Sun-Nimbus Flare, so the only distinction leant by that comparison is a bunch of cheap heat. &quot;Look, these are the powers that created <i>fundamental reality itself</i>! No that's not in any way resembling something that you'll be doing in actual play, but it's something you get to keep bringing up while talking yourselves up.&quot;<br /> <br /> I find that what the Infernal Exalted are intended to represent now are people who, in the look and variety and directness of their power, are invoking the image of the terrifying and grotesque ease of domination and abuse that is supposed to have characterised the worst that the Solars became at the height of the First Age, or could have become had they not been put down. The writing will not be looking for the stolen Solar that has been converted into a larval Primordial so that they can go around making friends with new shinma, they're looking for powers that can let you directly blast a person into one of those flesh trees at Essence 3. The Yozi mythology is there in terms of things like the aesthetics of those powers and the background in-character for why Exalted like that are included in the story of the return of the Solars to Creation, for elements such as &quot;returning such Solars is an act of their defining malice and vengeance&quot; and &quot;the Yozis have something in common with those Solars who were sealed away and are now finally returning&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are probably nuances to that in terms of what Infernals will have the agency to do, but the starting point is still with Solars, not Yozis.<br /> <br /> And the stuff from the Heretic Charms, well, extreme transhumanist apotheosis surpassing the Primordials themselves doesn't seem to amount to very much in terms of practical gameplay or stories with much resonance beyond... well, things I'll let lie.</span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T13:45:47-08:00","id":1351716,"title":"","content":"Should be noted that just like the Sun doesn't have Excellent Strike, Deathlords won't have some fo the Abyssal Charms and Infernals some of the Yozi Charms. There are some things that are pretty solidly &quot;just Abyssal&quot; or &quot;just Infernal&quot; that assuming their Charms all ape in some way their patrons misses. As noted, Lunars and Solars do a lot that is basically very much affects of the <i>Exalt</i>, than their patrons. The Deathlords and Yozis inspire their effects, not deterine them.<br /> <br /> In addition, I think that it might help give some thematic strength to Infernal aesthetics. In 2e, I kind of called Infernals at times the Wastebin Exalts. (Deriving from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wastebasket_taxon\" target=\"_blank\">biology taxon term</a>.) Since each Yozi was supposed to be its own character, it had to have a lot of redundent things to them. And since each was approached as if it were a complte Exalt, they had many jarring effects which sure, worked for neat combos, but had little underlying aeshtetic philosophy. And in this context, it also often had it where individual Yozis had Charms which were basically &quot;Didn't fit a main Exalt, put it here&quot; stuff, like shadowmancy, the evil genie stuff, or telekinesis. Things that just weren't going to show up in the main Exalts were tehre. Infernals likely will have things that help glue things together wiht more broadly Hellish and demonic themes, such as some of the self-realization in the Devil Tiger Charms being more easily acessable (Spirit of the Living World did literally nothing useful mechancially but folks wouldn't mind it), or general titanic stuff on world-creation, dreaming, music, and dance.<br /> <br /> There are some thing about the Infernals having the exact Charms the Yozis did that were outright caustic to character ideas in my view. When you made a rally good Fiend, you kind of have really the main route plus four (later five) flavors of spcie to it. And the way 2e Infenrals operated, they said nothing about <i>your character you are playing</i>. They were an exercise of basically glorifying playing a powerful NPC in the setting with a character-shaped skinsuit. It's cute to have &quot;No Infenral is ever a sailor because Yozis don't use boats&quot; but it's also kind of stupid that the mechanics also basically say &quot;No Infernal is a sailor since no Charms you ever buy will interact with Sail.&quot; It emphasized emulating NPCs rather than creating something to play your PC. This is cute in some context of exotic RPGs, but it's kind of weird in context of a game where you are encouraged to build your own character with their legend. Structuring their Charms around Abilities does a lot to give players things to hook their characters into, gives clearer ideas of giving more comprehensive Exalts (ie, suddenly we might have Archery Charms), and since each Yozi isn't bound to have to cover some suite of Caste Abilities or everything, more can actually be used where needed to give theamtic variety. The Ebon Dragon can have his Stealth Charms along with Adorjan-inspired ones. We can get some Szoreny Larceny and Socialize Charms without having to write-up a whole damned complete mini-Exalt for it.<br /> <br /> And in all this, a lot of the customization/homebrew stuff that I feel Infernals came the dumping ground for (Again, Devil-Tigers were cool, they were also basically blank checks to make Infernals the Ex MIsicllenia Exalt) are kind of now better realized I think in Exigents. Not calling htem a dumping ground, but an Exalt sort defined by smaller packages that do a theme well, rather than some bloated multi-tentalced ting that had five fairly different aesthetics, added on kind of as needed assuming anyone can us eit, and also on top of that had a whole other brnach of &quot;Just stop being htis Exalt sort entirely&quot; was to me at leas,t aeshteically and coherently a mess in a way &quot;Exalts defined by nicher aspect,s but doing that within the bounds of a character&quot; that I think Exisgents don't get into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T16:27:24-08:00","id":1351739,"title":"","content":"When I played an Infernal, I certainly found the powers lacked theme if you took stuff from multiple Yozi. It did seem like just a random grab-bag.<br /> <br /> Whereas when people stuck mostly to one Yozi, they were very cool characters... but you don't really want to stick to 1/6th of the charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T16:54:49-08:00","id":1351742,"title":"","content":"Let me preface this with saying, I love Ability based Exalted; it's a huge selling point of the game, that fundamentally a good part of why we all got into this was setting because we all thought that heroes doing chi-fueled feats of awesome and stylish superhuman ability is amazing and something which was very unique, certainly when attached to a setting with the mood and ideas and influences underlying Creation.<br /> <br /> And I think that's why it resonated with me when Holden and John made a great pitch for emphasizing up-selling *all* 3e Exalted as heroes with Ability based Charms as far as their design for Exigents, Infernals, etc went. This was coming after the weird, un-fun late 2e meta where being awesome at Abilities was sold as the sole province of the Solar Exalted, and was something that the *cool* and *successful* non-Solar Exalted didn't really do or try to do (in favour of &quot;weird, subverting takes&quot; on Abilities, having non-Ability based magic like 2e Infernals or Alchemicals and so forth) and was generally kind of a buzzkill for fans of Exalted who had Ability based Charms as part of their identity but which were not Solars.<br /> <br /> And yet I find myself these days not really caring if Infernals are actually Ability based on not, or instead follow purely esoteric Yozi based &quot;patterns&quot; or not. I think I'm less committed to the idea that an Exalt has to be successful and interesting in the game's full range of Abilities to be successful and matter. The dialogue around the Lunar Exalted in 3e probably helps with that. The Infernals could have &quot;holes&quot; where they really can't meaningfully, specifically support the expression of some Ability and it... wouldn't really matter to how successful they were.<br /> <br /> The only thing that seems genuinely non-negotiable is that Exalted player characters should not be aspiring to be beings of the singular power and nature of the Yozis as written by Jenna in Games of Divinity. Not even in a &quot;This could happen but is mechanically going to be unsupported&quot; sense. Has bad consequences (power inflation, messes with the goals of playing humanistic characters, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T19:26:32-08:00","id":1351763,"title":"","content":"Can't seem to quote multiple people using the comment system so I'll just type names to respond after the first:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351641#post1351641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're reading too much into the phrasing &quot;x-inspired&quot;. The Solar Charmset is Sol-inspired, the Sun doesn't have Excellent Strike, but that doesn't make Solars &quot;pale imitations&quot;. The same will go for Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> There will be as much overall power and sheer will of their creators in the Abyssals/Infernals as before, the Abyssals will simply focus more on Death Knight themes while the Infernals will draw from the overall alienness and transhumanism of the Yozis rather than pigeonhole themselves into specific Yozis. In effect, you could argue that every Infernal will be a Devil Tiger since all of them will transcend the individual Yozis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll wait until the finished product for a final judgement of course, but I simply don't see the premise of being a Devil-Tiger, transcending the fallen state of broken primordials to ascend as something greater expressing your own nature, as something as simplified as &quot;powers inspired by the Yozis&quot; so the basic concept absolutely does not inspire confidence.<br /> <br /> Croakamancer: Agreed! Like you said it's a long way off to start cherrypicking mechanics, and most of my griping's about which ideas are promoted and which are being downplayed. I wish I had the experience playing Abyssals to comment further on the mini-Deathlords thing, although I would have thought that the Heron would be the hardest to take seriously. At least Eye has a lab full of achievements plus Cold House he's simply too petty to make good use of, and the Lover's whole shtick is being underestimated (in 2e at least) for one of the more intellectual Deathlords. Just how much worse was 1e Lover anyway?<br /> <br /> The Hug Ninja: Ha! The Black Lantern Corps was always so ridiculously silly with their Hammer horror &quot;WOO WOO IM YOUR LOVED ONES DON'T YOU FEEL GUILTY GUYZ?!?&quot; act I'd hope the Neverborn would try for a <i>little </i>more actual menace. But in all seriousness what I meant was less of an antagonist entry and more of a thematically congruent gimmick, like say-channeling the symbolic death of light into darkness? Evoking entropy, rust, decay in it's more elemental forms similar to how Solars in 3e directly call on sunlight and thunderous power more?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T19:40:23-08:00","id":1351768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351742#post1351742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The only thing that seems genuinely non-negotiable is that Exalted player characters should not be aspiring to be beings of the singular power and nature of the Yozis as written by Jenna in Games of Divinity. Not even in a &quot;This could happen but is mechanically going to be unsupported&quot; sense. Has bad consequences (power inflation, messes with the goals of playing humanistic characters, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I would say in that, I don't think Infernals really ever provided that in 2e either, since I think the Yozis as they were in 2e were not the same things as presented in GoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T19:48:02-08:00","id":1351769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351763#post1351763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll wait until the finished product for a final judgement of course, but I simply don't see the premise of being a Devil-Tiger, transcending the fallen state of broken primordials to ascend as something greater expressing your own nature, as something as simplified as &quot;powers inspired by the Yozis&quot; so the basic concept absolutely does not inspire confidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Opinions are going to vary. <br /> Personally, I'm really glad that Devil-Tigers are getting axed because all I could think when I read that passage was &quot;Solar Exaltation &gt; Primordial&quot; and that's a sentiment that disgusts me. The idea of &quot;Infernal Exalt flips off the Yozi, does whatever&quot; was good but not at ESS 6 thank you there's supposed to be a game before that. And the Charms to do so didn't really help <i>you</i> do so as much as let your <i>Exaltation</i> do so. <br /> I also found that using Yozis as charm trees but only having six meant you really didn't have much room to play with concepts since the charmsets and Excellencies steered you so strongly towards the Yozi. I'm much more fond of &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; since then you'll be mixing and matching half a dozen Yozi instead of two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:00:44-08:00","id":1351770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351686#post1351686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You may despise the idea, but it's what's happening so far, and I'm very much glad it is. Solars are not &quot;arete incarnate&quot; and that alone; their Charms are inspired on the legend, archetypes and aesthetic of the Unconquered Sun, who IS arete incarnate (or as close as you can get to it). Lunar Charms are inspired by Luna in the same vein, Abyssal Charms are inspired by the legend and motifs of the Deathlords in 3e, Dragon-Blooded Charms are inspired by the archetypal elements, and so on. They are no &quot;Pale imitation&quot;, the same way Solars, Lunars, Abyssals and literally every other splat isn't. In fact, it's pretty nonsensical to equate &quot;inspired&quot; with &quot;imitation&quot;. An Infernal Brawler may become a crimson razor-wind gale that kills by contact, or a towering berserker who punches green sunfire into people and boils their blood from within, and both of those are inspired by Yozis and Demons, yet they are not Charms that Adorjan or Malfeas have in their imaginary sheets.<br /> <br /> As for Devil Tiger, since they're not meant to be transhuman or anything like that in 3e as far as I know - at least, not any more than the other splats also are -, the lack of that option seems pretty fitting for their premise. So, agree to disagree?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose we'll have to, yeah, given my position is the Infernals ascending through something they weren't supposed to do is one of my favourite things about them. For what it's worth I do actually agree with your points about the other splats (well, like I told the other guys I'm unsure about the Deathlord motifs thing for how out of left field it feels) and of course it would be foolish if Infernal powers had nothing to do with the Yozis at all from the get-go, but I'm concerned about splat dilution. <br /> <br /> Isator Levi: I can't agree your assessment about the Deathlords being &quot;vivid kings of the undead&quot;. What I largely took from their fluff in 2e was that they are, as a whole, <i>failed and pathetic</i>kings of the undead neither having earned nor deserving loyalty even if you actually are interested in ending the world. They were represented as a group of individuals so consumed by infighting their masters would ocasionally punish them, so it strikes me as bewildering that for Abyssals to take after them directly and not symbolic ceasation of Creation's aspects.<br /> <br /> Well, of course it's &quot;rhetorically convenient&quot; and &quot;cheap heat&quot; when we're merely discussing a brief, pre-released description for a gameline that isn't out yet. My point is that me and my group are absolutely more interested in the &quot;you carry the alien nature of the Primordials within you&quot; aspect of powers which set people on fire or blight feels, and don't appreciate them being treated as <b><u>diluted and anxilliary</u></b> to an exploration of First Age Solar hubris which, frankly, in many games we've run new Solars seem to represent perfectly well (funnily, we came to the conclusion some of our Solars were crueller out of Limit Break than in it). The issue is the personal capabilities of the Yozis feel sidelined, and as a result the powers bestowed feel diluted and insincere, hollow attempts at aping something with a greater mythos and potential scope for storytelling development. While I agree we start from the premise of a corrupted Solar I feel lot of your argument, I feel, predicated on the assumption that someone who wants to play Infernals wants to explore the worst traits of the returning Solars. Whereas my players and I would like to play something that starts out a Solar, and the endpoint of something that definitely isn't. For better and worse.<br /> <br /> I don't know what you mean by things you'll let lie.<br /> <br /> Blaque: Let me just say I don't take your &quot;wastebin Exalt&quot; analogy as insulting to my favourite splat, but also explain that I see most of your negatives as positives. You may say Infernals are a grab-bag but from where I'm standing my position is: Of course they are! The Infernal Exaltation was designed as a curse by a dysfunctional committee, and the miraculous storyline of your character was transcending that curse to strike out and carve their own path not because of their benefactors-but in spite of them! I'll also add that since the default premise was the Yozis were never getting into Creation I didn't really see a problem with using their direct powers to make a character's identity since effectively your character would be the true representative of that might within Creation, the place where most games take place anyway. There was a kind of beauty in that chaos to me of making it up as you, the character, go along even though I agree Devil-Tigers were more of a concept space than a functional game aspect.<br /> <br /> Ghosthead: As someone who's fine with ability-based charms for the other Exalts, the reason why I'm completely fine with Infernals having none is the idea that your charater is harnessing forces alien to yet superior within a narrow conceptual range to the conventional approach of effort through mundane means, and simultaneously I feel this design approach enables the &quot;holes&quot; you mentioned which I feel are just as defining to the Infernals as their strengths. &quot;Your greatest defense fails outside a city&quot; or &quot;To dodge perfectly, you must always run&quot; struck me as having an interesting effect on your character's progression as any of the actual emotional effects induced upon you by certain charms.<br /> <br /> As for that last part, I can't disagree more. In the same way Solars have Supernal abilities to represent their absolute elan, the other thing about Infernals that made them unique to my group was the narrative that they COULD, even if most games didn't actually reach that point, have a chance at transforming into beings of singular nature and power as written by Jenna in Games of Divinity. And I truly don't think the power disparity is disruptive with a good group due to the Imperfections of 2e providing gaping holes in these natures as well as, the basic goal of playing Infernals being an exploration of nonhuman characters as I said earlier and if nothing else the fact that Ambition 3 Solar Workings show that Solars themselves are capable of producing beings of singular nature and power wholesale or even making subtle alterations to the cosmos seemingly limited only by the ST's discretion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:08:07-08:00","id":1351772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351769#post1351769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Opinions are going to vary.<br /> Personally, I'm really glad that Devil-Tigers are getting axed because all I could think when I read that passage was &quot;Solar Exaltation &gt; Primordial&quot; and that's a sentiment that disgusts me. The idea of &quot;Infernal Exalt flips off the Yozi, does whatever&quot; was good but not at ESS 6 thank you there's supposed to be a game before that. And the Charms to do so didn't really help <i>you</i> do so as much as let your <i>Exaltation</i> do so.<br /> I also found that using Yozis as charm trees but only having six meant you really didn't have much room to play with concepts since the charmsets and Excellencies steered you so strongly towards the Yozi. I'm much more fond of &quot;Yozi-inspired&quot; since then you'll be mixing and matching half a dozen Yozi instead of two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That's an interesting perspective I never really thought of, actually. Personally about that passage: I took that less as &quot;Solar Exaltation &gt; Primordial&quot; and more as &quot;Solar Exaltation + The misguided efforts of 5 Yozis + the efforts of the hero these are bestowed on=unexpected and unique outcome&quot; like a metaphysical catalytic reaction creating harmony out of cross-purposes. The Yozis are ostensibly <i>trying</i> to empower the Infernals in the short term after all, they simply underestimated how much they could give out before humaintent and Exaltation spiralled out of control.<br /> <br /> But what you said about being able to draw from MORE Yozis is one of the biggest appeals I can see about 3e Infernals from what little's known, with the tentative descriptions of shintais in the preview being very appealing to me in terms of building up an eldritch god-monster. I do agree that in 2e you were more or less pigeonholed into 2 Yozis to focus on if you wanted a functional character, so I absolutely see the appeal of ability-based charms in that regard. I just wonder if there isn't some middle ground where charm-based trees (perhaps with a similar component as Supernal where 1 or 2 Yozis are discounted? Not caste and urge since to my knowledge in 3e the Yozis won't directly affect either) could have a bit more ease of access to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:10:58-08:00","id":1351773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351742#post1351742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'm less committed to the idea that an Exalt has to be successful and interesting in the game's full range of Abilities to be successful and matter. The dialogue around the Lunar Exalted in 3e probably helps with that. The Infernals could have &amp;quot;holes&amp;quot; where they really can't meaningfully, specifically support the expression of some Ability and it... wouldn't really matter to how successful they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on the range of activity they're sold as being engaged in. The limits of the Lunar Exalted exist in the setting in addition to their powers.<br /> <br /> Although fair enough, Second Edition showed that you could hype up Infernals whose powers had basically nothing to do with their song place as secret agents and geomantic saboteurs, nor much thematic tie in to the return of the Solars. So maybe there would be people who would buy it (and then basically ignore half of it and fill in their own gaps).<br /> <br /> Still, I wouldn't find it satisfying. I think they need to feel like they stand alongside the Solars of they're post of that narrative of the returning heroes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351763#post1351763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can't seem to quote multiple people using the comment system</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be a bit shaky, but you click Quote under each post and then the button at the top of the page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Long at</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I simply don't see the premise of being a Devil-Tiger, transcending the fallen state of broken primordials to ascend as something greater expressing your own nature, as something as simplified as &amp;quot;powers inspired by the Yozis&amp;quot; so the basic concept absolutely does not inspire confidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger and its follow ups actually did the thing you're talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:31:15-08:00","id":1351779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351773#post1351773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it depends on the range of activity they're sold as being engaged in. The limits of the Lunar Exalted exist in the setting in addition to their powers.<br /> <br /> Although fair enough, Second Edition showed that you could hype up Infernals whose powers had basically nothing to do with their song place as secret agents and geomantic saboteurs, nor much thematic tie in to the return of the Solars. So maybe there would be people who would buy it (and then basically ignore half of it and fill in their own gaps).<br /> <br /> Still, I wouldn't find it satisfying. I think they need to feel like they stand alongside the Solars of they're post of that narrative of the returning heroes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It can be a bit shaky, but you click Quote under each post and then the button at the top of the page.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What about Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger and its follow ups actually did the thing you're talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh thanks, I completely forgot about the button up top because I was so focused on the blue Post Reply one at the bottom. Anyway I did acknowledge that Devil-Tigers in practice were effectively empty space plus a blank cheque to write your own Charms, but that doesn't mean I don't admire the idea they represent even if I wish it had gotten an actual mechanical framework. I'd also argue that being able to create your own Third Circle Souls, being able to create your own Akuma and being able to slap away Limit onto Yozis whose Charms are open to you are all steps in that direction.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also just wanted to say, from the get-go my group and I have always seen Infernals as having a distinct narrative from Solars, which seems to be different to yours. We don't really think of them as returning heroes at all, we think of them more as a emergent god-monsters on a path that may not necessarily share the same values as humans, even divinely empowered ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12360,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","user":"Guitar Longcat","date":".  Addendum for prior point 11-29-2019, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:36:03-08:00","id":1351781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351770#post1351770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't agree your assessment about the Deathlords being &quot;vivid kings of the undead&quot;. What I largely took from their fluff in 2e was that they are, as a whole, <i>failed and pathetic</i>kings of the undead neither having earned nor deserving loyalty even if you actually are interested in ending the world. They were represented as a group of individuals so consumed by infighting their masters would ocasionally punish them</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about what they look like.<br /> <br /> Hence the description of First and Forsaken Lion and the kinds of Abyssal Charms that can produce. The actual character is irrelevant next to that (the fact of all the Deathlords receiving the same kind of writing revamp that Lunar elders have gotten notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">so it strikes me as bewildering that for Abyssals to take after them directly and not symbolic ceasation of Creation's aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a symbolic cessation of Creation's aspects?<br /> <br /> It's funny that Abyssals were supposed to be inspired by Wraith, when Oblivion is probably the least interesting thing about that property. Jesus, Oblivion is the least interesting thing about Oblivion; you've got all the stuff of Shadows and Spectres and the Onceborn, but somehow the elemental nothingness became the standard.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of mythology and literature to mine from the bleak domain of the ghosts before going into &quot;death as cessation&quot; being the motif for their powers. Have you listened to the soundtrack of Hadestown? I haven't, but I'm guessing it's not the next big Broadway success from being a lot of songs about becoming nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that me and my group are absolutely more interested in the &quot;you carry the alien nature of the Primordials within you&quot; aspect of powers which set people on fire or blight feels, and don't appreciate them being treated as <b><u>diluted and anxilliary</u></b> to an exploration of First Age Solar hubris which, frankly, in many games we've run new Solars seem to represent perfectly well (funnily, we came to the conclusion some of our Solars were crueller out of Limit Break than in it).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a conclusion, that's how you've chosen to play them, and it has some distinctions from how the game writes them.<br /> <br /> Infernals need to balance that line of being like the Solars enough to deserve a place in the Time of Tumult, and unlike enough to deserve being a separate thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is the personal capabilities of the Yozis feel sidelined, and as a result the powers bestowed feel diluted and insincere, hollow attempts at aping something with a greater mythos and potential scope for storytelling development.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that thing you said about how the Yozis were cast down and broken by the Exalted?<br /> <br /> That's why they should be sidelined, that's why their mythos is less significant, that's why their narratives are subordinate to the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I don't care about the Yozis. Stripmine their aesthetics to create tools for telling stories about larger than life human personalities. Take a Yozi as the basis for some braggart shooting fanged tentacles from his fingertips so the game can include Dio Brando.<br /> <br /> Abilities shall give those aesthetics structure, direction and depth. They will not be diluted Yozi Charms, they will be a framework for creating Exalted Charms. <br /> <br /> We've got three Third Edition Exalted Charm sets now. Consider what it means to have Melee Charms as strong as those of the Solars, but splintering off in multiple directions of sorcerous weirdness rather than being an extremely fast and precise swordfighter with a keen edge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T21:18:24-08:00","id":1351784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351781#post1351781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm talking about what they look like.<br /> <br /> Hence the description of First and Forsaken Lion and the kinds of Abyssal Charms that can produce. The actual character is irrelevant next to that (the fact of all the Deathlords receiving the same kind of writing revamp that Lunar elders have gotten notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What is a symbolic cessation of Creation's aspects?<br /> <br /> It's funny that Abyssals were supposed to be inspired by Wraith, when Oblivion is probably the least interesting thing about that property. Jesus, Oblivion is the least interesting thing about Oblivion; you've got all the stuff of Shadows and Spectres and the Onceborn, but somehow the elemental nothingness became the standard.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of mythology and literature to mine from the bleak domain of the ghosts before going into &quot;death as cessation&quot; being the motif for their powers. Have you listened to the soundtrack of Hadestown? I haven't, but I'm guessing it's not the next big Broadway success from being a lot of songs about becoming nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not a conclusion, that's how you've chosen to play them, and it has some distinctions from how the game writes them.<br /> <br /> Infernals need to balance that line of being like the Solars enough to deserve a place in the Time of Tumult, and unlike enough to deserve being a separate thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You know that thing you said about how the Yozis were cast down and broken by the Exalted?<br /> <br /> That's why they should be sidelined, that's why their mythos is less significant, that's why their narratives are subordinate to the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I don't care about the Yozis. Stripmine their aesthetics to create tools for telling stories about larger than life human personalities. Take a Yozi as the basis for some braggart shooting fanged tentacles from his fingertips so the game can include Dio Brando.<br /> <br /> Abilities shall give those aesthetics structure, direction and depth. They will not be diluted Yozi Charms, they will be a framework for creating Exalted Charms.<br /> <br /> We've got three Third Edition Exalted Charm sets now. Consider what it means to have Melee Charms as strong as those of the Solars, but splintering off in multiple directions of sorcerous weirdness rather than being an extremely fast and precise swordfighter with a keen edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, I'm just not sold on the idea of Abyssals being cooler if they look like that than if they look like-well sure, let's go with skipping the middleman and go with the bleak domain of the Underworld proper, pyreflame and bone and all that good stuff. The angle I'm getting at is something more elemental, more <i>fundamental </i>to death's dominion than the old poster boys for it.<br /> <br /> I never said it was a conclusion. And if it has distinctions from how the game writes them, well firstly the gameline left enough room for interpretation that I don't think it's invalid to play them the way we do. And secondly, I don't actually see how it's relevant when it's what we found fun and enjoyed from the game; say a lot of things about 2e but the one thing I didn't feel was a dogmatic obligation to adhere to some dogmatic cut-and-dried interpretation of splats that was the one thing, the true thing and the only thing they could ever be so in that regard I don't see how my opinion of what we enjoyed about Infernals, as a paying consumer, is any less valid than any other. <br /> <br /> I don't agree that Infernals have any obligation to be like Solars at all, TO deserve a place in the Time of Turmult. I certainly doubt Abyssals will, to the extent that a narrative of &quot;returning heroes&quot; will override a narrative of &quot;harbinger of death&quot; as a first impression before accounting for individual characterisations and games. I have to be honest here, the rest of what you wrote sounds like an inrreconcilable difference in personal opinion in what we enjoyed about Infernals: I feel there are many other splats for telling stories about larger than life people, and I find the idea of oversimplifying the alien and frightening nature of the Infernal Exalted to &quot;multiple directions of sorcerous weirdness&quot; as opposed to a fundamental and dramatic divorce from the human experience into a singular cosmic force incarnate of unknown provenance. Furthermore I <b>do not</b> think the Yozis necessarily have to be personally involved in Creaiton in as major a way as they were in 2e, but I do find an interesting part of Infernals being the part where the Yozis leave an impression on their own champions. If that's what you find fun well, I'm glad for you that you're enjoying the premises set out much more than I am. But from where I'm standing it feels, to be quite blunt emasculating to lose that metaphysical complexity, that potential for unknowable transcendence with what by all accounts appears to be a less interesting ceiling than what was promised in 2e.<br /> <br /> This is all predicated by the disclaimer that I am discussing themes and concepts only, given I have no mechanics or published materials to criticise of course, and that honestly if I end up eating my words by having fun with Infernals 3e when it's out I'll do so happily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T03:35:39-08:00","id":1351829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351773#post1351773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So maybe there would be people who would buy it (and then basically ignore half of it and fill in their own gaps).</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of &quot;holes&quot;, the context should have been clear, but if not, I am continuing on from ideas from Blaque's post in which he talks about Charms to support Abilities which cannot be present due to the underlying logic in Infernal Charms. I'm not talking about holes as in the Sidereal set, or simply limitations of wordcount. Intrinsic holes which exist due to structure. (To Blaque the section from Blaque's post. &quot;No Infernal is ever a sailor because Yozis don't use boats&quot;. Or equally you could say, &quot;No Lunar will ever have specific Bureaucracy Charms, because that is the nature of their magic&quot;).<br /> <br /> This being the case, I'm not sure how or why you'd propose that fans would later fill these in post-publishing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351770#post1351770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for that last part, I can't disagree more. In the same way Solars have Supernal abilities to represent their absolute elan, the other thing about Infernals that made them unique to my group was the narrative that they COULD, even if most games didn't actually reach that point, have a chance at transforming into beings of singular nature and power as written by Jenna in Games of Divinity. And I truly don't think the power disparity is disruptive with a good group due to the Imperfections of 2e providing gaping holes in these natures as well as, the basic goal of playing Infernals being an exploration of nonhuman characters as I said earlier and if nothing else the fact that Ambition 3 Solar Workings show that Solars themselves are capable of producing beings of singular nature and power wholesale or even making subtle alterations to the cosmos seemingly limited only by the ST's discretion.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get this appeal, but the power disparity (even as &quot;A point beyond which is actually supported by mechanics&quot;, which is kind of unsatisfying) really is destructive, imo to what Exalted is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Either Solars can meet the Infernals at that level, in which case they're going well beyond the implied Solars of the First Age (more towards some sort of ultra-potent, platonic version of the figure of the hero) and well beyond what actually supports the stories Exalted tells, and leaving the other Celestials Exalted behind... or the Solars can't, in which case they are no longer the central players in the story as the setting is built to be.<br /> <br /> If you assume that the Solars can meet the Infernals, and you want to avoid Celestials being left behind, you can introduce &quot;high essence transcendence&quot; for other Celestials too, as was proposed (through SMA or whatever) - but then there is the issue of how this actually fits with the return of the Solars being a big deal.<br /> <br /> It's the Devil or the Deep Blue Sea - either one of sets of options is inescapable and both are not desirable.<br /> <br /> If Exalted had been built from ground up to accommodate a long term evolution of all the Chosen to the power of the Yozis, as a supported part of the game, then that might have worked. But it would be a very different gameline with a very different history and setting!<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all postscripted that perhaps I'm really wrong about how powerful the Yozi are and this is not really a problem....! But that doesn't seem to fit with how I read GoD (the ur-text on the Yozi).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351768#post1351768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing I would say in that, I don't think Infernals really ever provided that in 2e either, since I think the Yozis as they were in 2e were not the same things as presented in GoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can add to everything Infernal characters probably can't be Yozis as presented in GoD and things which Infernal player characters can evolve into through accumulating Charms. (And 2e Yozi are partly this and partly change in writers). But that is an additional issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T03:40:26-08:00","id":1351832,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Never mind, misread previous posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T04:03:34-08:00","id":1351838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351829#post1351829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of &quot;holes&quot;, the context should have been clear, but if not, I am continuing on from ideas from Blaque's post in which he talks about Charms to support Abilities which cannot be present due to the underlying logic in Infernal Charms. I'm not talking about holes as in the Sidereal set, or simply limitations of wordcount. Intrinsic holes which exist due to structure. (To Blaque the section from Blaque's post. &quot;No Infernal is ever a sailor because Yozis don't use boats&quot;. Or equally you could say, &quot;No Lunar will ever have specific Bureaucracy Charms, because that is the nature of their magic&quot;).<br /> <br /> This being the case, I'm not sure how or why you'd propose that fans would later fill these in post-publishing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I get this appeal, but the power disparity (even as &quot;A point beyond which is actually supported by mechanics&quot;, which is kind of unsatisfying) really is destructive, imo to what Exalted is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Either Solars can meet the Infernals at that level, in which case they're going well beyond the implied Solars of the First Age (more towards some sort of ultra-potent, platonic version of the figure of the hero) and well beyond what actually supports the stories Exalted tells, and leaving the other Celestials Exalted behind... or the Solars can't, in which case they are no longer the central players in the story as the setting is built to be.<br /> <br /> If you assume that the Solars can meet the Infernals, and you want to avoid Celestials being left behind, you can introduce &quot;high essence transcendence&quot; for other Celestials too, as was proposed (through SMA or whatever) - but then there is the issue of how this actually fits with the return of the Solars being a big deal.<br /> <br /> It's the Devil or the Deep Blue Sea - either one of sets of options is inescapable and both are not desirable.<br /> <br /> If Exalted had been built from ground up to accommodate a long term evolution of all the Chosen to the power of the Yozis, as a supported part of the game, then that might have worked. But it would be a very different gameline with a very different history and setting!<br /> <br /> Of course, this is all postscripted that perhaps I'm really wrong about how powerful the Yozi are and this is not really a problem....! But that doesn't seem to fit with how I read GoD (the ur-text on the Yozi).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, you can add to everything Infernal characters probably can't be Yozis as presented in GoD and things which Infernal player characters can evolve into through accumulating Charms. (And 2e Yozi are partly this and partly change in writers). But that is an additional issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is that Infernals are to raw, spiritual power what Solars are to arete in fields of skill such as melee prowess or occult understanding and Abyssals are to the bringing of and rulership over death. Yes, given my druthers I would concede that endgame Infernals as I envision them would have the greatest &quot;raw&quot; power in terms of essence pools and wide scale Charms...BUT, at the same time I would never really see them escaping Imperfections and thus have wide, easily exploitable weakness as intrinsic to their supernal natures as their supernal natures are to their cosmic power. Similarly I doubt either Solars or Infernals would, within the strict focus of bringing about utter oblivion and death to the undying, be likely to outdo Abyssals. I do see &quot;being cosmic forces&quot; as Infernals' shtick but by no means do I think this makes them intrinsically superior to the other splats. A good example is the Supernal mechanic for 3e Solars, which allows a chargen Solar to access such ludicrous abilities as Fate-Shifting Solar Arete and Nine Aeons Thew. While I can't speak for a splat whose mechanics aren't published yet, I will say Solars being able to simply reroll a major success for any endeavor gives them a distict advantage over a splat whose cosmic power is thematically focus into a limited group.<br /> <br /> Of course, that is just conjecture based on our knowledge of Solars and I may be proven wrong when Infernals are actually out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T07:16:53-08:00","id":1351857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351829#post1351829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get this appeal, but the power disparity (even as &quot;A point beyond which is actually supported by mechanics&quot;, which is kind of unsatisfying) really is destructive, imo to what Exalted is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Either Solars can meet the Infernals at that level, in which case they're going well beyond the implied Solars of the First Age (more towards some sort of ultra-potent, platonic version of the figure of the hero) and well beyond what actually supports the stories Exalted tells, and leaving the other Celestials Exalted behind... or the Solars can't, in which case they are no longer the central players in the story as the setting is built to be.<br /> <br /> If you assume that the Solars can meet the Infernals, and you want to avoid Celestials being left behind, you can introduce &quot;high essence transcendence&quot; for other Celestials too, as was proposed (through SMA or whatever) - but then there is the issue of how this actually fits with the return of the Solars being a big deal.<br /> <br /> It's the Devil or the Deep Blue Sea - either one of sets of options is inescapable and both are not desirable.<br /> <br /> If Exalted had been built from ground up to accommodate a long term evolution of all the Chosen to the power of the Yozis, as a supported part of the game, then that might have worked. But it would be a very different gameline with a very different history and setting!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also in the camp that extremely enjoys the potential for cosmic-scale stories which Infernals bring, so I would be very unhappy if this is edited out.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the alternative you sketched is exhaustive. Why not simply make this part of the setting, posthuman evolution of Infernals, an optional canon, like the additional exalt types? Many fans find it <b>the</b> selling point of Infernals and one of the most interesting corners of the Exalted.<br /> <br /> I would just like to say that this kind of attitude in game design is one of the things I find most irritating about the 3rd Edition: forcefully choosing what is the only right tone and scope of the game. At this point, this is a broad game with a vast setting, with multiple themes and multiple sources of inspiration. Classic mythology, shonen anime, wuxia, sword-and-sorcery... There are many things there. Infernals was a part which was naturally leaning towards cosmic-scale stories. Radically changing this pure coolness in the name of purity of inspiration seems just wasteful. You are cutting out one of the selling points.<br /> <br /> I think that the ideal, non-aggressive solution of this and similar cases would be more or less this: the developers choose what kind of stories they want to tell. Let's say it is currently a mix of sword-and-sorcery with classic mythology. Then they treat the parts of the setting which have keen fans as explicitly optional. Just a sidebar saying &quot;in the previous editions Infernals could transcend Yozis because this and this. We chose to change the scope and the mood of the game, so we leave this option as extremely optional. If you choose it, keep in mind that this and that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, I sometimes happen to find small obscurities from the previous editions which were rather important part of the setting, looked to me immensely cool which get no mention in the third. It really feels like some propaganda and I fell as if uncovering bits of some forbidden lore, the actual, suppressed history of the setting. I really think they should follow the path of XXth Anniversary Mage which is actively friendly about the choice of the tone and playstyle, and become more explicitly open about crucial parts of the previous iterations of the setting and just write a sidebar to the effect that such-and-such thing is more canonical, but left as an option. By the way, I think that the Void also deserves this treatment, because having hole of all-consuming nothingness and the desperate escape plan of Dowager seem all immensely cool to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-30-2019, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:10:55-08:00","id":1351866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351829#post1351829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you assume that the Solars can meet the Infernals, and you want to avoid Celestials being left behind, you can introduce &amp;quot;high essence transcendence&amp;quot; for other Celestials too, as was proposed (through SMA or whatever) - but then there is the issue of how this actually fits with the return of the Solars being a big.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s also a bad idea because it creates a major rift between Solars/Abyssals/Sidereals/Lunars/Infernals and Liminals/Dragonblooded/getimen/Exigents ect. Right now there\u2019s a difference in power, but they still do fundamentally the same things and interact with eachother and the world in the same ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:35:28-08:00","id":1351872,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13416_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13416\" data-vbnamecard=\"13416\">Lanic</a>, sure an optional deutero-canon, Infernals-Gaiden, sidebar might be a way to go. I guess I am speaking more in a position of where I would think the developers would be sketching out the main direction and why they should, assuming limited resources. <br /> <br /> Putting in optional paragraphs / few pages of &quot;What If....?&quot; seems (tentatively) totally fine - like, to use a probably even more niche case example, maybe someone does want to play a game where Dragonbloods learn SMA and become an equal to the Celestials through it, or if someone does want to play a game where the Forest Witches really do Make <s>anime</s> the Sea of Mind Real and became as gods. Totally fine, but weird I guess places to put resources and default assumptions. Would that level of resource and coverage and optional status really satisfy people who want a lot of mechanical development towards Yozis-as-Infernals-transcendence and that to be the default assumption when they try to to get together groups though? I don't know. But yeah, OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:46:17-08:00","id":1351874,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"929\" data-vbnamecard=\"929\">Ghosthead</a> I wouldn't really need to have mechanically developed description of how you transcend Yozis. Generally, I believe that if your game reaches the point when it becomes relevant, probably ST and everyone involved will figure this out anyway. I was specifically thinking of this quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351742#post1351742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not even in a &quot;This could happen but is mechanically going to be unsupported&quot; sense. Has bad consequences (power inflation, messes with the goals of playing humanistic characters, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not even this quote in particular. It seemed representative of a general feel in third edition. You see, second edition has bad reputation for over-explaining things. But, from little what I saw, first edition would hint at many, let's say, cosmological aspects of the setting with strong hint that they may become relevant to your game, very much like oWoD, but without giving them any further explanation.<br /> <br /> I think that third edition sometimes rather than taking a step back into that mysterious flair, directly opposes the relevance or even existence of those weirder parts of the setting. Maybe more in the core book than in later supplements. I was very pleased to see Yatani's children or Arms mentioning &quot;stranger places for which current era has no name.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am sorry if this looked overly defensive, but I think that the status of Infernals will be a battlefield for the vision of third edition, as it directly touches upon more cosmic scale parts of the setting, and I would be very happy with more conciliatory take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 11-30-2019, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:52:39-08:00","id":1351875,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13416_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13416\" data-vbnamecard=\"13416\">Lanic</a>, you're probably right that I really should have said &quot;This *will* happen, canonically, and it's just a matter of time and accumulation of experience, but will be mechanically supported&quot; rather than &quot;could&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T11:17:15-08:00","id":1351886,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, you basically already have a canon-optional Devil-Tiger option. It was already written. That portion of Broken Winged Crane would port over just fine, as all of those charms were just purchased narrative justification, with very little interaction with any system or sub-system.<br /> <br /> What part of it needs to be rewritten?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T17:25:36-08:00","id":1351937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351886#post1351886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it, you basically already have a canon-optional Devil-Tiger option. It was already written. That portion of Broken Winged Crane would port over just fine, as all of those charms were just purchased narrative justification, with very little interaction with any system or sub-system.<br /> <br /> What part of it needs to be rewritten?</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally none, I guess? If it was just slightly revised and incorporporated into the text of third edition Infernals, I would be more than happy.<br /> <br /> Somewhat more seriously: we have some cool options for the setting and for the stories out there sketched for secod edition. We can ignore them, as they don't fit our propose vision and wait for fresh players to rediscover it and see how cool Infernals were on their own. Or we could just explicitely acknowledge that there was this option which we think currently doesn't work for the game, so we ignore ir, but manny people liked ir, so we describe it anyway.<br /> <br /> The second option seems so non-invasive that I seriously wonder why it is not considered an absolute standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:09:33-08:00","id":1351955,"title":"","content":"A bit of a problem with the Infernal-Solar arms race to some extent is that it in the end, made the entire rest of Exalted irreleviant or appear so. This is because the long term assumption is that 1 Solar = 1 Primordial. Which means that 1 Solar can defeat 1 Primordial. Which means that there being 300ish Solars either means 1) There are a fuckload more Primordials dead or Yozi or the number of Solars is pretty superfluous or 2) It had to be something time-gated (which Ex2 did with Essence 6+ admitedlY) that prevents this from being more than an &quot;Angels on pinheads&quot; situation...and so pretty much useless for most games of Exalted ever played since very few actually went to Essence 6+ and so a waste of time, concept space and word count..<br /> <br /> Like, for me, I never liked the Infernals = Yozis thing as it played on the &quot;Solars eventually become oomnipotent&quot; trope that made other Exalts feel superfluous and even at times the gameline's outright hostility to some of them. In trying to maintain Solars and derivitives as their peers, having a part of them be potentially 50 more Yozis meant that you do a lot to warp the setting's power scales in ways it was never built for or assumed. Exalted, early on, was a Dying Earth setting about the kind of romance of empires, heroism, and folks living up to legend of armies of the gods fighting great singular beings in titanomachy. When you can become one of those things it took armies of the other PC types to take down, the setting just kind of gets warped weirdly. Becoming a Yozi-level thing is interesting. It is also just in the end, probably something I think not explored in Exalted in a way that's healthy for setting integrity.<br /> <br /> When you have 300 or so Exalts who have various versions of &quot;Become Dr. Manhattan&quot; some of the stuff that sold folks on the setting relating to entirely different genres of fiction get lost along the way. No one gives a shit you made Zorayas' Zojad, Romances Han-style collapse of the Realm, or games of political wrangling over the corpse of Alexandar when oh hey this guy became the Ebon Dragon, gotta stop him or the whole world ends!<br /> <br /> When the arms race of &quot;How can a singular Solar fight a singular Infernal wiht a real Yozi-sized soul pantheon...&quot; means &quot;The Solar can singularly ifght a titan&quot;, you just end up with a setting that is more about fighting big numbers and not really interacting with the setting. Exalted really was never I think originally designed to be this DC New Gods duking it out or TTGL fighting Anti-Spirals. But hwen you are doing stories on that level of scale, stuff like I dunno, the Wars of the Diadochi, Romance of the 3 Kingdoms, or I dunno, Mahasamatman taking on Heaven by founding the EIghtfold Path or something, feel like they lose a lot of their relevance.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see just how Infernals, as characters you actually see play, wield power in the world they are expected to play in. You are Chosen and you have power. That power is mighty and alien. But you are still the person wielding that power for your goals and it is still a representation of your character's skill and will on the world. I'd rather see focus on that than some naval-gazing thing on how being &quot;super duper powerful means I can pretend to be something lockedin Hell for eternity to sfufer and meant to be a device to spawn the NPCs I enslave with sorcery.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 12-01-2019, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:11:52-08:00","id":1351957,"title":"","content":"Or to put another way, if a Solar has to have things to equal an Inferanl equalling a Primordial...why the fuck do we have nearly 800 Celetail Exalted, thousands of DBs and hundreds of other Exaltas again? Why should the game ultimately be &quot;Solars and their peers, plus these other guys?&quot; I'd rather a game be about the Exalted interacting as well, Exalted. Rather than Exalts trying to be something else and dragging the rest of the line to play their game in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:46:12-08:00","id":1351962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351784#post1351784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware, I'm just not sold on the idea of Abyssals being cooler if they look like that than if they look like-well sure, let's go with skipping the middleman and go with the bleak domain of the Underworld proper, pyreflame and bone and all that good stuff. The angle I'm getting at is something more elemental, more <i>fundamental </i>to death's dominion than the old poster boys for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, the Deathlords are built out of that stuff. On the other, Abyssals are ultimately not elemental, they're a different angle on larger than life heroes. Solars might have a bit more of a light show now, but that's not their raison d'etre and it's not what makes their stuff work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it was a conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wary of myself being to pedantic, but I do want to point out that it was the precise word that you used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if it has distinctions from how the game writes them, well firstly the gameline left enough room for interpretation that I don't think it's invalid to play them the way we do.</div> </div> </div> </div>That side is me getting off track a bit, yeah (although I do have thoughts about that having been a prevailing narrative about Sorts in the fandom that I might work out if there's ever a thread about it).<br /> <br /> The thing I've put together in the past is that the important thing for where the books start isn't individual characters but an underlying mythology to inform powers and narrative paths for players to explore. A side that should still ultimately have a lot of freedom; I think Infernals should still have room to play with the motif of the returned sealed away villainous sorcerer king in terms of things like challenging what people find villainous and why and ways that people might redirect those motifs to serve their own purposes.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a lot about comparisons to Lunars here, and how their book ultimately made them concerned with subtle themes of freedom and interrogation of the idea of the &quot;barbarian&quot; society, when a lot of people had spent years wanting shapeshifting as a means of transhumanism. I think the direction the book went in ultimately has more depth and touches on something that is more real to more people, especially in the world we currently live in. And it goes for the powers a lot as well, where they hardly involve much shapeshifting and go in a number of fantastical directions while still remaining essentially human.<br /> <br /> Something essentially human has always been at the core of Exalted. I think Autochthonia is one of the strongest illustrations of that; it has to be the single most weird part of the setting, and it's very popular, and its beating heart is in being about how humans cope in such a confining environment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And secondly, I don't actually see how it's relevant when it's what we found fun and enjoyed from the game; say a lot of things about 2e but the one thing I didn't feel was a dogmatic obligation to adhere to some dogmatic cut-and-dried interpretation of splats that was the one thing, the true thing and the only thing they could ever be so in that regard I don't see how my opinion of what we enjoyed about Infernals, as a paying consumer, is any less valid than any other.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be easier for you to build something you already know you want out of something designed to have a broader appeal than it will be for something made for this particular taste to appeal to a wider group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree that Infernals have any obligation to be like Solars at all, TO deserve a place in the Time of Turmult.</div> </div> </div> </div>The return of the Solars is the core conflict of the setting and underpins its themes, and the Second Edition approach smacked far too much of them only getting to be relevant for a few years before being pushed aside to make things revolve around the new hotness.<br /> <br /> You talk elsewhere about how being successors to the Yozis should make the cap on their power greater and their narratives grander. Do you not think that smacks of a certain ego in the concept, a thing that pushes the other groups aside rather than relating organically?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly doubt Abyssals will, to the extent that a narrative of &quot;returning heroes&quot; will override a narrative of &quot;harbinger of death&quot; as a first impression before accounting for individual characterisations and games.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, it was right there in the Kickstarter preview, and I do not think the change in developers has come with a particular change in that outlook.<br /> <br /> Second, there is no contradiction between returning heroes and harbingers of death when the place that the heroes are returning from is the grave. The mythology of the Solars plays it off as though they were just sleeping in those tombs; the mythology of the Abyssals leans right into &quot;no, we fucking died, and we have some things to tell you about what's on the other side&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which does require there to be something on the other side. The problem with them being just about killing people is that killing people is ultimately not very hard and does not have enough variation. To fit in with Exalted the death you're a harbinger of needs to be mythological and metaphysical rather than just &quot;then you cease to be&quot;, because that just doesn't support a whole group of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to be honest here, the rest of what you wrote sounds like an inrreconcilable difference in personal opinion in what we enjoyed about Infernals: I feel there are many other splats for telling stories about larger than life people</div> </div> </div> </div>I have ideas for Infernals that don't really work with the others. Especially now that there's a sharper limit on what Lunars can turn into.<br /> <br /> Some of it is expansions on some weird revolutionary mysticism, some of it is exploration of people who revel in the grime and the dregs of society and turn ugliness into something empowering, some of it is plain just imagining what the human ego does if it can respond to inconveniences by turning into a radioactive dragon on the spot and blasting it.<br /> <br /> Really, some pursuit of transcendence still falls into my idea of where Infernals can go, I just think it needs more definition for the people undergoing the pursuit and less for the destination.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the idea of oversimplifying the alien and frightening nature of the Infernal Exalted to &quot;multiple directions of sorcerous weirdness&quot; as opposed to a fundamental and dramatic divorce from the human experience into a singular cosmic force incarnate of unknown provenance. Furthermore I <b>do not</b> think the Yozis necessarily have to be personally involved in Creaiton in as major a way as they were in 2e, but I do find an interesting part of Infernals being the part where the Yozis leave an impression on their own champions. If that's what you find fun well, I'm glad for you that you're enjoying the premises set out much more than I am. But from where I'm standing it feels, to be quite blunt emasculating to lose that metaphysical complexity, that potential for unknowable transcendence with what by all accounts appears to be a less interesting ceiling than what was promised in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think the Second Edition Yozi Excellencies helped with any of that?<br /> <br /> That's another side to my criticism. I like a more abstract and incomprehensible Yozi. I think the idea of making characters who had to function in this setting into people using their literal powers ultimately made them a lot more knowable and a lot more human. We got a write-up for a Yozi that said that, rather than moving away from the Excellency as you got deeper into them, they became even more stuck with it.<br /> <br /> I never thought about it before, but that's the funny thing about Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger, it doesn't actually entail transcendence at all. It is all about defining the characteristics of your play avatar, and then becoming more deeply entwined in them by way of being empowered by them.<br /> <br /> The problem with placing so much stock in something being unknowable is that you can only ever gesture vaguely at it or undermine it. I remember a fair number of people coming to the forum really fretting over trying to know their character in the most exacting detail to precisely calibrate their Excellency. The only significance unknowability had there was people who were scared that they would end up developing their characters in ways that made their Excellency non-functional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T22:13:16-08:00","id":1351966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351962#post1351962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The return of the Solars is the core conflict of the setting and underpins its themes, and the Second Edition approach smacked far too much of them only getting to be relevant for a few years before being pushed aside to make things revolve around the new hotness.<br /> <br /> You talk elsewhere about how being successors to the Yozis should make the cap on their power greater and their narratives grander. Do you not think that smacks of a certain ego in the concept, a thing that pushes the other groups aside rather than relating organically?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, that's a good reason Solars are the corebook splat. It's almost like the fluff version of preventing power creep. Solars are the mightiest chosen, so any book that comes after isn't allowed to power creep them. They're also the focus of the central upturn in the setting, Solars, Abyssals and Infernals return to the world and rock the boat everywhere, and very explicitly are given ambiguity about their role in that. Not that there can't exist existential threats to Creation, but there shouldn't be a splat that gets released that makes the world feel like they're now the ones that really matter. <br /> <br /> So far we've got Dragonblooded, who made the Realm larger, more interesting and more terrifying than ever, but as much as some fans of DBs might want it to, it didn't make the Dragonblooded so great and powerful that the only thing in the world that matters is stopping them. The Realm is not laying in wait for the civil war to inevitably resolve itself and then steamroll the whole rest of Creation.<br /> <br /> We also have Lunars, who've grown and expanded, even getting an empire of their own way far away from the centre of the world. They still have powerful elders in charge of entire schools of Lunars and ruling nations, but their grand plan to take over everything isn't presented as something that's totally going to work. It might, but they're not like closing in a noose that makes battling the Realm seem like a pointless venture unless you want Lunar overlords. <br /> <br /> They're all just powerful but ultimately limited players in a world where centuries long norms are being upheaved. That climate magnifies their powers to affect change on the world, so magical powers that were already considerable lend themselves to the possibility of even grander stories. A ton of work has been put in this edition to make the world massive enough that a story that doesn't even involve a whole direction of Creation can still feel huge and epic without making it seem like you're hamstringing your players. It would suck to have all of that undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T22:24:33-08:00","id":1351967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351955#post1351955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of a problem with the Infernal-Solar arms race to some extent is that it in the end, made the entire rest of Exalted irreleviant or appear so. This is because the long term assumption is that 1 Solar = 1 Primordial. Which means that 1 Solar can defeat 1 Primordial. Which means that there being 300ish Solars either means 1) There are a fuckload more Primordials dead or Yozi or the number of Solars is pretty superfluous or 2) It had to be something time-gated (which Ex2 did with Essence 6+ admitedlY) that prevents this from being more than an &quot;Angels on pinheads&quot; situation...and so pretty much useless for most games of Exalted ever played since very few actually went to Essence 6+ and so a waste of time, concept space and word count..<br /> <br /> Like, for me, I never liked the Infernals = Yozis thing as it played on the &quot;Solars eventually become oomnipotent&quot; trope that made other Exalts feel superfluous and even at times the gameline's outright hostility to some of them. In trying to maintain Solars and derivitives as their peers, having a part of them be potentially 50 more Yozis meant that you do a lot to warp the setting's power scales in ways it was never built for or assumed. Exalted, early on, was a Dying Earth setting about the kind of romance of empires, heroism, and folks living up to legend of armies of the gods fighting great singular beings in titanomachy. When you can become one of those things it took armies of the other PC types to take down, the setting just kind of gets warped weirdly. Becoming a Yozi-level thing is interesting. It is also just in the end, probably something I think not explored in Exalted in a way that's healthy for setting integrity.<br /> <br /> When you have 300 or so Exalts who have various versions of &quot;Become Dr. Manhattan&quot; some of the stuff that sold folks on the setting relating to entirely different genres of fiction get lost along the way. No one gives a shit you made Zorayas' Zojad, Romances Han-style collapse of the Realm, or games of political wrangling over the corpse of Alexandar when oh hey this guy became the Ebon Dragon, gotta stop him or the whole world ends!<br /> <br /> When the arms race of &quot;How can a singular Solar fight a singular Infernal wiht a real Yozi-sized soul pantheon...&quot; means &quot;The Solar can singularly ifght a titan&quot;, you just end up with a setting that is more about fighting big numbers and not really interacting with the setting. Exalted really was never I think originally designed to be this DC New Gods duking it out or TTGL fighting Anti-Spirals. But hwen you are doing stories on that level of scale, stuff like I dunno, the Wars of the Diadochi, Romance of the 3 Kingdoms, or I dunno, Mahasamatman taking on Heaven by founding the EIghtfold Path or something, feel like they lose a lot of their relevance.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see just how Infernals, as characters you actually see play, wield power in the world they are expected to play in. You are Chosen and you have power. That power is mighty and alien. But you are still the person wielding that power for your goals and it is still a representation of your character's skill and will on the world. I'd rather see focus on that than some naval-gazing thing on how being &quot;super duper powerful means I can pretend to be something lockedin Hell for eternity to sfufer and meant to be a device to spawn the NPCs I enslave with sorcery.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See the thing is, while I do enjoy the &quot;Solars eventually become so powerful as to be effectively omnipotent&quot; I don't actually see it as an impediment to the other splats because...well, it's like you said: They're ALSO miraculously empowered Chosen of the highest powers? To me a Solar being outnumbered and beaten down by Dragonblooded isn't a statement of Solar weakness, it's a statement of Dragonblooded strength. Heck I even remember fluff in Lords of Creation's Transcendant Gaian Harmony (I remember someone being told to &quot;think bigger&quot; when they asked if the end state was that of a Third Circle Demon or Behemoth) suggesting Dragonbloods have their own level of evolution beyond conventional wisdom they might reach if sufficiently long lived (there are hearthstones that confer immortality after all) and with enough effort. And the admittedly extraordinary and otherworldly but still DB-managed Sea of Mind has been present since 1e. I've heard a lot of people say similar things about 1e but having read into it after 2e I can't help but feel the editions don't truly contradict each other, just expand. One thing I enjoyed was how the Exalted apparently existed in Oramus' Beyond-arsenal as impossible heroes, and that Oramus was alarmed on the day they stopped being in there!<br /> <br /> Which brings me to my perspective: Coming into 2e even if the actual gameplay seldom takes place at that level, to me Exalted always HAS been about DC New Gods duking it out with TTGL wrestling the Anti-Spirals...BUT ALSO interacting with the setting. I don't see those things being mutually exclusive at all, because Creation as a setting always read to me as being intended to raise questions about consequences moreso than insurmountable limits. Heck, I could use those examples as reference points: Just as being a champion warrior of a race of supradimensional self-aware ideas endowed with the universe bomb-containing Astro Force didn't stop Orion from forming friendships with the humans he rescued, I could see a Dawn capable of hurling a daiklave at the horizon so hard it cleaved a path into the firmament befriending a merchant who took care of his wounds when he was injured. Simon certainly doesn't look down on Nia or the rest of the Dai-Gurren brigade even though he's the one who gets the most &quot;oh shit!&quot; moments in the story, just like how a cocky Lunar warlord might feel paternal loyalty to their horde. <br /> <br /> I don't really think, in my experience, that it's the setting's powerlevel that dictates the gameplay. I think it's the players that do, and the powerlevels exist to give a scope of grandeur for the enormity of their characters' actions; background music to the opera, if you will. It strikes me as right that the Solars and their peers be first among equals, but just as correct that their subordinates hold the potential to challenge insurmountable odds just as the Solars themselves brought down the Primordials at low Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T22:49:06-08:00","id":1351969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351962#post1351962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the one hand, the Deathlords are built out of that stuff. On the other, Abyssals are ultimately not elemental, they're a different angle on larger than life heroes. Solars might have a bit more of a light show now, but that's not their raison d'etre and it's not what makes their stuff work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm wary of myself being to pedantic, but I do want to point out that it was the precise word that you used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That side is me getting off track a bit, yeah (although I do have thoughts about that having been a prevailing narrative about Sorts in the fandom that I might work out if there's ever a thread about it).<br /> <br /> The thing I've put together in the past is that the important thing for where the books start isn't individual characters but an underlying mythology to inform powers and narrative paths for players to explore. A side that should still ultimately have a lot of freedom; I think Infernals should still have room to play with the motif of the returned sealed away villainous sorcerer king in terms of things like challenging what people find villainous and why and ways that people might redirect those motifs to serve their own purposes.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking a lot about comparisons to Lunars here, and how their book ultimately made them concerned with subtle themes of freedom and interrogation of the idea of the &quot;barbarian&quot; society, when a lot of people had spent years wanting shapeshifting as a means of transhumanism. I think the direction the book went in ultimately has more depth and touches on something that is more real to more people, especially in the world we currently live in. And it goes for the powers a lot as well, where they hardly involve much shapeshifting and go in a number of fantastical directions while still remaining essentially human.<br /> <br /> Something essentially human has always been at the core of Exalted. I think Autochthonia is one of the strongest illustrations of that; it has to be the single most weird part of the setting, and it's very popular, and its beating heart is in being about how humans cope in such a confining environment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It will be easier for you to build something you already know you want out of something designed to have a broader appeal than it will be for something made for this particular taste to appeal to a wider group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The return of the Solars is the core conflict of the setting and underpins its themes, and the Second Edition approach smacked far too much of them only getting to be relevant for a few years before being pushed aside to make things revolve around the new hotness.<br /> <br /> You talk elsewhere about how being successors to the Yozis should make the cap on their power greater and their narratives grander. Do you not think that smacks of a certain ego in the concept, a thing that pushes the other groups aside rather than relating organically?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First off, it was right there in the Kickstarter preview, and I do not think the change in developers has come with a particular change in that outlook.<br /> <br /> Second, there is no contradiction between returning heroes and harbingers of death when the place that the heroes are returning from is the grave. The mythology of the Solars plays it off as though they were just sleeping in those tombs; the mythology of the Abyssals leans right into &quot;no, we fucking died, and we have some things to tell you about what's on the other side&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which does require there to be something on the other side. The problem with them being just about killing people is that killing people is ultimately not very hard and does not have enough variation. To fit in with Exalted the death you're a harbinger of needs to be mythological and metaphysical rather than just &quot;then you cease to be&quot;, because that just doesn't support a whole group of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have ideas for Infernals that don't really work with the others. Especially now that there's a sharper limit on what Lunars can turn into.<br /> <br /> Some of it is expansions on some weird revolutionary mysticism, some of it is exploration of people who revel in the grime and the dregs of society and turn ugliness into something empowering, some of it is plain just imagining what the human ego does if it can respond to inconveniences by turning into a radioactive dragon on the spot and blasting it.<br /> <br /> Really, some pursuit of transcendence still falls into my idea of where Infernals can go, I just think it needs more definition for the people undergoing the pursuit and less for the destination.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think the Second Edition Yozi Excellencies helped with any of that?<br /> <br /> That's another side to my criticism. I like a more abstract and incomprehensible Yozi. I think the idea of making characters who had to function in this setting into people using their literal powers ultimately made them a lot more knowable and a lot more human. We got a write-up for a Yozi that said that, rather than moving away from the Excellency as you got deeper into them, they became even more stuck with it.<br /> <br /> I never thought about it before, but that's the funny thing about Triumphant Howl of the Devil Tiger, it doesn't actually entail transcendence at all. It is all about defining the characteristics of your play avatar, and then becoming more deeply entwined in them by way of being empowered by them.<br /> <br /> The problem with placing so much stock in something being unknowable is that you can only ever gesture vaguely at it or undermine it. I remember a fair number of people coming to the forum really fretting over trying to know their character in the most exacting detail to precisely calibrate their Excellency. The only significance unknowability had there was people who were scared that they would end up developing their characters in ways that made their Excellency non-functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. I'd honestly forgotten I'd used &quot;conclusion&quot; verbatum, haha. I can certainly agree about splats having room to play different things being a good thing? I guess I just differ on what the focal concepts of the splat should be. I'm not really sure what you mean by how Lunars feel &quot;real to more people in the world we currently live in&quot;, could you explain more? I've never really played Exalted with the intent to think too deeply about current events because of how removed Creation feels from our society. <br /> <br /> As for humanity and ego, for the first part: To paraphrase a certain quote regarding the Ebon Dragon's relationship with virtues, I've always felt the other splats played with extremes of humanity while Infernals played with extremes of <i>lack</i> of humanity. I don't really feel this is egotistical at all so much as that Infernals have a role and position that I enjoy where they challenge the boundary between what makes an empowered champion and what makes a titanic god-monster. And paradoxically, I'd argue there's plenty of humanity to explore in a fundamentally inhuman character in a transformation state from their initial humanity. Hellboy, many characters from Neonomicon and Promethea would all be good examples, I think. I certainly don't feel this alienates the other splats at all when I remember a developer-I think Grabowski? Listing several non-confrontational ways other Solars could interact with Infernals stressing the lack of prejudice about shining green. I could see Sidereals trying to persuade unknown, powerful champions of Hell it's in their interest to not rock the boat given 3e emphasises decoupling the Reclaimation as a concept. I could see Lunars trying to rekindle bonds with their old mates similar to Solars, or the more philosophical ones drawing comparisons between their generally barbarian societies and the hard streets of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Ah, I'd forgotten too much about the Kickstarter it seems. Truth be told I actually agree with everything you wrote there, I just don't see why the alternate <i>has </i>to include emulating the Deathlords. Solars certainly draw on more themes and natural phenomena than simply being perfectperfectPERFECTperfect alone, can't Abyssals raise walls of bone and evoke rains of pyreflame and bless their manses with a layer of reinforcing ash? I have to stress I'm not truly sure about my position about this since I'm not an Abyssal player and I only know one who mostly played one in a combat-heavy game, and if other people do like the concept all the better for them.<br /> <br /> I can honestly throw my support about the pursuit of transcendence and definitions of said transcendence; I think it would be really fun to play. I don't really see how Second Edition Yozi Excellencies hindered that, or unknowable Yozis would help with that though. The Excellencies surely aren't meant to be computer programs for the Yozis but guidelines towards the themes, strategems and outlooks that transcendental gestalt titans perceive and interact with the world through, which is helpful for somebody who wants to interact with one without resorting to making half of their traits up and supplementing the other half with Cthulhu Mythos-style complete cosmic horror while still retaining a lot of leeway to make them mysterious. While I agree there were...complications with statting up the Ebon Dragon ultimately I appreciate the attempt to make a force of nature that is simultaneously a very influential and frankly punchable character into something your characters can interact with. It's something quite a few players express interest in, in my experience. And about that last thing I do accept that ultimately Devil-Tigers were very challenging to build from nothing even if I enjoyed reading other peoples' writeups and my hope for the point-build shintai thing, even though by the sounds of it it's not quite what I was hoping for, is that the traits inputted into the shintai will provide similar guidelines to how the character evolves as Excellencies do as a &quot;roadmap&quot; to interacting with a Yozi.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T22:59:06-08:00","id":1351971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the thing is, while I do enjoy the &quot;Solars eventually become so powerful as to be effectively omnipotent&quot; I don't actually see it as an impediment to the other splats because...well, it's like you said: They're ALSO miraculously empowered Chosen of the highest powers? ...</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of this is focus in writing. 2e spent a lot of time basically making Essence 6+ this special arena of kind of stuff that most games didn't use or never got to. But it impacted a lot of presentation. WHich well, gets weird there. It also affected the actual way other splats were written, since the Solars were also given their thematic heat often at the expense of other splats. Which well, also didn't sit well in a game about the Exalted, but eventually spiralled to &quot;Solars making sure Infernals didn't outdo them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... To me a Solar being outnumbered and beaten down by Dragonblooded isn't a statement of Solar weakness, it's a statement of Dragonblooded strength. Heck I even remember fluff in Lords of Creation's Transcendant Gaian Harmony (I remember someone being told to &quot;think bigger&quot; when they asked if the end state was that of a Third Circle Demon or Behemoth) suggesting Dragonbloods have their own level of evolution beyond conventional wisdom they might reach if sufficiently long lived (there are hearthstones that confer immortality after all) and with enough effort. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Which again, most games didn't do, which also kind of gets into weird navel-gazing and angel son pinheads than well, games. It was a runaway effect based on Solars becoming omnipotent, DBs needing over a million to even matter (and still being fodder) and then the gameline also spending a lot of time noting that standing up to the obviously supernatural &quot;betters&quot; ws wrong. But that's admitedly other issues iwht the editions writing there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... And the admittedly extraordinary and otherworldly but still DB-managed Sea of Mind has been present since 1e. I've heard a lot of people say similar things about 1e but having read into it after 2e I can't help but feel the editions don't truly contradict each other, just expand. One thing I enjoyed was how the Exalted apparently existed in Oramus' Beyond-arsenal as impossible heroes, and that Oramus was alarmed on the day they stopped being in there!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sea of Mind was something DBs stumbled upon and b arely understood, so not sure the point of bringing that one in? It was a bit of cyberpunk post-singularity immortailtiy with a healhty dose of Lee and Lovecraft layered on it. And in the end, soem little bit of fluff about using logic about some demon-god locked in Hell who was, I'll note, ended up having more wordcount on him than the hundreds of demons his kind were designed ot help people spin-out ideas for. It's setting minutia that adds little save setting factoids and writers being self-congratulatorily clever at times.<br /> <br /> And again, worrying about what's Real and Not is in the end, irrelevant when you're trying to be Zorayas, the Lady, or found a Dandelion Dynasty I feel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings me to my perspective: Coming into 2e even if the actual gameplay seldom takes place at that level, to me Exalted always HAS been about DC New Gods duking it out with TTGL wrestling the Anti-Spirals... ...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of a term I've used called &quot;RPG.net Meme Exalted&quot;. Exalted 1e for instance, notes <i>Ninja Scroll</i>, not anime as a whole. It has Cook's Black Company, Lee's Flat Earth, Wolfe's Book of New Sun, and Moorcock's Hawkmoon as inspirations. These are stories that do get epic, do deal with great spanning supernatural things, and even has great threats to the world like Hate or unleashing the shadows of the Plane of Glittering Stone on the world. But I think it's notable that even in these stories when you have heroic people with powers doing that, they don't all come down to Big Number Clashes. Or that when references are over the top like the Mahabarata or the Iliad, it's over moe tangible things like naitons, cities, and so on. Exalted early on was Epic, but it wasn't Cosmic. That came from hyperoble of T-Rexes and F15s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... BUT ALSO interacting with the setting. I don't see those things being mutually exclusive at all, because Creation as a setting always read to me as being intended to raise questions about consequences moreso than insurmountable limits. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a thing about fiction to me that I admit might be my push-back here.<br /> <br /> Like, to take a similar tack. I think most Marvel films have become boring in part due to their stakes-raising. For a lot of people, that the heroes have seemingly impossible odds means it's interesting to see how they fix them. To me, I find them boring because I know the plot. And I find them especially boring since in the end, when the stakes are existential, I just don't care as much since you know it has to be fixed or things end. It's a problem a lot for fiction to me.<br /> <br /> In contrast, my favorite Marvel film was <i>Civil War</i> in part because at the end of the day, the stakes were actually pretty low. The world would change. You would have conflict with people. But no matter who won the fights, the world wasn't going to end. But the effects on the world were still large, you still had powerful people who affected it, and it had ripples about. That's ultimatley just to me mor eitneresting than any shit with. New regimes and fighting over ideals and actual questions on how to wield or contorl power is more interesting than whether or not you stop extinction level events.<br /> <br /> That's a big issue with the New Gods or TTGL stuff. They're stakes are so high that they dont' actually ask about power. THey simply present you lots of power, and say one is better for using it better or something. They're fun spectacles, TTGL is my favorite mecha anime even. I think it's still outright bad way to go into Exalted as in the end, the story isn't about consequences of power, but about getting around those consequences or using it inspite of them. It asks no questions since it's pure revelry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Heck, I could use those examples as reference points: Just as being a champion warrior of a race of supradimensional self-aware ideas endowed with the universe bomb-containing Astro Force didn't stop Orion from forming friendships with the humans he rescued, I could see a Dawn capable of hurling a daiklave at the horizon so hard it cleaved a path into the firmament befriending a merchant who took care of his wounds when he was injured. Simon certainly doesn't look down on Nia or the rest of the Dai-Gurren brigade even though he's the one who gets the most &quot;oh shit!&quot; moments in the story, just like how a cocky Lunar warlord might feel paternal loyalty to their horde.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big issue note is 2e never actually wrote things this way. The Realm was always pathetic and weak because it was a realm of DBs, not Solars. Lunars basically had a doomed entire thesis with the Thousand Stream River since with the return fo Solars and their derivitives, Creaiton would always be faced with existential level threats. Trade wars or empires didn't matter becuase in the end, a Solar could always negate the influence of poliites, and their states would always dominate.<br /> <br /> And Solar power was so great towards the end of 2e, especially to keep up with Inferanls, it made that Lunar warlord pointless. At a point, no Exalt matters to Solars save other Solars and their peers, save window dressing ot their stories. And while they the core splat, having this entire different cosmic game they're playing with themselves and the other Solar sderivitives and Primordials, lends nothing but making everythinga bout Creation feel like the prelude or b-plot. I'm more intersted in seeing wha it would be like if Alexandar could make an empire which crossed form one side of Okeanos ot the other than whether he went to Olympos to usurp Zeus or fight Cancer in the stars. Since in the end, I care about cultures, peoples and things on the ground and interacting with that than what to me with big cosmic stuff, ends up often generic fistfights in shiny white rooms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346010-5-years-with-no-abyssals-liminals-or-sidereals?p=1351967#post1351967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think, in my experience, that it's the setting's powerlevel that dictates the gameplay. I think it's the players that do, and the powerlevels exist to give a scope of grandeur for the enormity of their characters' actions; background music to the opera, if you will. It strikes me as right that the Solars and their peers be first among equals, but just as correct that their subordinates hold the potential to challenge insurmountable odds just as the Solars themselves brought down the Primordials at low Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The last line to me is the big one. <b>The Exalted</b> brought down the enemies of the gods. And I think the moment one assumes a Solar can, on her own, do that one-on-one with no support, it denegrates other Exalts, and to some extent, the creators themselves. What fucking point is it in making these vast corperations of being that are titanic and alien in nature if in the end one human just kind fo beats it? It feeds into both I think making the other Exalts feel superfluos and to some extent furthers the whole issue 2e also had of &quot;souls are fodder&quot; since well...they were. It's cheap and lazy, and to me just is power shown as DBZ numbers smashing without maybe appreciating beings could be mighty but just do so differently. A Solar can be the mighteist Exalts without them having to treat Creation as the tutorial stage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T01:05:20-08:00","id":1351975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1346